hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22201","Judamah bint Wahb al-Asadiyyah. 534 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, (H) and Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, (H) and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, both said: Malik informed us, from Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from A'ishah, from Judamah bint Wahb al-Asadiyyah, she said: She informed me that she heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: I intended to forbid ghilah (intercourse while nursing) until I remembered that Persia and Rome do that and it does not harm their children."
"22202","535 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from A'ishah, from Judamah bint Wahb, she said: I was present with the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - among people while he was saying: I intended to forbid ghilah, then I looked at Persia and Rome and saw that they practice ghilah with their children and it does not harm their children at all. Then they asked him about coitus interruptus, so the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: That is the hidden burying alive, and it is when the buried girl will be asked."
"22203","536 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Rabi' ibn Tariq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from A'ishah, from Judamah bint Wahb al-Asadiyyah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: I wanted to forbid ghilah, but then Persia and Rome practice ghilah with their children and it does not harm them at all."
"22204","Jamrah bint Abd Allah al-Yarbu'iyyah. 537 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Atwan ibn Mushkan al-Dabbi narrated to us, Jamrah bint Abd Allah al-Yarbu'iyyah narrated to me, she said: My father took me to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - after I had returned the camels to my father, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah for blessing for this daughter of mine. She said: So the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - seated me in his lap, placed his hand on my head, and supplicated for blessing for me."
"22205","Jamrah bint Quhafah. 538 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi the judge narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Azib narrated to us, Shabib ibn Gharqadah narrated to me, he said: Jamrah bint Quhafah narrated to me, she said: I was with Umm Salamah, the Mother of the Believers, in the Farewell Pilgrimage, and I heard the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: O my ummah, have I conveyed to you? He said: Then a son of hers said: O mother, why is he calling his mother? She said: So I said: O my son, he means only his ummah, and he is saying: Beware, your honors, your wealth, and your blood are sacred upon you, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this land of yours, in this month of yours."
"22206","539 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Azib narrated to us, Shabib ibn Gharqadah narrated to me, from Jamrah bint Quhafah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying in the Farewell Pilgrimage: Give charity even from your jewelry, for you are the majority of the people of the Fire. Then Zaynab came and said: O Messenger of Allah, my husband is in need; is it permissible for me to spend on him? He said: Yes, for you are two rewards."
"22207","Jamilah bint Abi Jahl ibn Hisham. 540 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abd Allah ibn Umayrah, from the husband of the daughter of Abu Jahl, from the daughter of Abu Jahl, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The best generation is my generation."
"22208","Jamilah bint Ubayy ibn Salul al-Ansariyyah, the wife of Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas. 541 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Jamilah bint Ubayy ibn Salul came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not blame Thabit ibn Qays in character or religion, but I cannot endure him out of hatred, and I hate disbelief in Islam. So the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Will you return to him his garden? She said: Yes. So the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - ordered him to take from her what he had given her, and not to take more."
"22209","542 - Yahya ibn Mu'adh al-Tustari narrated to us, Isa ibn Shadhan narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Darir narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani and Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Jamilah bint Ubayy ibn Salul came to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not blame Thabit in character or religion, but I hate disbelief in Islam. So the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Will you return to him his garden? She said: Yes. So she returned it to him, and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - separated between them."
"22210","Jamilah bint Thabit ibn Abi al-Aflah al-Ansariyyah, the wife of Umar ibn al-Khattab. 543 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, and he mentioned a hadith."
"22211","544 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Sahl ibn Zanjalah and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, both said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - changed the name Asiyah and said: You are Jamilah."
"22212","The chapter of Ha'. Halimah bint Abi Dhu'ayb al-Sa'diyyah, and the name of Abu Dhu'ayb is Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Habban ibn Sa'd ibn Bakr, of Banu Sa'd ibn Bakr ibn Hawazin, and she is the mother of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - who nursed him and weaned him. 545 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, (H) and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abd Allah al-Bakka'i narrated to us, (H) and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Masruq ibn al-Marzuban al-Kindi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, all of them, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Jahm ibn Abi al-Jahm, the freedman of al-Harith ibn Hatib, from Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Talib, he said: Halimah bint Abi Dhu'ayb al-Sa'diyyah narrated to me, of Sa'd ibn Bakr ibn Hawazin, and she is the mother of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - who nursed him and weaned him, that she narrated, she said: A dry year struck us and left us nothing, so we set out among women of Banu Sa'd ibn Bakr to Makkah seeking infants to nurse. When we arrived in Makkah, there was not a woman among us but the Prophet of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was offered to her, and she refused him and disliked him, and that was because he had no father, and wet-nurses hoped for good only from fathers. A woman would say: What shall I do with this one? What can his mother do for me? So they disliked him. She said: He was offered to me and I refused him. There remained no woman of my people but found an infant, and the time of their departure to their lands came. I feared returning without an infant, so I said to my husband: If I took that orphan boy, it would be better than returning without an infant. So I came to his mother and took him, and brought him to my dwelling. I had a son whom I nursed, and he would stay awake much of the night from hunger and would not sleep. When I placed the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - on my breasts, they both flowed to him with whatever milk he wished, until he was satiated and his brother was satiated, and he slept. My husband stood in the middle of the night to a she-camel with us that, by Allah, would not drip a drop. She said: His hand fell upon her udder and it was full, yielding milk. He came to me and said: O daughter of Wahb, by Allah, I think this soul is blessed. Then he informed me of the news of the old she-camel, and I informed him of what I had seen of my breasts that night. We set out on a she-donkey of ours that before that could not catch up with the donkeys out of weakness. When we rode it heading to our lands, it would go ahead of the people until they would shout to me: Woe to you, O daughter of Abi Dhu'ayb, you have cut yourself off from us; indeed there is something about this she-donkey of yours. She said: We arrived with him in the lands of Banu Sa'd ibn Bakr recognizing nothing but blessing, such that our shepherd would go with our sheep to pasture them, and our people would send their sheep, and when night came they would return, and our sheep would come with full udders while not a sheep of theirs would drip a drop. They would say to their shepherds: Woe to you, pasture where the shepherd of the daughter of Abi Dhu'ayb pastures. She said: He remained thus with us. One day he was behind our houses among lambs of ours, he and his brother playing, when his brother came running and said: That Qurashi brother of mine has been killed. We hastened to him, I and his father, and he met us pale in color. We embraced him, I one time and his father one time, saying to him: What is wrong with you, O my son? He would say: I do not know; two men came to me, threw me down, split open my belly, and began stirring it. His father turned to me and said: I do not see this boy but that he has been afflicted; hasten him to his family before the matter worsens with us. She said: I had no concern until I brought him to Makkah to his mother. I said to her: O foster mother, I have weaned my son, and he is free of ailment, so keep him. She said: Why are you disinterested in him, when you used to ask me to leave him with you, as if you feared Satan for him? Shall I not tell you about me and about him? I saw when I gave birth to him that a light came out of me by which the palaces of Busra in the land of Syria were lit."
"22213","Hasanah, the mother of Shurahbil: she is mentioned, and she has no hadith. 546 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr saying: Shurahbil ibn Hasanah; Hasanah is his mother, and she was among those who emigrated to Abyssinia."
"22214","Hiqqah bint Amr. 547 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Khalaf al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Sharik, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Mijlaz, from Hiqqah bint Amr, and she had prayed both qiblahs with the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -: that when she wanted to enter ihram, she would place her cloak in her lap, wear whatever of her clothes she wished, including the saffron-dyed ones, and then raise the talbiyah."
"22215","Hamnah bint Jahsh, kunya Umm Habibah, and she is the wife of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and she is the sister of Zaynab, the wife of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -. 548 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ishaq said: Among the women of Banu Asad who emigrated was Hamnah bint Jahsh, among women he mentioned."
"22216","549 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Shabib al-Madani narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hani' al-Shajari narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Asim ibn Abd Allah, from Mu'awiyah ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ahmad ibn Jahsh, he said: I saw with my own eyes Hamnah bint Jahsh on the day of Uhud giving water to the thirsty and treating the wounded."
"22217","550 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Habibah bint Jahsh, she said: I suffered istihadah for seven years, and I complained of that to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: That is not menstruation, but it is a vein, so wash. She used to wash at every prayer, and she would wash in the basin and the yellowness of blood would be seen in the basin."
"22218","551 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah, from Umm Habibah, she said: I suffered a heavy, prolonged istihadah, so I came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - seeking his fatwa and informing him. I found him in the house of my sister Zaynab, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a need. He said: What is it, O hantah? I said: I suffer a heavy, prolonged istihadah that has prevented me from prayer and fasting, so what do you command me regarding it? He said: I prescribe for you cotton, for it removes the blood. I said: It is more than that. He said: Then wear a waist-wrapper. I said: It is more than that. He said: Then take a garment. She said: It is more than that, O Messenger of Allah; it gushes forth pouring. He said: I shall command you with two matters; whichever of them you do will suffice you for the other, and if you are able to do both, then you know best. He said: This is but a kick from among the kicks of Satan. He said: You will menstruate six or seven days in the knowledge of Allah, then wash; when you see that you are pure and are certain, then pray twenty-four nights and their days, or twenty-three and their days, and fast, for that suffices you. Do likewise every month as women menstruate and become pure according to the time of their menstruation and purity. If you are able to delay Zuhr and hasten Asr and wash for both together, then delay Maghrib and hasten Isha and wash for both and combine the two prayers, and wash with Fajr - then do so, and fast if you are able to do that. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: And this is the more pleasing of the two matters to me, that you wear a waist-wrapper - meaning that you wear a pad."
"22219","552 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, both said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah, from his uncle Imran ibn Talhah, from Umm Habibah bint Jahsh, she said: I suffered an objectionable istihadah, so I came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and he said: Wear a waist-wrapper and stuff cotton. She said: O Messenger of Allah, it is more severe than that; I pour it forth pouring. He said: Then insert, wear a pad, consider yourself menstruating in the knowledge of Allah six or seven days every month, then wash, fast, and pray twenty-three or twenty-four days; delay Zuhr and bring Asr forward, wash once for both, wash for Fajr - and this is the dearer of the two matters to me."
"22220","553 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah, from his uncle Imran ibn Talhah, from his mother Hamnah bint Jahsh, she said: I suffered a severe, heavy istihadah, so I came to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - seeking his fatwa and asking him. I found him in the house of my sister Zaynab bint Jahsh, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a need of you. He said: What is it, O hantah? I said: O Messenger of Allah, it is a matter by Allah that must be spoken of, and I am shy about it. He said: What is it, O hantah? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I suffer a severe, heavy istihadah; what do you think about it? It has prevented me from prayer and fasting. He said to her: I prescribe for you cotton, for it removes the blood. I said: It is more than that. He said: I shall command you with two matters; whichever of them you do will suffice you for the other, and if you are able to do both, then you know best. This is but a kick from among the kicks of Satan. So pray twenty-four nights and their days, and fast, for that suffices you. Do likewise every month as women menstruate and as they become pure according to the time of their menstruation and purity. If you are able to delay Zuhr and hasten Asr and wash for both, then pray Zuhr and Asr together, then delay Maghrib and hasten Isha and combine the two prayers, then do so; wash with Fajr and pray - do so, and pray and fast if you are able to do that. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: And this is dearer to me."
"22221","Hawwa' al-Ansariyyah bint Zayd ibn al-Sakan ibn Kurz ibn Za'wara'. 554 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, that he said: Hawwa' bint Zayd ibn al-Sakan, and she is the one from whom Zayd ibn Aslam narrates, from Bijad, from his grandmother."
"22222","555 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, (H) and Abu Yazid Yusuf ibn Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, (H) and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, both said: Ibn Anas informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Bujayd, from his grandmother, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Do not turn away the beggar even with a burnt hoof."
"22223","556 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Bujayd al-Ansari, from his grandmother, from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - he said: Do not turn away the beggar, even with a burnt hoof."
"22224","557 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, Abu Hammam al-Dallal narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Amr ibn Mu'adh, from his grandmother, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: Do not turn away the beggar, even with a burnt hoof."
"22225","558 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Hafs ibn Maysarah al-San'ani narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to me, from Amr ibn Mu'adh al-Ansari, from his grandmother Hawwa', she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: Give the beggar, even with a burnt hoof."
"22226","559 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, (H) and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Amr ibn Mu'adh al-Ashhali, from his grandmother, that she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: O believing women, let none of you belittle for her neighbor, even a burnt sheep's trotter."
"22227","560 - Abu Muslim narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhi'b al-Madani narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Bujayd, from his grandmother, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, the poor man stands at my door until I am shy, and I find nothing to give him. He said: Place in his hand, even a burnt hoof."
"22228","561 - Ibrahim ibn Suwayd narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, al-Thawri narrated to us, (H) and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Hayyan, from Ibn Bujayd, from his grandmother, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, the beggar comes to me and I have nothing with me to give him. He said: Do not turn him back except with something, even with a hoof."
"22229","562 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Mu'adh al-Taymi, from his grandmother Hawwa', she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: O believing women, let none of you belittle for her neighbor, even a burnt sheep's fetlock."
"22230","563 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jumahi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hunayni narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Bujayd al-Harithi, from his grandmother Hawwa', and she was among the women who gave pledge, she said: I heard the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: Pray Fajr at dawn brightness, for it is greater in reward."
"22231","Al-Hawla' bint Tuwayt: she is mentioned. 564 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar ibn Faris narrated to us, Yunus ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from A'ishah, that al-Hawla' bint Tuwayt passed by her while the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was with her, and she said: This al-Hawla', they claim she does not sleep at night. He said: Take of deeds what you can bear, for by Allah, Allah does not tire until you tire."
"22232","Habibah bint Sahl, the wife of Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas. 565 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed me, that Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman narrated to him: that Habibah bint Sahl was told that Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas had beaten her with a beating she did not know what it was. She came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - in the darkness before dawn and mentioned to him what was with her. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Take from her. She said: What he gave me is with me as it is. He said: So take from her. Amrah said: And she stayed with her family."
"22233","566 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Amrah, that Habibah bint Sahl was told that Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas - and he mentioned the like of it."
"22234","567 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Amrah, from Habibah bint Sahl, a woman whom the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - had intended to marry, then Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas proposed to her and married her. Thabit ibn Qays had harshness in character, so he beat her. She appeared in the darkness before dawn at the door of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - came out and said: Who is this? She said: I am Habibah, O Messenger of Allah; neither I nor Thabit. Thabit came after her, and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to him: Did you beat her? He said: Yes, I beat her. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Take from her. She said: O Messenger of Allah, all that he gave me is with me. He said: So he took from her, and she stayed in her house."
"22235","568 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Quddus ibn Bakr ibn Khunays narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, and al-Hajjaj, from Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from his uncle Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, he said: Habibah bint Sahl was under Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas al-Ansari, and she disliked him, and he was an ugly man. She came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I see him, and were it not for fear of Allah I would spit in his face. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Will you return to him his garden which he gave you as dower? She said: Yes. He sent to him, and she returned to him his garden, and he separated between them. That was the first khul' in Islam."
"22236","Habibah bint Zayd ibn Kharijah ibn Abi Zuhayr al-Khazraji, the wife of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with them both. 569 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, she said: Abu Bakr sought permission from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -, when he saw lightness in him, to go to Bint Kharijah, and he permitted him - in a long hadith."
"22237","Habibah bint Abi Sufyan. 570 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us, Aban ibn Dam'ah narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Sirin saying: Habibah bint Abi Sufyan narrated to me, she said: I was sitting in the house of A'ishah when the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered and said: There are no two Muslims whose three children die before reaching puberty except that Allah admits them both to Paradise by virtue of His mercy toward them."
"22238","571 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Yusuf al-Sha'ir narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: I heard Hisham ibn Hassan narrating from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Yazid ibn Abi Bakrah, he said: Habibah narrated to me that she was with A'ishah when the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - came until he entered upon her and said: There are no two Muslims whose three children die before reaching puberty except that they will be brought on the Day of Resurrection until they are made to stand at the gate of Paradise, and it will be said to them: Enter Paradise. They will say: Until our fathers enter. Then it will be said to them: Enter Paradise, you and your fathers."
"22239","Habibah bint Abi Tijrah al-Abdariyyah. 572 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Surayj ibn al-Nu'man al-Jawhari narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mu'ammil narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhaysin, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, she said: Habibah bint Abi Tijrah narrated to us, she said: I saw myself among women of Quraysh in the house of Abi Husayn, while the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was between al-Safa and al-Marwah. She said: I heard him when he reached the place of running saying: Run, for Allah has prescribed running upon you."
"22240","573 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Idris al-Shafi'i narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mu'ammil narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhaysin, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Bint Tijrah, one of the women of Banu Abd al-Dar, he said: I entered the house of Al Abi Husayn with women of Quraysh, and the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - looked at me while he was running between al-Safa and al-Marwah. I saw him running in the belly of the valley, and his waist-wrapper was turning from the intensity of running, such that I would say: I see his knee. I heard him saying: Run, for Allah has prescribed running upon you."
"22241","574 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Mu'ammil, from Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhaysin, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, she said: Habibah narrated to us, she said: I was among women of Quraysh in the house of Abi Husayn, while the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was running between al-Safa and al-Marwah. I heard him saying: Run, for running has been prescribed upon you. She said: His izar was turning about him from the intensity of running."
"22242","575 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mu'ammil al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn narrated to us, from Ata, from Habibah bint Abi Tijrah, she said: I looked at the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - while he was circumambulating between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and I was among women of Quraysh, and he was running at the end of the people saying: Run, for Allah has prescribed running upon you. I looked at him while he was running, and his waist-cloth was turning from the intensity of running."
"22243","576 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Umar al-Muqaddami narrated to us, al-Khalil ibn Uthman al-Tamimi narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Nubayh, from his grandmother Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Habibah bint Abi Tijrah, she said: I looked out from an opening between al-Safa and al-Marwah and saw the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - running between al-Safa and al-Marwah, saying to his Companions: Run, for Allah has prescribed running upon you. Had you seen him, from the intensity of running the izar would turn around his belly and his thighs until I saw the whiteness of his thighs."
"22244","The chapter of Kha'. Khawlah bint Qays ibn Quhayd ibn Qays ibn Tha'labah al-Ansari, the wife of Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, kunya Umm Muhammad. 577 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, (H) and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to me, both said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Ubayd Sanuta, he said: We entered upon Khawlah bint Qays while she was the wife of al-Nu'man ibn al-Ajlan at that time, and she is the one who had been with Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib. We said to her: Narrate to us, O Umm Muhammad. Her husband said to her: Look, O Umm Muhammad, what you narrate, for narrating from the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - without certainty is grave. She said: Evil is what I have if I narrate to them from the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - what benefits them, and lie about the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -. I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: The world is green and sweet; whoever takes wealth with its right, it will be blessed for him in it. And many a one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger as his soul wishes - for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"22245","578 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Ubayd ibn al-Walid, he said: I heard Khawlah bint Qays ibn Qahd, and she had been under Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: This wealth is green and sweet; whoever attains it with its right, it will be blessed for him in it. And many a one who plunges into whatever his soul wishes of the wealth of Allah and His Messenger - for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"22246","579 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abd Allah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Ubayd Sanuta, he said: Umm Muhammad, the wife of Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, used to narrate. She said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered upon Hamzah, and they mentioned the world. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The world is green and sweet; whoever takes it with its right, Allah will bless it for him in it. And many a one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger in what his soul desires - for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"22247","580 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah, from Ubayd Sanuta, from Khawlah bint Qays, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and Hamzah discussed the world together. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The world is sweet and green; whoever takes its surplus, it will be blessed for him. And many a one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger - for him is the Fire on the day he meets Him."
"22248","581 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah, from Ubayd, from Khawlah, the wife of Hamzah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and Hamzah mentioning the world, and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The world is green; whoever takes it with its right, it will be blessed for him in it. And many a one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger - for him is the Fire on the day he meets his Lord."
"22249","582 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, (H) and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, (H) and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, all said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah, from Ubayd Sanuta, from Khawlah bint Qays ibn Quhayd, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - discussing the world with Hamzah, and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The world is sweet and green; whoever takes its surplus, it will be blessed for him in it. And many a one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger - for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"22250","583 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to me, from Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah, from Ubayd Sanuta, from Khawlah bint Qays, she said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The world is green and sweet; whoever takes it with its right, Allah will bless it for him in it. And many a one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger - for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"22251","584 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah, from Ubayd Sanuta, from Khawlah bint Qays, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: This wealth is sweet and green; whoever takes it with its right, it will be blessed for him in it. And many a one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger - for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"22252","585 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah, from Ubayd Sanuta, from Khawlah bint Qays, that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - came to Hamzah, and Khawlah was the wife of Hamzah. They discussed the world, and the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The world is sweet and green; whoever takes it with its right, Allah will bless it therein. And many a one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger - for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"22253","586 - Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran al-Naqid narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Isa al-Attar narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Aban al-Muktib, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah, from Ubayd Sanuta, from Khawlah bint Qays, that Hamzah and the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - discussed the world together. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The world is green and sweet; whoever takes it with its right, it will be blessed for him in it. And many a one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger - for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"22254","587 - Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Waki'i narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Mu'ammil ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah, from Ubayd Sanuta, from Khawlah bint Qays, that Hamzah and the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - discussed the world together - and he mentioned the like of it."
"22255","588 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, (H) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, both said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Isa ibn al-Nu'man, of the offspring of Rafi' ibn Khadij, narrated to me, he said: Mu'adh ibn Rifa'ah ibn Rafi' ibn Khadij narrated to me, from Khawlah bint Qays, and she had been under Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered upon me, and I made kharirah for him and presented it to him. He put his hand in it and felt its heat, so he withdrew it and said: O Khawlah, we do not endure heat or cold. O Khawlah, Allah has given me al-Kawthar, and it is a river in Paradise. No creature is dearer to me to come to it than your people. O Khawlah, many a one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger in what his soul desires - for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"22256","589 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Khawlah bint Qays ibn Qahd, and she had been the wife of Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, and he was killed while she was his wife. She came to the Prophet of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - visiting him. She said: O Prophet of Allah, I desired to meet you and ask you about something: I was told that you mention that you have a Hawd from such-and-such to such-and-such. He said to her: Yes. And the dearest of people to me - or the dearest of people to me - for your people to come to it. She said: So I brought near to him asidah in a tawr. When he put his hand in it, it burned, and he said: Hass. Then he said: When heat befalls the son of Adam, he says Hass, and when cold befalls him, he says Hass."
"22257","590 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Khawlah bint Hakim, she said: I said: I have heard that you have a Hawd. He said: Yes, and the dearest of those who come to me are your people. Thus Abu Khalid narrated it, from Khawlah bint Hakim, and the correct is the hadith of Hammad ibn Zayd."
"22258","591 - al-Husayn ibn al-Samaydi' al-Antaki narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Ibn Abi al-Jawn, from Abu Sa'd, from Mu'awiyah ibn Ishaq, from Khawlah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Allah does not sanctify a nation in which the weak cannot take the right from the strong without being made to stammer. Then he said: Whoever whose creditor turns away from his right while pleased with him, the beasts of the earth and the fish of the water invoke blessings upon him. And whoever whose creditor turns away while angry, there is written upon him, for every day, night, Friday, and month he wrongs."
"22259","592 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Hibban ibn Ali narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Tarif, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Khawlah, the wife of Hamzah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - owed a wasq of dates to a man of Banu Sa'idah. He came to him to settle it, and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - ordered a man of the Ansar to settle it. He settled it with dates inferior to his dates, and he refused to accept it. He said: Do you refuse against the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -? He said: Yes, and who is more deserving of justice than the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -? The eye of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - filled with his tears. Then he said: He has spoken the truth; who is more deserving of justice than me? Allah does not sanctify a nation in which the weak cannot take his right from the strong without being made to stammer. Then he said: O Khawlah, count for him, accompany him, and settle him, for there is no debtor who leaves his creditor pleased except that the beasts of the land and the fish of the seas invoke blessings upon him. And there is no debtor who puts off his creditor while being able except that Allah writes upon him a sin for every day and night."
"22260","593 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, that al-Dahhak ibn Abd Allah al-Qurashi narrated to him: that Mahmud ibn Labid narrated to him, from Ibnat Qahd, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Shall I not inform you of the expiation of sins? Thorough ablution at disliked times, steps to the prayers, and waiting for prayer after prayer."
"22261","594 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from al-Dahhak ibn Abd Allah al-Qurashi, from Mahmud ibn Labid, that Khawlah bint Qays ibn Qahd narrated to him that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Shall I not inform you of the expiations of sins? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Thorough ablution at disliked times, many steps to the mosques, and waiting for prayer after prayer."
"22262","Khawlah bint Qays, Umm Subayyah al-Juhaniyyah. 595 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Kharijah ibn al-Harith ibn Rafi' ibn Makith al-Juhani narrated to me, from Salim ibn Sarj, the freedman of Umm Subayyah bint Qays, and she is Khawlah bint Qays, and she is the grandmother of Kharijah ibn al-Harith, that he heard her saying: My hand and the hand of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - have alternated in one vessel."
"22263","596 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, (H) and Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd informed me, from Salim ibn al-Nu'man, from Umm Subayyah al-Juhaniyyah, she said: My hand and the hand of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - alternated in one vessel in ablution."
"22264","597 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (H) and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr and Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, all said: Waki' narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Salim ibn al-Nu'man ibn Kharrabudh, he said: I heard Umm Subayyah al-Juhaniyyah saying: My hand alternated with the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - in ablution from one vessel."
"22265","598 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Salim ibn al-Nu'man ibn Kharrabudh, he said: I heard Umm Subayyah saying: My hand and the hand of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - alternated in ablution from one vessel."
"22266","599 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Salim ibn al-Nu'man, from a woman of Juhaynah called Umm Subayyah, she said: I would sometimes contend with the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - over the vessel; I and he would perform ablution from one vessel."
"22267","600 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishkab narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Mihzam, from Abu Hafs, from Abu al-Nu'man, from Umm Subayyah, she said: My hand and the hand of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - alternated in one vessel in ablution."
"22268","Khawlah bint Hakim ibn Umayyah ibn Harithah ibn al-Awqas ibn Murrah ibn Hilal al-Sulamiyyah, the wife of Uthman ibn Maz'un, and she was among those who offered themselves to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -. 601 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Khallad al-Iskandarani narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Khawlah bint Hakim ibn al-Awqas, that she was among those who offered themselves to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -."
"22269","602 - Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali al-Madani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: Khawlah bint Hakim was among those who offered themselves to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -."
"22270","603 - Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd informed us, (H) and Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from al-Harith ibn Ya'qub, that Ya'qub ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj narrated to him that he heard Busr ibn Sa'id saying: I heard Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas saying: I heard Khawlah bint Hakim al-Sulamiyyah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: Whoever stops at a stopping place and says: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He created - nothing will harm him until he departs from that stopping place of his."
"22271","604 - Abu Yazid Yusuf ibn Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib and al-Harith ibn Ya'qub, from Ya'qub ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from Khawlah bint Hakim, that she heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: When one of you stops at a stopping place, let him say: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He created, for nothing will harm him until he departs from it."
"22272","605 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj narrated to us, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from Khawlah bint Hakim al-Sulamiyyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever stops at a stopping place and says: I seek refuge in the complete word of Allah from the evil of what He created - nothing in that stopping place will harm him until he departs."
"22273","606 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, (H) and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, both said: Wahb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Ya'qub ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd ibn Malik, from Khawlah bint Hakim, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: If one of you, when he stops at a stopping place, says: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He created - nothing of that stopping place will harm him until he departs."
"22274","607 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, (H) and Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, (H) and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, both said: Malik informed us, that it reached him from Ya'qub ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Sa'id, the freedman of the Hadramis, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, from Khawlah bint Hakim, that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever stops at a stopping place and says: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He created - nothing in that dwelling of his will harm him until he departs from it."
"22275","608 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, (H) and Abd Allah ibn Najiyah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Mani' narrated to us, both said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Rabi' ibn Malik, from Khawlah bint Hakim, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Whoever stops at a stopping place and says: I seek refuge in all the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He created - nothing in that dwelling of his will harm him until he moves from it."
"22276","609 - al-Hasan ibn Abd al-A'la al-Narsi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, (H) and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, both from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Suwayd saying: I heard Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz saying: The righteous woman Khawlah bint Hakim, the wife of Uthman ibn Maz'un, claimed that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - came out one day while embracing one of the sons of his daughter, saying: By Allah, you make one miserly, cowardly, and ignorant. You are of the fragrance of Allah. And the last foothold that the Lord of the worlds trod was at Wajj. Ibn Abi Umar added in his hadith: Sufyan said: The last expedition the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - undertook was Ta'if. And the poet said."
"22277","Khawlah bint Hakim al-Ansariyyah. 610 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that Khawlah bint Hakim asked the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and said: O Messenger of Allah, a woman sees in a dream what a man sees. He said: When she sees, let her wash."
"22278","611 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Khawlah bint Hakim, that she sought the fatwa of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - about a woman who sees in her sleep what a man sees: is washing obligatory upon her? He said: Yes, when she sees water."
"22279","612 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Khawlah bint Hakim, that she asked the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - about a woman who sees in her sleep what a man sees. He said: There is nothing upon her, just as when a man does not ejaculate, there is no washing upon him until he ejaculates."
"22280","613 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Khawlah bint Hakim, that she asked the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - about a woman who sees in her sleep what a man sees. He said: There is nothing upon her, just as when a man does not ejaculate, there is nothing upon him."
"22281","614 - al-Hasan ibn Abd al-A'la al-Narsi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Ibrahim ibn Suwayd, from Ibn Abi Suwayd al-Thaqafi, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, he said: The righteous woman Khawlah bint Hakim claimed that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Children are cause of grief, cowardice, ignorance, and miserliness. And the last foothold Allah Almighty trod was at Wajj."
"22282","615 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit al-Jazari narrated to us, from al-Wazi' ibn Nafi', from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Khawlah bint Hakim, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I menstruate and I have only one garment. He said: Wash it and pray in it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, a trace of blood remains in it. He said: It will not harm you."
"22283","616 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Khawlah bint Hakim, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, you have a Hawd? He said: Yes, and the dearest of those who come to me are your people. Thus Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated it, and people said: from Khawlah bint Qays."
"22284","Khawlah bint Thamir al-Ansariyyah. 617 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from al-Nu'man ibn Abi Ayyash al-Zuraqi, from Khawlah bint Thamir al-Ansariyyah, she said: I heard the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: The world is sweet and green, and men will plunge into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger without right; for them is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"22285","Khawlah bint al-Yaman al-Absiyyah, the sister of Hudhayfah, and it is said Fatimah. 618 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Bashshar ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from his wife, from the sister of Hudhayfah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - addressed us and said: O assembly of women, do you not have in silver what suffices you? For there is no woman who adorns herself with gold and displays it except that she will be punished with it."
"22286","619 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from his wife, from the sister of Hudhayfah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - addressed us and said: O assembly of women, do you not have in silver what suffices you? For there is no woman among you who adorns herself with gold and displays it except that she will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection."
"22287","620 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, both said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Mansur, from Rib'i, from his wife, from the sister of Hudhayfah, she said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - addressed us and said: O assembly of women, do you not have in silver what suffices you? No woman among you wears gold and displays it except that she will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection."
"22288","621 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Absi narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from his wife, from the sister of Hudhayfah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - stood among us, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O assembly of women, do you not have in silver with which to adorn yourselves? No woman adorns herself with gold and displays it except that she will be punished with it."
"22289","622 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abidah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from his wife, from the sister of Hudhayfah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - addressed us and said: O assembly of women, do you not have in silver with which to adorn yourselves? No woman among you adorns herself with gold except that she will be punished for it."
"22290","623 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ammi narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Rib'i, from his wife, from the sister of Hudhayfah, that she heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - addressing, and he said: O assembly of women, do you not have in silver with which to adorn yourselves? No woman among you wears gold and displays it except that she will be punished with it."
"22291","624 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Umar ibn Ubayd al-Tanafisi narrated to us, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from his wife, from the sister of Hudhayfah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - addressed us and said: O assembly of women, do you not have in silver with which to adorn yourselves? No woman adorns herself with gold and displays it except that she will be punished with it."
"22292","625 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from his wife, from the sister of Hudhayfah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - addressed us, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O assembly of women, do you not have in silver with which to adorn yourselves? No woman adorns herself with gold and displays it except that she will be punished with it."
"22293","626 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi' al-Kufi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Hudhayfah, from his paternal aunt, she said: I entered upon the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - while he had fever and the fever had intensified. I said: You, O Messenger of Allah, the fever has intensified upon you; if you supplicated Allah, He would remove it from you. He said: The most severely tried of people are the prophets, then those next to them. She said: A waterskin had been hung for him on a tree, and he lay under it with water dripping upon his chest."
"22294","627 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Hudhayfah, from his paternal aunt, she said: We entered upon the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - among the Muhajir women visiting him while he had fever. He ordered a waterskin containing water, and it was hung on a tree. The water began to drip upon his chest from the intensity of what he felt. We said: O Messenger of Allah, if you supplicated Allah, He would remove what is with you. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The most severely tried of people are the prophets, then those next to them, then those next to them."
"22295","628 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Husayn, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Hudhayfah, from his paternal aunt, that she entered upon the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -. He ordered a waterskin, and it was hung on a tree. Then he lay under it, and it began to drip upon his chest. I said: Supplicate Allah and He will remove it from you. He said: The most severely tried of people are the prophets, then those next to them."
"22296","629 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Sa'id ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I heard Abu Ubaydah ibn Hudhayfah narrating from his paternal aunt Fatimah, she said: I visited the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - among women, and he had hung the waterskin dripping upon him from the intensity of fever. I said: O Messenger of Allah, if you supplicated, its severity would leave you. He said: The most severely tried of people are the prophets, then the righteous, then the best, then the best."
"22297","630 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, both said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Husayn, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Hudhayfah, from his paternal aunt, she said: I entered upon the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - while he had fever. He ordered a waterskin, and it was hung on a tree. Then he lay under it, and the water began to drip upon his chest. I said to him: O Messenger of Allah, if you supplicated Allah, He would remove it from you. He said: Among the most severely tried of people are the prophets, then those next to them, then those next to them."
"22298","631 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim Abu Ma'mar al-Qati'i narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Husayn, from Khaythamah, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Hudhayfah, from his paternal aunt, she said: I entered upon the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - while he was suffering fever, and he had hung a waterskin dripping upon his chest. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this? He said: We, the assembly of prophets, trial is doubled upon us."
"22299","632 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jumhur ibn Mansur narrated to us, (H) and Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, both said: Ali ibn Thabit al-Jazari narrated to us, from al-Wazi' ibn Nafi', from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Khawlah bint al-Yaman, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: There is no good in the gathering of women except at a dead person, for when they gather they say and say."
"22300","Khawlah bint Malik ibn Tha'labah, the wife of Aws ibn al-Samit, and she is the one from whom zihar was made. 633 - Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ma'mar ibn Abd Allah ibn Hanzalah, from Yusuf ibn Abd Allah ibn Salam, he said: Khawlah bint Tha'labah narrated to me, and she had been with Aws ibn al-Samit, the brother of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, she said: He entered upon me one day and spoke to me about something while he was as if irritated. I answered him back, and he said: You are to me as the back of my mother. Then he went out and sat, then called his people, then returned to me and wanted me for himself. I refused him, and he wrestled me and I wrestled him, and I overcame him as a woman overcomes a weak man. I said: No, by the One in whose hand is Khuwaylah's soul, you shall not reach her until Allah judges concerning me and you. I came to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - complaining to him of what I had met from him. He said: Your husband and your cousin; fear Allah. Then Allah sent down: Allah has heard the statement of she who disputes with you concerning her husband and complains to Allah - until the expiation. Then the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Order him to free a neck. I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, he has no neck to free. He said: Then let him fast two consecutive months. I said: O Messenger of Allah, he is an old man; by Allah, he cannot fast. He said: Then let him feed sixty poor. I said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, he has nothing to feed with. He said: Rather, we shall help him with an irq of dates, and the irq is a basket holding thirty sa's. I said: And I shall help him with another irq. He said: You have done well; order him to give it in charity."
"22301","634 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Yazid, from Khawlah bint al-Samit, and her husband was ill. He called her, and she was slow to him. He said to her: If you come near me or I tread you, you are to me as the back of my mother. She came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and complained that to him. He did not answer her anything, and nothing concerning it had reached him. Then she came to him another time, and the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - came and said: Free a neck. He said: I do not have. He said: Fast two consecutive months. He said: I cannot. He said: Then feed sixty poor thirty sa's. He said: I do not own that unless you help me. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - helped him with fifteen sa's, and the people helped him until it was complete. He said: By Allah, there is no one poorer in need of it than me and my household. He said: Take it, you and your household. Abu al-Qasim said: Thus he said Khawlah bint al-Samit, and she is Khawlah bint Tha'labah, the wife of Aws ibn al-Samit."
"22302","Khawlah, without lineage. 635 - al-Husayn ibn al-Samaydi' al-Antaki narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Jawn, from Abu Sa'd, from Mu'awiyah ibn Ishaq, from Khawlah, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Allah does not sanctify a nation in which the weak cannot take his right from the strong without being made to stammer. And he said: Whoever turns away from his creditor while he is pleased with him, the beasts of the earth and the fish of the seas invoke blessings upon him. And whoever turns away from his creditor while he is angry, there is written upon him, for every day, night, Friday, and month he wrongs."
"22303","Khawlah, the servant of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -. 636 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Hafs ibn Sa'id al-Qurashi narrated to us, my mother narrated to me, from her mother, and she had been the servant of the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -: that a puppy entered the house and entered under the bed and died. The Prophet of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - remained days with no revelation descending upon him. He said: O Khawlah, what has happened in the house of the Messenger of Allah? Jibril does not come to me. Has something happened in the house of the Messenger of Allah? I said: By Allah, no day better than our day has passed upon us. He took his cloak, wore it, and went out. I said: If only I prepared the house and swept it. I leaned with the broom under the bed, and something heavy came; I kept at it until I brought it out, and it was a dead puppy. I took it in my hand and cast it behind the house. The Prophet of Allah came with his beard trembling - and when revelation came to him, trembling seized him. He said: O Khawlah, cover me. Then Allah sent down: By the morning brightness, and the night when it covers, your Lord has not forsaken you nor hates you."
"22304","Khalidah bint Anas al-Ansariyyah, then al-Sa'idiyyah. 637 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Umarah, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad, that Khalidah bint Anas, Umm Bani Hazm al-Sa'idiyyah, came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and showed him ruqyas, and he commanded concerning them."
"22305","Khulaydah bint Qa'nab. 638 - Ahmad ibn Zayd ibn al-Harish al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Bahrani narrated to us, Humayd ibn Hammad ibn Abi al-Khuwar Abi al-Jahm narrated to us, Taghlib bint al-Khuwar narrated to me, from her maternal aunt Khulaydah bint Qa'nab, and she had been among the women who came to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and gave him pledge, she said: A woman came to him wearing a bracelet of gold, and he refused to take her pledge. She left the crowd, threw away the bracelet, then came and he took her pledge. She went out looking at the bracelet; she went to look at it and it had been taken."
"22306","Khadrah, the servant of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -. 639 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, he said: There was a servant of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - called Khadrah."
"22307","Khansa' bint Khidham ibn Khalid al-Ansariyyah. 640 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Malik narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman and Mujammi', the sons of Yazid ibn Jariyah, from Khansa' bint Khidham, that her father married her off while she was previously married, and she disliked that. She came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -, and he annulled his marriage."
"22308","641 - Sa'id ibn Isra'il al-Qati'i narrated to us, Hibban ibn Musa al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid ibn Wadi'ah, from Khansa' bint Khidham, she said: My father married me off while I disliked it, and I was a virgin. I complained of that to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -, and he said: Do not marry her off while she dislikes."
"22309","642 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abd al-Rahman and Mujammi', the sons of Yazid ibn Jariyah, from Khansa' bint Khidham, that her father married her off - while she was a girl - unwilling, and the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - annulled her marriage."
"22310","643 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Hajjaj ibn al-Sa'ib, from his father, from his grandmother Khansa' bint Khidham ibn Khalid, that she became widowed from a man, and her father married her to a man of Banu Amr ibn Awf, and she yearned for Abu Lubabah ibn Abd al-Mundhir. Her case was raised to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -. A man ordered, and her father married her to a man of Banu Amr ibn Awf, and she yearned for Abu Lubabah."
"22311","644 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Muslim al-Mustamli Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that Khansa' bint Khidham, her father married her off while she disliked it. She came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -, and he annulled her marriage."
"22312","Khayrah bint Abi Hadrad, Umm al-Darda', and she is called Hujaymah. 645 - Habbush ibn Rizq Allah al-Misri narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Zabban ibn Fa'id narrated to us, from Abu Marhum, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas, from Umm al-Darda', that the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - met her while she was coming from the bathhouse and said: Where have you come from, O Umm al-Darda'? She said: From the bathhouse, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Any woman who puts off her clothes in other than her house tears the covering between her and Allah."
"22313","646 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Rushdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Zabban ibn Fa'id, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas, from his father, he said: I heard Umm al-Darda' saying: I came out of the bathhouse and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - met me and said: Where from, O Umm al-Darda'? I said: From the bathhouse. He said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, no woman puts off her clothes in other than the house of one of her mothers except that she tears every covering between her and the Most Merciful, blessed and exalted."
"22314","647 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Asbahani narrated to us, (H) and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Ahmad ibn Asad narrated to us, all said: Sharik narrated to us, from Khalaf ibn Hawshab, from Maymun ibn Mihran, he said: I said to Umm al-Darda': Did you hear anything from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -? She said: Yes. I entered upon him while he was sitting in the gathering, and I heard him saying: The first thing placed in the Scale is good character."
"22315","648 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Ali ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Amir, from Umm al-Darda', from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - he said: Whoever guards in something of the coasts of the Muslims for three days, it suffices him for a year's guarding."
"22316","649 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Tha'labah ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abu Imran Sulayman ibn Abd Allah, from Umm al-Darda', from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - he said: Allah created disease and cure, so seek treatment, and do not seek treatment with the unlawful."
"22317","650 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Bilal ibn Abi al-Darda' narrated to us, he said: My mother narrated to me, from her grandmother, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, does anger harm? He said: Yes, as beating harms trees."
"22318","651 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Safwan ibn Abd Allah ibn Safwan - and Umm al-Darda' loved him, so he came to her and found Umm al-Darda' but did not find Abu al-Darda'. She said to him: Do you intend Hajj this year? He said: Yes. She said: Supplicate Allah for us with good, for the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - used to say: The supplication of a Muslim for his brother in his absence is answered; at his head is an angel who says Amin to his supplication whenever he supplicates for him with good, and says: Amin, and for you the like. He said: Then I went out to the market and met Abu al-Darda', and he narrated to me from the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - the like of it."
"22319","652 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi' al-Tahhan al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh informed me, he said: Abu Sakhr narrated to me that Yuhannas Abu Musa narrated to him: that Umm al-Darda' narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - met her one day and said: Where have you come from, O Umm al-Darda'? She said: From the bathhouse. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to her: No woman removes her clothes in other than her house except that she tears the covering between her and Allah."
"22320","653 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from Ata al-KaykharanI, from Abd Allah ibn Babah, from Umm al-Darda', she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - saying: The best thing placed in the Scale on the Day of Resurrection is good character."
"22321","Khayrah, the wife of Ka'b ibn Malik. 654 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from a man of the offspring of Banu Ka'b ibn Malik called Abd Allah ibn Yahya, from his father, from his grandfather, from his grandmother Khayrah, the wife of Ka'b ibn Malik, that she came to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - with jewelry and said: I have given this in charity. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: It is not permissible for a woman to dispose of her wealth except with her husband's permission. Have you sought Ka'b's permission? I said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - sent to Ka'b and said: Have you permitted Khayrah to give her jewelry in charity? He said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - accepted it from her."
"22322","Al-Kharqa' al-Sawda', who used to remove harm from the mosque of the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -. 655 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, and he mentioned the hadith."
"22323","The chapter of Dal. Durrah bint Abi Lahab ibn Abd al-Muttalib, and the name of Abu Lahab is Abd al-Uzza. 656 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: I heard Amr ibn Uthman narrating from Ibn Abi Husayn, he said: Durrah bint Abi Lahab had been with al-Harith ibn Abd Allah ibn Nawfal, and she bore him Uqbah, al-Walid, and Abu Muslim. Then she came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - in Madinah, and the people spoke much about her parents. She came to the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and said: O Messenger of Allah, have only disbelievers given birth to other than me? The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to her: What is that? She said: The people of Madinah have hurt me concerning my parents. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said to her: When you pray Zuhr, pray where I see. The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - prayed Zuhr, then turned to her and faced the people with his face and said: O people, do you have lineage and I have no lineage? Umar jumped up and said: Allah's anger upon whoever angers you. He said: This is my cousin; let no one say to her but good."
"22324","657 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi, Ubayd ibn Ghannam, and Ahmad ibn Mas'ud al-Maqdisi narrated to us - they said: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abd Allah ibn Umayrah, from the husband of Durrah bint Abi Lahab, from her, she said: I was with A'ishah when a man was brought to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him -. He had called him while he was on the minbar and said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are best? She said: The man came and was seized, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have no sin; so-and-so ordered me. The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: The best of people are the most God-fearing of them, the most commanding of good, the most forbidding of evil, and the most joining of kinship."
"22325","658 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hakim al-Muqawwim narrated to us, al-Bakrawi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abd Allah ibn Umayrah, from a man, from the husband of the daughter of Abu Jahl, from the daughter of Abu Jahl, she said: The Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - passed by us and asked for drink. I stood to a jug and gave him drink. A man wearing two green garments asked him and he said: Worship Allah, associating nothing with Him, establish prayer, and give zakah. He said: Then he said: The best of my ummah is my generation, then those who follow them. Shu'bah erred in the isnad of this hadith."
"22326","659 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Tahir ibn Abi Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ma'bad ibn Qays, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umayrah narrated to me, he said: The husband of the daughter of Abu Lahab narrated to me, he said: The Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - entered upon us when I married the daughter of Abu Lahab and said: Is there any amusement?"
"22327","660 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Nafi', the freedman of Ibn Umar, and Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, and from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, and from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abu Hurayrah, and from Ammar ibn Yasir, they said: Durrah bint Abi Lahab arrived in Madinah as an emigrant and stayed in the house of Rafi' ibn al-Mu'alla al-Zuraqi. Women sitting with her from Banu Zurayq said to her: You are the daughter of Abu Lahab, about whom Allah Almighty says: Perish the hands of Abu Lahab, and perish he; his wealth and what he earned availed him not. What avails you your emigration? Durrah came to the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and complained to him of what they had said to her. He calmed her and said: Sit. Then he prayed Zuhr with the people and sat on the minbar a while, then said: O people, why am I hurt concerning my family? By Allah, my intercession will reach Hayy, Ha, Hakam, Suda', and Salhab on the Day of Resurrection."
"22328","The chapter of Ra'. Ruqayqah bint Abi Sayfi ibn Hashim ibn Abd Manaf. 661 - Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Hammad al-Barbari narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Abu al-Sakan al-Ta'i narrated to us, the paternal uncle of my father Zahr ibn Hisn narrated to us, from his grandfather Humayd ibn Munhib, he said: Urwah ibn Mudarris narrated to me, he said: Makhramah ibn Nawfal narrated, from his mother Ruqayqah bint Abi Sayfi ibn Hashim, and she had been with Abd al-Muttalib, she said: Successive years of drought befell Quraysh, drying the udder and thinning the bone. While I lay sleepless with worry - or worried - a caller cried out in a hoarse voice saying: O assembly of Quraysh, this dispatched Prophet, his days have cast their shadow over you, and this is the time of his stars. Come to life and fertility. Look for a man among you, eminent, large-boned and bulky, white with radiance, with long eyelashes, smooth-cheeked, high-nosed; he has a resolved character he restrains, and a sunnah he guides to. Let him go apart, he and his son, and let a man from every clan descend to him. Let them pour water, touch perfume, touch the Corner, then ascend Abu Qubays. Then let the man supplicate and the people say Amin, and you will be rained upon as you wish. I awoke, by Allah's knowledge, frightened; my skin shivered and my mind wandered. I recounted my dream and slept in the ravines of Makkah. By the sanctity and the Sanctuary, there remained no Bat'hi but said: This is Shaybat al-Hamd. The men of Quraysh came to him, and a man from every clan descended to him. They poured, touched perfume, touched the Corner, then ascended Abu Qubays and lined up around him as far as their striving reached, until when they stood even at the mountain top, Abd al-Muttalib stood, and with him the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - a boy grown or near grown. He raised his hand and said: O Allah, Filler of need and Remover of distress, You are taught, not taught, and asked, not niggardly. These are Your male and female servants at the courtyards of Your Sanctuary, complaining to You of their year that has removed hoof and cloven hoof. O Allah, rain upon us a soaking, fertile rain. By the Lord of the Ka'bah, they had not moved until the sky burst with its water and the valley filled with its outpouring. I heard the elders of Quraysh and their notables - Abd Allah ibn Jud'an, Harb ibn Umayyah, and Hisham ibn al-Mughirah - saying to Abd al-Muttalib: Congratulations to you, O father of al-Batha'; the people of al-Batha' live by you. Concerning that, Ruqayqah bint Abi Sayfi says: And the flowing torrent glistened."
"22329","Ruqayqah al-Thaqafiyyah. 662 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'la ibn Ka'b al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, Abd Rabbih ibn al-Hakam narrated to me, he said: The daughter of Ruqayqah narrated to me, from her mother Ruqayqah, she said: When the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - came seeking help at Ta'if, he entered upon me, and I brought out for him a drink of sawiq. He said: O Ruqayqah, do not worship their taghut nor pray to it. She said: Then they will kill me. He said: When they say to you, then say: My Lord is the Lord of this taghut; and when you see it, turn your back to it. Then the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - went out from me."
"22330","Ra'itah bint Sufyan al-Khuza'iyyah. 663 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, both said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman al-Hatibi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from A'ishah bint Qudamah ibn Maz'un, she said: I was with my mother Ra'itah bint Sufyan, a woman of Khuza'ah, while the Prophet - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - was taking their pledge, saying: I take your pledge upon that you associate nothing with Allah, steal not, commit not adultery, kill not your children, bring not a slander you forge between your hands and your feet, and disobey me not in good. They lowered their heads, and the Messenger of Allah - peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - said: Say: Yes, as far as you are able. We said: Yes, as far as we are able. I would say as they said, and my mother would say: Say: Yes, say: Yes."
"22331","Rubayyi' bint al-Nadr. 664 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that al-Rubayyi' bint al-Nadr slapped a slave-girl of the Ansar and broke her incisor tooth, so they came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and demanded retaliation, so Anas ibn al-Nadr said: O Messenger of Allah, will the tooth of al-Rubayyi' be broken? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Anas, the decree of Allah is retaliation, so the people pardoned, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed among the servants of Allah are those who, if they swear upon Allah, He fulfills it; among them is Anas ibn al-Nadr."
"22332","665 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that al-Rubayyi' bint al-Nadr came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, my son Harithah was struck on the day of Badr; if he is in Paradise I shall be patient and seek reward, and if it is otherwise I shall exert myself in weeping. So he said: O Umm Harithah, they are gardens within Paradise, and he has attained al-Firdaws, the highest."
"22333","Ra'itah bint Abd Allah al-Thaqafiyyah, wife of Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud. 666 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ra'itah, wife of Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, and she was skilled with her hands, and she used to sell of her handiwork and give charity, so she said to Abd Allah one day: You and your child have preoccupied me, so I am not able to give charity along with you at all. So he said: Would you not like that you have two rewards? So they both asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about that, and he said: Indeed for you is the reward of what you spend on them."
"22334","667 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, that Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah informed him, from Ra'itah bint Abd Allah, wife of Ibn Mas'ud, mother of his child, and she was a skilled craftswoman, and Ibn Mas'ud had no wealth, and she used to spend on him and on his child from the price of her handiwork, so she said: By Allah, you and your child have preoccupied me from charity, so I am not able to give charity along with you at all. So he said: I would not like you to do it if there is no reward for you in that. So she asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, she and he, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman skilled in a craft by which I earn, and neither I nor my husband nor my child have anything, and they have preoccupied me so I cannot give charity. So he said: For you in that is the reward of what you spend on them."
"22335","668 - Muhammad ibn Mu'adh al-Khayli narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Maslamah al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ra'itah, wife of Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, and she was a skilled craftswoman, and Ibn Mas'ud had no wealth, and she used to spend on him and on his child from the price of her handiwork, so she said: By Allah, you and your child have preoccupied me from charity, so I am not able to give charity along with you at all. So he said: I would not like you to do it if there is no reward for you in that. So she asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, she and he, and he said: For you in that is a reward."
"22336","669 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ra'itah, wife of Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, she said: I asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I am a woman skilled in a craft by which I earn, and neither I nor my husband nor my child have anything; they preoccupy me so I do not give charity. So he said: For you in that is the reward of what you spend on them."
"22337","670 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah al-Thaqafi, that Ra'itah, sister of Abd Allah al-Thaqafi, was under Ibn Mas'ud, and she was a skilled craftswoman who would craft and sell of her handiwork, so she said to Ibn Mas'ud: You and your child have preoccupied me from spending in the cause of Allah, so I am not able to spend in the cause of Allah. So he said: I would not like you to do it if there is no reward for you in that. So she asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Spend on them, for indeed for you is the reward of what you spend on them."
"22338","Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra, an Ansari woman. Abu Salamah, and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Thawban, from Rubayyi'. 671 - Habush ibn Rizq Allah al-Misri narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad Yahya ibn al-Nadr, from Abu Salamah, and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh, that she heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrating about the wife of Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas al-Ansari, that there was some discord between him and his wife, and he was a man in whom there was harshness, so she came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and spoke to him, so he sent for Thabit ibn Qays, and they spoke in his presence as Allah willed, then he accepted compensation from her, and she ransomed herself from him, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded her to observe a waiting period of one menstruation."
"22339","Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from al-Rubayyi'. 672 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father and Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to me, they said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah narrated to us, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra, he said: I said: Narrate to me your hadith. She said: I sought separation from my husband, then I came to Umar and asked him what waiting period is upon me. So he said: There is no waiting period upon you, unless he has recently been with you, then you remain until you menstruate one menstruation. She said: And in that only the judgment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning Maryam al-Maghaliyyah is followed, and she was with Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, and she separated from him by compensation."
"22340","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi'. 673 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, he said: I entered upon al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra, and she said: Who are you? So I said: I am Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil ibn Abi Talib. She said: Who is your mother? I said: Raytah bint Ali, or so-and-so bint Ali ibn Abi Talib. She said: Welcome to you, O son of my brother. I said: I have come to ask you about the ablution of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. She said: Yes, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to visit us, and he would perform ablution in this vessel, and in the like of this vessel, and it is about a mudd. She said: He would wash his hands, then rinse his mouth and sniff water, then wash his face three times, then wash his hands three times, then wipe his head twice, and wipe his ears, their outer and inner sides, and wash his feet three times each."
"22341","674 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to me, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, similar to it."
"22342","675 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Isma'il narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra al-Ansariyyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us, so I poured purification water for him, and he rinsed his mouth and sniffed water, and washed his face three times each, and his forearms three times each, and wiped his head twice, beginning with its back before its front, and wiped the back of his ears, and inserted his fingers into the holes of his ears, and washed his feet three times each."
"22343","676 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to come to us, so we would bring him a wash-vessel of ours in which there was water, taking a Madinan mudd, a mudd and a half or a third; so I would pour upon him, and he would wash his hands three times, and rinse his mouth and sniff water, and wash his face three times, and wipe his head one time, and wipe his ears, their outer and inner sides, and purify his feet."
"22344","677 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar narrated to us, they said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, he said: Ali ibn al-Husayn sent me to al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra to ask her about the ablution of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to perform ablution in her presence, so I came to her and asked her, and she brought out to me a vessel, and that was about a mudd and a quarter by the Hashimi measure, and she said: I used to bring out his ablution water for him in this, so he would begin and pour upon his right hand, and wash it three times before inserting it into the vessel, then rinse his mouth and blow his nose three times, and wash his face three times, and wash his right hand three times, and wash his left hand three times, then wipe his head moving forward and backward, and Sufyan described how he wipes his head until he reached its beginning; this is the wording of the hadith of Ibn Abi Umar, and Ibn Abi Umar added in his hadith, Sufyan said: And Ibn Ajlan added to me in it, from Ibn Aqil, he said: Al-Rubayyi' said: Then he wiped his temples and cheeks, then returned them to its middle, then extended them to his nape, then wiped his ears, then washed his feet."
"22345","678 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution and wiped the front of his ears and their back."
"22346","679 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, they said: Musaddad narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Sa'id, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiped his head with the remainder of what was in his hand, so he began with the back of his head, then drew it to its front, then drew it to its back."
"22347","680 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi', that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution three times each."
"22348","681 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to come to us often. She said: He came to us, so we placed the wash-vessel for him, and he performed ablution: he washed his palms three times, then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water once, and washed his face three times, and his forearms three times, and wiped with what remained of his ablution water twice, beginning with its back, then he returned his hands upon his forelock, and washed his feet three times each."
"22349","682 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh, she said: I performed the ablution for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so I brought him a wash-vessel holding a mudd, or a mudd and a third, and he said: Pour. So he performed ablution, and wiped the front of his head, and wiped the outer of his ears and their inner."
"22350","683 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us, so he performed ablution and wiped the front of his head, and wiped the outer of his ears and their inner."
"22351","684 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, he said: I heard al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to come to us, and I used to pour ablution water for him, so he would perform ablution in our presence in a wash-vessel of ours of the measure of a mudd and a half, and a mudd and a third, and I would pour upon his palms three times, then I would place it for him, so he would rinse his mouth and sniff water, and wash his face three times, and his hands three times, and wipe his head and his ears, then wash his feet three times each."
"22352","685 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Surayj ibn al-Nu'man al-Jawhari narrated to us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, he said: We entered upon al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra among a group, so I asked her about the ablution of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and she said: Yes, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution in about this vessel, and she was pointing with her hand to a small pitcher taking a mudd and a third by the first measure as I see, so he rinsed his mouth and sniffed water, and washed his face and his hands three times, then wiped the front of his head and its back, and wiped his ears along with the back of his head, and washed his feet."
"22353","686 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to come to us, so she narrated to us that he said: Pour ablution water. So I poured for him in a wash-vessel, and it is the small pitcher, taking a mudd and a third, or a mudd and a quarter, of water, and he said: Pour upon my hand. So he washed his palms three times, then said: Put down. She said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution while I was looking: he washed his face three times, and rinsed his mouth and sniffed water once, and washed his right hand three times, and washed his left hand three times, and wiped his head twice, beginning with the back of his head, then with its front, and with both his ears, their backs and their insides, and washed his right foot three times, and washed his left foot three times."
"22354","687 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiyy narrated to us, Ali ibn Ma'bad al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to come to us, so I would take a wash-vessel of ours of the measure of a mudd and a half, or a mudd and a third, and pour upon him of the water, so he would wash his hands three times, and rinse his mouth and sniff water, and wash his face three times, and wipe his head twice, then wash his feet three times each."
"22355","688 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, and Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, they said: Al-Layth narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed ablution in her presence, so he wiped his head: he wiped his whole head from above the hair, every side toward where the hair falls, without moving the hair from its state."
"22356","689 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil ibn Abi Talib, that al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra informed him that she saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performing ablution. She said: He wiped his head, what faces forward of it and what faces backward, and his temples and his ears, one time."
"22357","690 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fill his hands with water, then pour it, then wipe his head, its front and its back, then return to the middle of his head and wipe, and take his hands to his head and wipe his ears, their inside and their outside, and take the lobes of his ears."
"22358","691 - al-Nu'man ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti, the judge, narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Hazim, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon her and called for ablution water, so he was brought a vessel holding a mudd and a third, or a mudd and a half of the mudd of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he performed ablution: he washed his face, then washed his hand, and wiped his head, and wiped the back of his head until he reached its middle in every wipe."
"22359","692 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Khalid ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Hazim al-Zayyat narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, similar to it."
"22360","693 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Utbah al-Shaybani narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Shababab ibn Sawwar narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, perform ablution, so he took fresh water for his head, moving his hands backward and bringing them forward."
"22361","694 - Muhammad ibn Ya'qub ibn Sawrah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, and Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, they said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra, she said: I brought the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a basket of fresh dates and young cucumbers, so he gave me a handful full of jewelry, or gold."
"22362","Abu Ja'far al-Khatmi, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh. 695 - Zakariyya ibn Hamdawayh al-Saffar narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far al-Khatmi, he said: We were in Madinah on the day of Ashura, with slave-girls beating the tambourine and singing, so al-Rubayyi' entered upon us, and we mentioned that to her, so she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me on the morning of my wedding, and with me were two slave-girls singing and lamenting my fathers who were killed at Badr, and they were saying: And among us is a Prophet who knows what is in tomorrow. So he said: As for this, no; and say: None knows what is in tomorrow except Allah, mighty and majestic."
"22363","Abu Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Yasir, from al-Rubayyi'. 696 - Abd Allah ibn al-Saqr al-Sukkari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Musa al-Taymi narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Yasir, he said: I said to al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra: Describe the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to me. So she said: If you had seen him, you would have seen the sun rising."
"22364","697 - al-Qasim ibn Abbad al-Khattabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Yasir, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra, she said: Mu'awwidh ibn Afra sent me with a basket of fresh dates upon which were young cucumbers to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to love cucumbers, and they were good dates that had arrived from Bahrain, so he filled his hand from them and gave them to me."
"22365","Khalid ibn Dhakwan Abu al-Husayn al-Basri, from al-Rubayyi'. 698 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi Abu Khalifah narrated to us, they said: Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Khalid ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, that al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came and entered upon me on the morning after I was wed, and sat upon my bed, and little girls began beating a tambourine of theirs and lamenting those of my fathers killed on the day of Badr, until one of them said: And among us is a Prophet who knows what is in tomorrow. So he said: Leave this, and say what you were saying."
"22366","699 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abd al-Samad ibn Sulayman al-Azraq, from Khalid ibn Dhakwan, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me on the morning after I was wed, and she mentioned the like of it."
"22367","700 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Khalid ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent on the morning of the day of Ashura to the villages of the Ansar around Madinah: Whoever woke up fasting, let him complete his fast, and whoever woke up not fasting, let him fast the rest of his day. So we would fast it, and our small children would fast, and we would make for them the toy of wool, and go with them to the garden, and when one of them cried for food we would give him that, until it was time for breaking the fast."
"22368","701 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abd al-Samad ibn Sulayman al-Azraq, from Khalid ibn Dhakwan, he said: Al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh ibn Afra al-Ansariyyah narrated to me, she said: We would go out on expeditions with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, but we would not fight; rather we would give them water to drink and treat the wounded."
"22369","702 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Dhakwan, from al-Rubayyi', she said: We would go out on expeditions with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so we would give the people water to drink, and serve them, and return the slain and the wounded to Madinah."
"22370","Rumaythah al-Ansariyyah. 703 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah al-Harawi narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali al-Madini and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, they said: Abu Mus'ab narrated to us, they said: Yusuf ibn al-Majishun narrated to us, my father informed me, Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah informed me, from his grandmother Rumaythah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and if I wished to kiss the seal that was between his shoulders, from my nearness to him, I could have kissed it, while he was saying to Sa'd ibn Mu'adh on the day he died: The Throne of the Most Merciful shook for him."
"22371","Ruzaynah, freedwoman of Safiyyah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. 704 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, they said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, they said: Ulalyah bint al-Kumayt al-Atakiyyah narrated to us, from her mother Umaynah, she said: I said to Amat Allah bint Razinah: Did you hear your mother mention anything about the fast of Ashura? She said: Yes, I heard my mother Razinah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to honor it, to the extent that he would call his young children and the nursing infants of Fatimah on that day, and spit in their mouths, and say to their mothers: Do not nurse them until night. So his saliva would suffice them."
"22372","705 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, Ulalyah bint al-Kumayt narrated to us, from her mother Umaynah, from Amat Allah bint Razinah, from her mother Razinah, she said: When the day of Qurayzah and al-Nadir came, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came with Safiyyah bint Huyayy, with her forearm in his hand. When she saw the captives, she said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that you are the Messenger of Allah. So he released her forearm from his hand, and freed her, and proposed to her, and married her, and gave her Razinah as dowry."
"22373","706 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Ulalyah bint al-Kumayt narrated to us, from her mother Umaynah, from Amat Allah bint Razinah, from her mother Razinah, freedwoman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: That Hafsah, Mother of the Believers, visited A'ishah, Mother of the Believers, one day, and Sawdah entered upon them wearing a Yemeni tunic and a head-cover, with two specks like two lentils in the corner of her eye, of aloes and saffron. Ulalyah said: And I knew women adorning themselves with it for their husbands. So Hafsah said to A'ishah: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, will enter upon us, and there are two of us, and she is between us shining; I shall surely spoil her adornment today. So A'ishah said: Fear Allah, O Hafsah. So Sawdah said: What are you saying, and there was heaviness in her ears. So they said: The one-eyed has come out. She said: The one-eyed has come out? They said: Yes. She said: Where shall I hide? They said: Upon you is the tent, a tent of theirs of palm leaves in which they cooked pots, in which was a spider's web. So she went and entered it. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered, while the two were laughing, unable to speak to him from laughter. So he said: What is the laughter? So they pointed with their hands to the tent. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered the tent, and there was Sawdah trembling. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: What is wrong with you? So she said: O Messenger of Allah, the one-eyed has come out. So he said: He has not come out, and he shall surely come out. Then he entered and took her hand, and began shaking off the dust from her, and of the spider."
"22374","Rawdah. 707 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad and Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid al-Basri narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Jalil ibn al-Harith al-Saffar narrated to us, he said: Shaybah bint al-Aswad, daughter of my mother's aunt, narrated to me, she said: My grandmother Rawdah narrated to me, she said: I was a maidservant of a woman in Madinah, and when the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, emigrated from Makkah to Madinah, my mistress said to me, Rawdah: Stand at the door of the house, and when this man passes, inform me. So I stood, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to them with a group of his Companions, so I took hold of the edge of his cloak, and he smiled in my face - Shaybah said: And I think he wiped his hand upon my head - so I said to my mistress: O lady, here the man has come. So my mistress came out, and whoever was with her in the house, and he presented Islam to them, so they embraced Islam. He said: And Shaybah narrated to me, she said: Rawdah was with me in the house among Banu Sulaym; when the neighbors bought a slave, or a servant, or a garment, or food, they would say to her: O Rawdah, place your hand upon it; and everything she touched had blessing in it."
"22375","Rahma, not attributed. 708 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Sha'ir narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Balkhi narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from a woman called Rahma, she said: I was with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when a woman came to him with a son of hers and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate Allah for me concerning him for blessing, for three of mine have died. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Since you embraced Islam? She said: Yes. So he said: A strong shield. So a man said: Listen, O Rahma, to what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, says."
"22376","Chapter of Za. Zaynab bint Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Asad al-Makhzumi, and she is the stepdaughter of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. 709 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, that Zaynab bint Abi Salamah asked him: What have you named your daughter? He said: I named her Barrah. So she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade this name. I was named Barrah, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not declare yourselves pure; Allah knows best those of you who are pious. They said: What shall we name her? He said: Name her Zaynab."
"22377","710 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"22378","711 - al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, she said: My name was Barrah, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, named her Zaynab."
"22379","712 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Abbas ibn Abi Shamalah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ya'qub, from Quraybah bint Wahb ibn Abd Allah ibn Zam'ah, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, that she entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was bathing, so he took a handful of water and struck her face with it, and said: Behind you, O wicked one."
"22380","713 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to me, Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to me, that he entered upon Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, and she narrated to them, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was with Umm Salamah, and he entered upon her with al-Hasan and al-Husayn and Fatimah, so he placed al-Hasan on one side, and al-Husayn on one side, and Fatimah in his lap, then said: The mercy of Allah and His blessings upon you, people of the house; indeed He is Praiseworthy, Glorious. And I and Umm Salamah were sitting, so Umm Salamah wept, so he looked at her and said: What makes you weep? So she said: O Messenger of Allah, you have singled out these and left me and my daughter. So he said: You and your daughter are of the people of the house."
"22381","714 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yahya ibn al-Rabi' ibn Abi Rashid narrated to us, Amr ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from his father, he said: Zaynab bint Umm Salamah narrated to me, that the players were playing while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in the mosque, and he mentioned the hadith."
"22382","715 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, Attaf ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi narrated to us, from his mother, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, she said: My mother, when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered to bathe, would say: Go and enter. She said: So I entered, and he sprinkled water in my face, then said: Go back. Al-Attaf said: My mother said: So I saw the face of Zaynab, while she was a very old woman, and nothing of her face had diminished."
"22383","716 - Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Kulayb ibn Wa'il narrated to us, the stepdaughter of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to me, I think it is Zaynab, she said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the gourd vessel and the green glazed jar. He said: And I see in it the hollowed stump."
"22384","Zaynab bint Abi Mu'awiyah al-Thaqafiyyah, wife of Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud. 717 - Ubayd ibn Muhammad al-Kashwari al-San'ani narrated to us, Maymun ibn al-Hakam al-Shirazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sharhabil ibn Ju'shum narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Zaynab al-Thaqafiyyah, wife of Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you go out to the last evening prayer, do not touch perfume."
"22385","718 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Zaynab, wife of Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you attends the evening prayer, let her not touch perfume."
"22386","719 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Zaynab, wife of Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you attends the mosque, let her not touch perfume."
"22387","720 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj narrated to me, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Zaynab, wife of Abd Allah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you attends the mosque, let her not touch perfume."
"22388","721 - Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muslim, brother of al-Zuhri, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Zaynab, wife of Abd Allah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you attends the mosque, let her not touch perfume."
"22389","722 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Hisham, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Zaynab, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"22390","723 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, they said: Al-Layth narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Zaynab al-Thaqafiyyah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whichever of you goes out to the mosque, let her not touch perfume."
"22391","724 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, Asim ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ashja'i narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhubab, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Zaynab al-Thaqafiyyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood among us and said: Whichever of you attends the evening prayer, let her not touch perfume."
"22392","725 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Zaynab al-Thaqafiyyah, wife of Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Give charity, even from your jewelry. So Zaynab said to Abd Allah: Will it suffice me that I place my charity in you and in the orphaned sons of my brother? And Abd Allah was poor. So Abd Allah said: Ask the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about that. Zaynab said: So I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and there was a woman of the Ansar called Zaynab who had come to ask about what I had come to ask about. So Bilal came out to us, and we said to him: Ask the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and do not inform him who we are: Will it suffice me that I place my charity in my husband and the orphaned sons of my brother? So Bilal came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned it to him. So he said: Which of the Zaynabs? He said: The wife of Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, and a woman of the Ansar. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Inform her that she has two rewards: the reward of charity, and the reward of kinship."
"22393","726 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, they said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Amr ibn al-Harith ibn al-Mustaliq, from the nephew of Zaynab, wife of Abd Allah, from Zaynab, wife of Abd Allah, she said: Bilal came out, and we said to him: Ask the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, whether spending upon our husbands and what our laps contain suffices us as spending. So he entered and asked him, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Two rewards: the reward of charity, and the reward of kinship."
"22394","727 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, they said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Amr ibn al-Harith, nephew of Zaynab, from Zaynab, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, similar to it."
"22395","728 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Zaynab, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there reward for me if I give charity to the children of Abd Allah from other than me? So he said: For you are two shares of reward."
"22396","729 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Tarif al-Bajali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abu Ubaydah, from Amr ibn al-Harith ibn al-Mustaliq, from Zaynab, wife of Abd Allah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us while we were in the mosque and said: O assembly of women, give charity, and he mentioned the hadith."
"22397","730 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, that the wife of Ibn Mas'ud said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to me while I was among women of the Ansar and said: Give charity, even from your jewelry. So ask the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, whether my spending upon you and upon my nephews suffices me as charity, otherwise I shall spend it in the cause of Allah. So he said: I am shy to ask him, so ask him yourself. So I reached the door of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and there was a woman of the Ansar whose need was my need. Then Bilal passed by us, and we said: O Bilal, convey from us to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, greeting and mercy of Allah, and inform him that we have our husbands and the sons of our brothers; whether our spending upon our husbands and the sons of our brothers suffices us, otherwise we shall spend in the cause of Allah. So Bilal entered and informed him. So he said: Convey to them greeting and mercy of Allah, and inform them that their spending upon their husbands and the sons of their sisters is doubled: double of kinship, and double of charity."
"22398","731 - al-Husayn ibn Mansur al-Missisi al-Ramadi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abi Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Abi Yazid Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Mujalid ibn Sa'id, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Zaynab, wife of Abd Allah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed charity upon a relative is doubled twice in reward."
"22399","732 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Abu al-Umays, from Yazid ibn Ju'dubah, from Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Zaynab, wife of Abd Allah al-Thaqafi, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave her at Khaybar fifty wasqs of dates and twenty wasqs of barley in Madinah."
"22400","Zaynab bint Qays ibn Makhramah al-Zuhriyyah. 733 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Amr ibn Muhammad al-Anqazi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from his father, he said: Zaynab bint Qays ibn Makhramah made a contract of manumission with me for ten thousand, and when it fell due she left a thousand for me. And Zaynab was of those who prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, toward both prayer directions."
"22401","Zaynab al-Asadiyyah. 734 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Amir ibn Ibrahim al-Asbahani narrated to us, from Ya'qub ibn Abd Allah al-Qummi, from Anbasah ibn Sa'id, from Zakariyya ibn Khalid, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Mujahid, from Zaynab al-Asadiyyah, that she said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father died and left a slave-girl, and she gave birth to a boy, and we suspected her. So he said: Bring him to me. When they brought him to him, he looked at him and said: The inheritance is for him, and as for you, veil yourself from him."
"22402","Zaynab bint Nubayt al-Ansariyyah, wife of Anas ibn Malik. 735 - Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, and Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, they said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Umarah al-Hazmi, from Zaynab bint Nubayt ibn Jabir, wife of Anas ibn Malik, she said: Abu Umamah entrusted my mother and my maternal aunt to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so there came to him gold jewelry and pearls called al-ri'ath. She said: So he adorned them with the ri'ath."
"22403","Zaynab bint Humayd. 736 - Harun ibn Mallul al-Misri narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, Abu Aqil Zuhrah ibn Ma'bad narrated to me, from his grandfather Abd Allah ibn Hisham, and he had met the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and his mother Zaynab bint Humayd took him to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, he is small. So he wiped upon his head and supplicated for him."
"22404","Chapter of Sin. Sahlah bint Suhayl ibn Amr, wife of Abu Hudhayfah ibn Utbah ibn Rabi'ah, of her reports. 737 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd Allah ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Mulaykah informed me, that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr informed him, that A'ishah informed him, that Sahlah bint Suhayl ibn Amr came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, Salim, freedman of Abu Hudhayfah, is with us in our house, and he has reached what men reach, and has known what men know. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Nurse him, you become unlawful to him."
"22405","738 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qaddah, he said: Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from A'ishah, that the wife of Hudhayfah came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Salim, freedman of Abu Hudhayfah, enters upon me while I have laid aside my garment, so I find in myself. So he said: Nurse him, what you find will leave you."
"22406","739 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Maslamah al-Umawi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id and Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from A'ishah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded Sahlah bint Suhayl to nurse Salim, so that what was in the soul of Abu Hudhayfah would leave."
"22407","740 - Abu Yazid Yusuf ibn Yazid al-Qaratisiyy narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from A'ishah, she said: Sahlah bint Suhayl came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I see in the face of Abu Hudhayfah something concerning Salim. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Nurse him. So she said: He is grown. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, smiled and said: Do I not know that he is a man? She said: So she did, then came to him and said: By the One who honored you with what He honored you with, I have not seen in the face of Abu Hudhayfah anything."
"22408","741 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Musafir narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr and Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman informed me, from A'ishah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that Abu Hudhayfah ibn Utbah ibn Rabi'ah ibn Abd Shams, and he was of those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, adopted Salim as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, adopted Zayd ibn Harithah. And whoever adopted a man in the pre-Islamic age, the people attributed him to him, and he inherited from his inheritance, until Allah revealed concerning that: Call them by their fathers; that is more just with Allah; but if you do not know their fathers, then they are your brothers in religion and your freedmen. So they were returned to their fathers, and whoever had no known father was a freedman. A'ishah said: And Sahlah bint Suhayl ibn Amr al-Qurashi, then al-Amiri, was under Abu Hudhayfah ibn Utbah ibn Rabi'ah. She came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when Allah revealed that, and said: O Messenger of Allah, we used to consider Salim a son, and he would stay with me and with Abu Hudhayfah in one house, and see me while I am in light dress, and Allah has revealed concerning them what you have known. So what do you see concerning him, O Messenger of Allah? So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: Nurse him. So she nursed him five nursings, so prohibition is established by them, and he was in the position of her son through nursing."
"22409","What Sahlah bint Suhayl transmitted. 742 - Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Sahlah bint Suhayl ibn Amr, wife of Abu Hudhayfah, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, Salim, freedman of Hudhayfah, enters upon me while he is bearded. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Nurse him. So I said: How shall I nurse him while he is bearded? So he said: Nurse him. So she nursed him, and he would enter upon her."
"22410","743 - Abd al-Malik ibn Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Hubayrah, from Sahlah bint Suhayl, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, does one of us take the ritual bath when she has a wet dream? He said: Yes, if she sees water."
"22411","Sahlah bint Asim ibn Adi al-Ansariyyah. 744 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qatawani narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Ziyad al-Muktib, from Hafs ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, he said: I heard my grandmother Sahlah bint Asim ibn Adi al-Ansariyyah saying: I was born at Hunayn on the day the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, conquered Hunayn, so he named me Sahlah and said: May Allah ease your affair, and he struck a share for me, and married me to Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf on the day I was born."
"22412","Subay'ah bint al-Harith al-Aslamiyyah. What Subay'ah bint al-Harith transmitted. 745 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq and Amr ibn Utbah, that they two wrote to Subay'ah bint al-Harith al-Aslamiyyah asking her about her affair, so she wrote to them that she gave birth twenty-five days after the death of her husband, so she prepared herself for seeking good, then Abu al-Sanabil ibn Ba'kak passed by her and said: You have hastened; observe the waiting period of the later of the two terms, four months and ten days. So I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me. So he said: And what is that? So I informed him of the report. So he said: If you find a righteous husband, then marry."
"22413","746 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Subay'ah bint al-Harith, she said: My husband died with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the Farewell Pilgrimage, and he is Sa'd ibn Khawlah. So I remained after him two months, then I delivered what was in my belly. Then Abu al-Sanabil ibn Ba'kak, brother of Banu Abd al-Dar, passed by; he entered upon my in-laws, and he had wanted me for himself, and I had prepared for marriage and adorned myself. So he said: What is wrong with you, O Subay'ah? I said: I intended marriage. He said: No, by Allah, it is four months and ten days. So I put on my clothes and came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in the house of Umm Salamah, and asked him. So he said: You have become lawful, so marry."
"22414","747 - Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani and Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Sa'igh al-Baghdadi narrated to us, they said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to me, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Abd Allah ibn Ikrimah, from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, from his father, from Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever of you is able to die in Madinah, let him die, for no one dies in it except I shall be for him an intercessor or a witness on the Day of Resurrection."
"22415","748 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, that Ibn Shihab wrote mentioning that Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah ibn Mas'ud informed him, from his father, that he wrote to Ibn al-Arqam to ask Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah: How did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, command her when her husband died? So she said: He gave me fatwa that when I deliver, I may marry."
"22416","749 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah informed me, that his father wrote to Abd Allah ibn al-Arqam al-Zuhri ordering him to enter upon Subay'ah bint al-Harith al-Aslamiyyah and ask her about her hadith and about what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her when she miscarried. So Umar ibn Abd Allah wrote to Abd Allah ibn Utbah informing him that Subay'ah informed him that she was under Sa'd ibn Khawlah, and he was of Banu Amir, and was of those who witnessed Badr; he died leaving her in the Farewell Pilgrimage while she was pregnant, so she delivered her pregnancy after his death. When she recovered from her confinement she adorned herself for suitors. Then Abu al-Sanabil ibn Ba'kak, a man of Banu Abd al-Dar, entered upon her and said to her: Why do I see you adorned? Perhaps you desire marriage; by Allah, you shall not marry until four months and ten days pass upon you. Subay'ah said: When he said that to me, I gathered my clothes upon me until evening, then came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and asked him about that. So he gave me fatwa that I had become lawful on the day I delivered my pregnancy, and commanded me to marry if it seemed good to me."
"22417","750 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, he said: Marwan sent Abd Allah ibn Utbah to Subay'ah bint al-Harith to ask her about what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave her fatwa. So she informed him that she was under Sa'd ibn Khawlah, and he died leaving her in the Farewell Pilgrimage, and he was a Badri. So she delivered her pregnancy before four months and ten days of his death passed for her. Then Abu al-Sanabil ibn Ba'kak met her when she recovered from her confinement, and she had applied kohl. So he said: Perhaps you desire marriage; it is four months and ten days from the death of your husband. She said: So I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned to him what Abu al-Sanabil said. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You have become lawful when you delivered your pregnancy."
"22418","Salma bint Qays Umm al-Mundhir al-Ansariyyah, one of the maternal aunts of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. 751 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub, author of al-Maghazi, narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Sulayt ibn Ayyub narrated to me, from al-Hakam ibn Sulaym, from his mother Salma bint Qays - and she was one of the maternal aunts of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; she had prayed with him toward both prayer directions, and was one of the women of Banu Adi ibn al-Najjar - she said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and pledged allegiance to him among women of the Ansar. When he stipulated upon us that we associate nothing with Allah, and not steal, and not commit adultery, and not kill our children, and not come with slander that we fabricate between our hands and feet, and not disobey him in good, he said: And do not deceive your husbands. She said: So we pledged allegiance to him, then we left. So I said to a woman among them: Return and ask the Messenger of Allah: What of our husbands' wealth has been forbidden to us? So she asked him, and he said: She takes his wealth and exceeds with it to another."
"22419","752 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Sulayt ibn Ayyub narrated to me, from his mother Salma bint Qays, she said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among those women who pledged allegiance to him, and he mentioned the like of it, and al-Hakam ibn Sulaym was not mentioned in the chain."
"22420","753 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Awaqi narrated to us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari informed me, from Ya'qub ibn Abi Ya'qub, from Umm al-Mundhir al-Ansariyyah, and she was one of the maternal aunts of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me, and with him was Ali, and Ali was recovering from an illness, and in the house was a hanging bunch of dates. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ate from it while standing, and Ali was with him. So he said: Do not eat of this, for it does not suit you. So he sat, and I made for him chard and barley. So he said: Eat of this, for it suits you better."
"22421","Salma, wife of Abu Rafi', freedman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; it is said the freedwoman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and it is said the freedwoman of Safiyyah bint Abd al-Muttalib. 754 - Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, they said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Ma'n ibn Isa narrated to us, Fa'id, freedman of Abbad, narrated to us, from his master Ubayd Allah ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi', from his grandmother Salma, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to dislike that food be taken from the top of it."
"22422","755 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawali narrated to us, Fa'id, freedman of Ali ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', narrated to me, from his grandmother Salma, and she was a servant of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when one of us complained of his head, he would say: Go and be cupped; and when he complained of his leg, he would say: Go and dye it with henna."
"22423","756 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Fa'id narrated to us, freedman of Ubayd Allah, from Ubayd Allah ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi', he said: Salma Umm Rafi' narrated to me, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, no sore or thorn would befall him except he would place henna upon it."
"22424","757 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Ubayd Allah ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi', from his grandmother Salma, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A house in which there are no dates, there is no food in it."
"22425","758 - Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Hamzah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Nashit al-Makhzumi al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Harithah ibn Muhammad, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi' informed me, from his mother, and she was a servant of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: A house in which there are no dates, its people are hungry."
"22426","759 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, al-Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Fa'id narrated to us, freedman of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', that his grandmother Salma informed him, she said: I entered upon al-Hasan ibn Ali and Abd Allah ibn Ja'far and Abd Allah ibn Abbas, and they said: Describe for us a food of what the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to like eating. So she said: O my sons, then you would not desire it today. So I stood and took barley and ground it, and winnowed it, and made of it a loaf, and its condiment was oil, and I sprinkled upon it pepper, and brought it near to them, and said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to love this."
"22427","760 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Fa'id narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Ali, that his grandmother Salma informed him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent Abu Rafi' to Banu Umayyah ibn Zayd to kill dogs, and sent another man to kill dogs."
"22428","761 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Fa'id narrated to us, freedman of Ubayd Allah ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi', he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi' narrated to me, that his grandmother Salma, freedwoman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed him, that she made khazirah for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and brought it near, so he ate, and with him were people of his Companions. Then a little of it remained. Then a Bedouin passed by the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called him. So the Bedouin took all of it with his hand. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Put it down. Then he said: Mention Allah, and eat from what is near you, you will be satiated. So he was satiated from it, and a remainder remained."
"22429","762 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Hilal ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Uthmah narrated to us, Musa ibn Ya'qub al-Zam'i narrated to us, from Fa'id, freedman of Ubayd Allah ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi', that his grandmother Salma informed him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded her one day, so she made khazirah for him, and he mentioned similar to it."
"22430","763 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Fa'id narrated to us, freedman of Ubayd Allah ibn Ali, that his grandmother Salma informed him: That the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent to Abu Rafi' for a sheep, and that was on the day of the Trench as I know. So Abu Rafi' roasted it and placed it in a basket, then went forth with it. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, met him returning from the Trench and said to him: O Abu Rafi', hand me the foreleg. So I handed it to him. Then he said: O Abu Rafi', hand me the foreleg. So I handed it to him. Then he said: O Abu Rafi', hand me the foreleg. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, does a sheep have but two forelegs? So he said: Had you been silent, you would have handed me whatever I asked you."
"22431","764 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Rafi'i narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Rafi'i, from his grandmother Salma, that she said: I was with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the markets, and he said: A man of the people of Paradise shall surely appear before you, when I heard a light footstep, and there was Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him."
"22432","765 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, and al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, they said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from A'ishah, she said: Salma, wife of Abu Rafi', came complaining of her husband Abu Rafi'. So she said: O Messenger of Allah, he beats me. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is wrong with you and her? So he said: She harms me. So he said to her: How do you harm him? So she said: O Messenger of Allah, wind came out of him, and he stood to pray, so I said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever has wind come out of him, let him repeat ablution. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, smiled and said: Do not beat her."
"22433","766 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Bukayr ibn Mismar narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam informed me, from Salma Umm Bani Abi Rafi', freedwoman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of words, and do not make many upon me. So he said: Say: Allah is Greatest, ten times; Allah says: This is for Me. And say: Glory be to Allah, ten times; Allah says: This is for Me. And say: O Allah, forgive me; He says: I have done. So you say it ten times, and He says: I have done."
"22434","Salma bint Umays ibn Ma'bad al-Khath'amiyyah, sister of Asma. 767 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Uqbah, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The believing sisters, and he mentioned the hadith."
"22435","Salma bint Nasr al-Muharibiyyah, she is said to have companionship. 768 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Salma bint Nasr al-Muharibiyyah, she said: I asked A'ishah about freeing the child of adultery. So she said: Free him."
"22436","Sumayyah bint Khabbat, freedwoman of Abu Hudhayfah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Makhzum, mother of Ammar ibn Yasir, and she was of those tortured for the sake of Allah, may Allah be pleased with her. 769 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, Asad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Qarm, from al-A'mash, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Zinad, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Uthman ibn Affan, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying to the father of Ammar and the mother of Ammar: Be patient, family of Yasir, your appointment is Paradise."
"22437","al-Sawda bint Asim ibn Khalid ibn Dirar ibn Abd Allah ibn Qurt ibn Razah ibn Adi ibn Ka'b. 770 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Na'ilah narrated to us, from Umm Asim, from al-Sawda, she said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to pledge allegiance to him. So he said: Go and dye with henna, then come until I pledge allegiance to you."
"22438","771 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Azdi narrated to us, Na'ilah narrated to us, from Umm Asim, from al-Sawda, she said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to pledge allegiance to him. So he said: Go and dye with henna, then come until I pledge allegiance to you."
"22439","Su'da al-Murriyyah, wife of Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah. 772 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Harun ibn Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Qannad narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Yahya ibn Talhah, from his mother Su'da al-Murriyyah, she said: Umar passed by Talhah after the death of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was distressed. So he said to him: What is wrong with you; has the leadership of your cousin grieved you? So he said: No, but I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Indeed I know a word none says at his death except it is light in his record, and his body and soul find relief by it at death. But I did not ask him about it until he died. So Umar said: I know it; it is the one he offered to his uncle; had he known anything more saving for him than it, he would have commanded him with it."
"22440","Su'da, another woman not attributed. 773 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn As'ad al-Ammi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Hakim, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah, from his grandmother Su'da or Asma, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib and said to her: O aunt, perform pilgrimage. So she said: I am a heavy woman, and I fear being held back. So he said: Perform pilgrimage and stipulate: My release is where I am held back."
"22441","Sudaysah, freedwoman of Hafsah bint Umar. 774 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Fadl ibn Muwaffaq narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Isra'il, from al-Awza'i, from Sudaysah, freedwoman of Hafsah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Satan has not met Umar since he embraced Islam except he fell upon his face."
"22442","Sirin, sister of Mariyah, concubine of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and she is the mother of Abd al-Rahman ibn Hassan ibn Thabit; al-Muqawqis, king of the Copts, gifted her sister to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he gave her to Hassan ibn Thabit, so she bore him Abd al-Rahman ibn Hassan. 775 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Jabbarah ibn Mughallis narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to me, from al-Mundhir ibn Ubayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hassan ibn Thabit, from his mother Sirin, she said: I attended the death of Ibrahim, son of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and whenever I cried out, and my sister, and the women cried out, he would not forbid us. When he died, he forbade us from crying out, and he carried him to the edge of the grave, with al-Abbas at his side, and al-Fadl ibn Abbas and Usamah ibn Zayd descended into his grave, while I was weeping at his grave. And the sun eclipsed, so the people said: This is for his death. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It does not eclipse for the death of anyone nor for his life. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a gap in the grave and commanded that it be closed. So it was said: O Messenger of Allah, will it benefit him? So he said: It benefits him, and does not harm him, but it harms by the eye of the living. And he died on Tuesday, ten nights past of Rabi' al-Awwal, year ten."
"22443","776 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Zabalah al-Makhzumi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Talhah al-Taymi, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Harithah ibn al-Nu'man, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hassan ibn Thabit, from his mother Sirin, she said: The son of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was attended, so I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and whenever I and my sister cried out, he forbade us from crying out. And al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas washed him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and al-Abbas, and he was placed upon a bier, then carried. Then I saw him sitting at the edge of the grave, at his side al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib. Then al-Fadl ibn Abbas and Usamah ibn Zayd descended into his grave, while I was crying out at the grave, and no one forbade me. And the sun was eclipsed that day. So the people said: For the death of Ibrahim. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is not eclipsed for the death of anyone nor for his life. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a gap in the brickwork and commanded that it be closed. So he said: When the servant does a deed, Allah loves that he perfect it. And he died on Tuesday, four nights past of Rabi' al-Awwal, year ten."
"22444","Sarra bint Nabhan al-Ghanawiyyah. 777 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Rabi'ah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hisn al-Ghanawi narrated to us, he said: Sarra bint Nabhan narrated to me, and she was a mistress of a house in the pre-Islamic age, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying in the Farewell Pilgrimage: Do you know what day this is? She said: And it is the day you call the day of heads. They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: This is the middle of the days of Tashriq. He said: Do you know what land this is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: This is the Sacred Monument. Then he said: I do not know, perhaps I shall not meet you after this. Behold, your blood and your wealth and your honor are inviolable to you, like the inviolability of this day of yours, in this land of yours, until you meet your Lord and He asks you about your deeds. Behold, let your nearest convey to your farthest. Behold, have I conveyed? When he arrived in Madinah, he did not remain but a little until he died."
"22445","778 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yazid ibn Amr ibn al-Bara al-Ghanawi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Harith al-Ghassani narrated to us, he said: Shakiyah bint al-Ja'd narrated to us, from Sarra bint Nabhan al-Ghanawiyyah, she said: The clan dug in the house of Kilab and found an ancient treasure. So Kilab said: Our house. And the clan said: We dug. So they referred that dispute to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he judged it for the clan and took the fifth from them. So we bought with our share of that a hundred of cattle. So we brought them to the clan, then the alms-collector wanted to take alms from us, so we refused him, and came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning that. So he said: If you had combined them with other than them, otherwise there is nothing upon you in this year. And he said: When the alms-collector leaves the people while pleased with them, Allah is pleased with them; and when he leaves while angry with them, Allah is angry with them."
"22446","779 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yazid ibn Amr ibn al-Bara al-Ghanawi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Shakiyah bint al-Ja'd narrated to us, she said: I heard Sarra bint Nabhan al-Ghanawiyyah saying: Nusayb, our slave boy, asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about snakes, which of them to kill. She said: So I heard him saying: Kill what appears of them, its large and its small, its black and its white; for whoever of my community kills it, it is ransom for him from the Fire, and whoever it kills is a martyr."
"22447","Sallamah bint Mi'qal al-Khuza'iyyah. 780 - Abu Shu'ayb Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Khattab ibn Salih, from his mother Sallamah bint Mi'qal, she said: My uncle brought me in the pre-Islamic age and sold me to al-Hubab ibn Amr, so he took me as a concubine, and I bore him Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hubab. And when spring came, they would rest the palms from watering, and send out their water-camels. So he would send me out with his water-camel, and I would sometimes stay two months pasturing it, and sometimes I would prolong upon it until night fell upon it. So I went out one of those years as I used to go out, then he died behind me, leaving debt. When I arrived, his wife said to me: Now, by Allah, you shall be sold, O Sallamah, for the debt. So I said: If Allah has decreed that upon me, I shall seek reward. So I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him of my report. So he said: Who is the keeper of the inheritance of al-Hubab? They said: His brother Abu al-Yasar ibn Amr. So he was called. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Free her; and when you hear of slaves that have come to us, come to me, I shall compensate you from them. So they freed her. Then slaves came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he called Abu al-Yasar and said: Take from these slaves a boy for your nephew. So he went and took a weak, sick boy, and left the strong, powerful ones. So I said: What prevented you from taking of the strong? So he said: I feared them, by Allah, for my nephew. Then he did not remain but died. Ibn Ishaq said: So I narrated this hadith to Rabi'ah ibn Abd al-Rahman, and he said: By Allah, Umar freed them only by this hadith."
"22448","Sallamah bint al-Hurr al-Ju'fiyyah. 781 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Umm Dawud al-Wabishiyyah, from Sallamah bint al-Hurr, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by me in the beginning of Islam while I was grazing, and said: O Salamah, to what do you testify? I said: I testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. So he smiled, laughing."
"22449","782 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Hammad al-Hadrami and Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, they said: Waki' narrated to us, he said: Umm Ghurab narrated to me, from Aqilah, freedwoman of Umm al-Banin, from Sallamah bint al-Hurr, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: In Thaqif is a liar and a destroyer."
"22450","783 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, they said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Umm Ghurab narrated to us, from a woman called Aqilah, from Sallamah bint al-Hurr, sister of Kharashah bint al-Hurr, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: There shall come upon the people a time when they stand an hour, finding no imam to pray for them."
"22451","784 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, they said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, from Talhah, from Umm Ghurab, she said: A freedwoman of Banu Fazarah called Aqilah, or Uqaylah, informed me, from Sallamah bint al-Hurr, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Among the signs of the Hour is that the people of the mosque push one another, finding no one to pray for them."
"22452","Samra bint Nuhayk. 785 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Abu Balj Yahya ibn Abi Sulaym, he said: I saw Samra bint Nuhayk, and she had met the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: upon her was a thick tunic and a thick head-cover, with a whip in her hand, disciplining the people, and enjoining good and forbidding evil."
"22453","Sawdah bint Musarrih. 786 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Tarif al-Bajali narrated to us, and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Dirar ibn Surad narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ali ibn Muyassar, from Umar ibn Umayr, from Urwah ibn Fayruz, from Sawdah bint Musarrih, she said: I was among those who attended Fatimah when labor seized her, with women. She said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came and said: How is she? We said: She is in hard labor. He said: When she delivers, do not precede me in anything concerning him. She said: So she delivered, and I wrapped him in a yellow cloth and put tahnik in his mouth. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came and said: How is she? I said: She has delivered, O Messenger of Allah, and I wrapped him in a cloth and put tahnik in his mouth. She said: So he said: You have disobeyed me. I said: I seek refuge in Allah from disobedience to Allah and disobedience to His Messenger; I put tahnik in his mouth and wrapped him, and found no escape from that. He said: Bring him to me. So he removed the yellow cloth from him, and wrapped him in a white cloth, and spat in his mouth, and fed him with his saliva. Then Ali came, and he said: What have you named him, O Ali? He said: I named him Ja'far, O Messenger of Allah. He said: No, but he is Hasan, and after him Husayn, and you are Abu Hasan al-Khayr."
"22454","Chapter of Shin. Shifa bint Abd Allah ibn Hashim ibn Khalaf ibn Abd Shams, Umm Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah. 787 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Tahir ibn Abi Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Khalid ibn Ilyas narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from al-Shifa bint Abd Allah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sought rain on Friday in the mosque and raised his hands, and said: Seek forgiveness of your Lord; indeed He is Forgiving. And he turned."
"22455","788 - ... his cloak. Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-Attar al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Ilyas, from Abu Bakr ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from al-Shifa Umm Sulayman, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, employed Abu Jahm ibn Hudhayfah over the spoils, so a man struck another with his bow and wounded him with a displacing wound. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged in it fifteen camels."
"22456","789 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from al-Shifa bint Abd Allah, she said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one day asking him, and he began excusing himself to me while I was blaming him. Then noon came, so I went out until I entered upon my daughter, and she is under Shurahbil ibn Hasanah. So I found Shurahbil in the house, and I began blaming him. So he said: O girl, do not blame me, for there was a garment of mine the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, borrowed. So I said: By my father and mother, I was blaming him since today, and this is his state, while I did not know."
"22457","790 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to me, from Abu Bakr ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, that al-Shifa bint Abd Allah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me while I was sitting with Hafsah bint Umar, and said: Why do you not teach her the ruqyah of the namlah as you taught her writing."
"22458","791 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus and Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Maqabiri narrated to us, they said: Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to me, from Uthman ibn Abi Hathmah, from his grandmother al-Shifa, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while a man asked him: Which deeds are best? He said: Faith in Allah, and striving in the cause of Allah, and an accepted pilgrimage."
"22459","792 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Humayd narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman, from his father's grandmother, she said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I desire striving in the cause of Allah. So he said: Shall I not guide you to a striving in which there is no thorn? I said: Yes. He said: Pilgrimage to the House."
"22460","793 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, they said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, he said: Such-and-such al-Qurashi narrated to me, from his grandmother, that she heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The best of deeds are faith in Allah, and striving in the cause of Allah, and an accepted pilgrimage."
"22461","794 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Shababab ibn Sawwar narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from a man of the family of Abi Hathmah, from al-Shifa, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked: Which deeds are best? So he said: Faith in Allah, and striving in the cause of Allah, and an accepted pilgrimage."
"22462","795 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from al-Shifa bint Abd Allah, she said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asking him, and he began excusing himself to me, while I was blaming him. Then the prayer came, so I went out and entered upon my daughter, and she is under Shurahbil ibn Hasanah. So I found Shurahbil in the house, and I said: The prayer has come and you are in the house, and I began blaming him. So he said: O aunt, do not blame me, for there was a garment of ours the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, borrowed. So I said: By my father and mother, I was blaming him since today, and this is his state, while I did not know. So Shurahbil said: It was only a tunic we had raised."
"22463","796 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Jarrah ibn al-Dahhak, from Kurayb al-Kindi, he said: Ali ibn al-Husayn took my hand, and we went to an old man of Quraysh called Ibn Abi Hathmah, praying toward a pillar. So we sat with him, and when he finished, Ali said to him: Narrate to us the hadith of your mother concerning ruqyah. So he said: My mother narrated to me that she used to perform ruqyah with a ruqyah of hers in the pre-Islamic age. When Islam came, she said: I shall not perform ruqyah with it until I seek permission of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So I came to him and sought his command. So he said: Perform ruqyah with what contains no polytheism."
"22464","797 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abu Bakr ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from Hafsah, she said: I entered upon a woman called al-Shifa,"
"22465","And Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Harun ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abu Bakr ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from Hafsah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon her, and with her was a woman called al-Shifa who performs ruqyah for the namlah. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: Teach it to Hafsah."
"22466","798 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abu Bakr ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to his grandmother al-Shifa: Teach Hafsah your ruqyah."
"22467","799 - Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn Ahmad al-Waki'i narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abd al-Karim, from Sulayman ibn Abi al-Tayyib, from Umm Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, she said: We saw women of the elderly who sit at home praying the obligatory prayers with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"22468","800 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Humayd ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abd al-Karim ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Tayyib, from Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from his mother, she said: We saw the elderly women praying with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the mosque."
"22469","Shamus bint al-Nu'man ibn Amir ibn Mujammi' al-Ansariyyah. 801 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, they said: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us, Asim ibn Suwayd ibn Amir al-Ansari narrated to us, from Utbah ibn Rabi'ah, from al-Shamus bint al-Nu'man, she said: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, laying the foundation of the mosque of Quba, and I would sometimes see him carrying the huge stone, pressing it to his belly. So we would come to take it from him, and he would say: Leave it, and carry another. And Jibril, peace be upon him, was directing it toward the Ka'bah."
"22470","802 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Shababab ibn Sawwar narrated to us, Asim ibn Suwayd ibn Amir ibn Yazid ibn Jariyah narrated to us, my father Suwayd ibn Amir narrated to me, from al-Shamus bint al-Nu'man, she said: I looked at the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he arrived and alighted and founded this mosque, the mosque of Quba. So I saw him taking the stone - or the rock - until the stone scorched him, and I would look at the whiteness of dust upon his belly and navel. Then a man of his Companions would come and say: By my father and mother, O Messenger of Allah, give me, I shall suffice you. So he would say: No, take a stone like it. Until he founded it, and he would say: Jibril, peace be upon him, is directing it to the Ka'bah. She said: So it was said: It is the straightest mosque in prayer direction."
"22471","Sharaf bint Khalifah ibn Farwah al-Kalbiyyah, sister of Dihyah ibn Khalifah; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married her and did not consummate with her. 803 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Fadl ibn Muwaffaq narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Jabir, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, proposed to a woman of Kalb, and sent A'ishah to look at her."
"22472","Chapter of Sad. Safiyyah bint Abd al-Muttalib, of her reports. 804 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered the women on the day of the Confederates into a fortress of the fortresses of Madinah. And Hassan ibn Thabit was a cowardly man, so he entered him with the women and locked the door. Then a Jew came and sat at the door of the fortress. So Safiyyah bint Abd al-Muttalib said: Come down, O Hassan, to this infidel and kill him. So he said: I would not risk myself for this infidel. So I wrapped myself in a cloak and took a staff, and went down to him and cut off his head."
"22473","805 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Safiyyah bint Abd al-Muttalib would not cover her head from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, nor from ten of the first Emigrants: Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, her brother; and Ja'far and Ali, sons of Abu Talib, sons of her brother; and al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, her son; and Uthman ibn Affan, son of her sister's daughter - his mother Arwa bint Kurayz, and her mother al-Bayda Umm Hakim bint Abd al-Muttalib; and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Asad; and Abu Sabrah ibn Abi Ruhm, sons of her sister Barrah bint Abd al-Muttalib; and the mother of Tulayb ibn Umayr ibn Wahb ibn Abd Qusayy: Arwa bint Abd al-Muttalib; and the mother of Abd Allah and Abu Ahmad the blind poet, whose name is Abd ibn Jahsh ibn Ri'ab ibn Ya'mar ibn Hubayrah ibn Murrah ibn Ghanm ibn Duddan ibn Asad ibn Khuzaymah: Umaymah bint Abd al-Muttalib. And Safiyyah died in the caliphate of Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"22474","806 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, he said: Safiyyah bint Abd al-Muttalib said, elegizing the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: ... [two garbled poetic fragments] ..."
"22475","807 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, he said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed away, Safiyyah came out trailing her cloak, saying: ... [garbled fragment] ..."
"22476","What Safiyyah narrated. 808 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us: Ishaq al-Hashimi narrated to us, from Safiyyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to me, and I served him a shoulder (of meat) which I had set aside for him; he ate it, then he rose to pray."
"22477","809 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated to us: Umm Urwah bint Jafar ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from her father, from his grandmother Safiyyah bint Abd al-Muttalib: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out for Uhud, he placed his womenfolk in a fortress called Fari', and he placed Hassan ibn Thabit with them. Hassan would keep watch toward the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): when he charged the polytheists he would shout along with him from the fortress, and when he pulled back he pulled back behind him. She said: Some Jews came, and one of them climbed the fortress until he looked down upon us from the fortress, so I said to Hassan: Get up to him and kill him. He said: That is not in me; had it been in me, I would have been with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Safiyyah struck his head until she severed it, and when she had severed it she said: O Hassan, get up to his head and throw it down to them, while they were at the foot of the fortress. He said: By Allah, that is not in me. She said: So I took his head and threw it at them, and they said: By Allah, we knew that Muhammad had not left his family behind unprotected with no one among them; and they scattered and left. She said: And Sa'd ibn Mu'adh passed by with a trace of yellow dye on him, as though he had been a bridegroom shortly before, saying: [the remainder is missing in the source]."
"22478","Safiyyah bint Shaybah ibn Uthman al-Hajabiyyah. 810 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Bashir narrated to us, (ha) and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, both of them from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Thawr, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, she said: When the people settled down on the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated on a camel, touching the Stone with a curved stick in his hand; then he entered the Ka'bah while I was watching, and he saw a bundle of sticks, so he stood and broke them, then threw them out, while I was watching."
"22479","811 - Jafar ibn al-Fadl al-Mukharrimi al-Mu'addib narrated to us: Dawud ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Kiram al-Jafari narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from his mother, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wet a garment while he was in the Ka'bah, then he began striking the images that were in it."
"22480","812 - Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Thawr, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated in the year of the conquest, when he entered Makkah, on his mount around the House, touching the Corner with his curved stick."
"22481","813 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ali ibn Hakam al-Awdi narrated to us: Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from al-Mughirah ibn Hakim, from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform the sa'y, for the sa'y has been prescribed for you."
"22482","814 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Maymun ibn Mihran, he said: I came to Safiyyah bint Shaybah, an elderly woman, and I said to her: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marry while he was in ihram? She said: No; he married her while they were both non-muhrims."
"22483","Safiyyah bint Umar ibn al-Khattab. 815 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Sahl al-Hannat narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: Safiyyah bint Umar ibn al-Khattab was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Khaybar."
"22484","Al-Samma', sister of Busr, al-Maziniyyah. 816 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati and Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, both said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Ibn Abd Allah ibn Busr, from his father, from his paternal aunt al-Samma', sister of Busr, that she used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting on Saturday, and said: If none of you finds anything but a green stick, let him break his fast on it."
"22485","817 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Ibn Abd Allah ibn Busr, from his father, from his paternal aunt al-Samma', that she used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting on Saturday."
"22486","818 - Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Misri al-Ayli narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, (ha) and Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us: my father narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, from his sister al-Samma', that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not fast on Saturday except for what has been made obligatory upon you; if none of you finds anything but the bark of a tree, let him chew it."
"22487","819 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb narrated to us: my uncle Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us: Qurrah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, from his sister al-Samma', she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not fast on Saturday except for the fasting that has been made obligatory upon you; whoever finds nothing but bark or a grapevine cutting, let him chew it."
"22488","820 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qatawani and Muhammad ibn al-Wazir al-Wasiti narrated to us, both said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Asbagh ibn Zayd informed us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, from his sister al-Samma', that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not fast on Saturday except for what has been made obligatory upon you; if none of you finds anything but a stick or the bark of a tree, let him chew it."
"22489","821 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, (ha) al-Hadrami said: and al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Habib narrated to us, both said: Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, from his sister al-Samma', from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"22490","822 - Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, from Fudayl ibn Fadalah, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, from his maternal aunt, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not fast on Saturday except for what Allah has made obligatory upon you."
"22491","Sumaytah al-Laythiyyah. 823 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Sumaytah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is able to die in Madinah, let him die there; whoever dies in Madinah, I shall be for him a witness or an intercessor. Thus Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated it, but he was contradicted in its chain."
"22492","824 - Harun ibn Kamil al-Misri narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to me: Yunus narrated to me, (ha) and Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us: Anbasah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Sumaytah, a woman of Banu Layth ibn Bakr who was under the care of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: I heard her narrating to Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever among you is able to die in Madinah, let him die there, for he dies a martyr and intercession is made for him."
"22493","825 - Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from an orphaned woman who was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever is able to die in Madinah, let him die there; whoever dies in Madinah, I shall be for him a witness or an intercessor on the Day of Resurrection."
"22494","826 - Sulayman ibn al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd, from al-Dariyyah, a woman of Banu Abd al-Dar who was under the care of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is able to die in Madinah, let him die there; whoever dies in it, I shall be for him a witness or an intercessor on the Day of Resurrection."
"22495","Chapter of Dad. Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib; some of her reports. 827 - Abu Aqil Anas ibn Salim al-Khawlani narrated to us: Abu al-Asbagh Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Harrani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Aban ibn Salih, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Duba'ah: Perform Hajj, and stipulate that my place of release is wherever You detain me."
"22496","828 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I wish to perform Hajj; should I stipulate? He said: Yes. She said: What should I say? He said: Say: At Your service, O Allah, at Your service; my place of release on the earth is wherever You detain me."
"22497","829 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Duba'ah: Perform Hajj and stipulate that my place of release is wherever You detain me."
"22498","830 - Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah al-Baghdadi narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Yahya al-Umawi narrated to us: Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah al-Ashhali, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Duba'ah: Perform Hajj and stipulate; say: O Allah, my place of release is wherever You detain me."
"22499","831 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Khallad al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Amr ibn Makhlad al-Laythi narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us: Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Duba'ah: Stipulate that my place of release is wherever You detain me."
"22500","832 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us: Khalid ibn Makhlad al-Qatawani narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Duba'ah: Perform Hajj and stipulate; say: O Allah, my place of release is wherever You detain me."
"22501","833 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from A'ishah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib while she was ill, and she said: I wish to perform Hajj, but I am ill. He said: Perform Hajj and stipulate; say: O Allah, my place of release is wherever You detain me."
"22502","834 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib: Do you wish to perform Hajj? She said: I am sick. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Perform Hajj and stipulate, and say: O Allah, my place of release is wherever You detain me."
"22503","835 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us: Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib, who was married to al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, a companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said to her: Perhaps you intend Hajj? She said: By Allah, I find myself nothing but aching. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Perform Hajj and stipulate; say: O Allah, my place of release is wherever You detain me."
"22504","836 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Duba'ah: Perform Hajj and stipulate that my place of release is wherever You detain me."
"22505","What Duba'ah narrated. 837 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Umar ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Abd al-Karim: one who heard Ibn Abbas narrated to me, he says: Duba'ah narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded her to stipulate in her ihram."
"22506","838 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Khalaf ibn Musa ibn Khalaf al-Ammi narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah al-Hashimi, from Umm Atiyyah, from her sister Duba'ah: She saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat a shoulder, then he rose to prayer and did not perform ablution."
"22507","839 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from his grandmother Umm Hakim, from her sister Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr: She served meat to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he tore off a bite from it, then he prayed and did not perform ablution."
"22508","840 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Zaynab bint Nubayt, from Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Perform Hajj and stipulate."
"22509","841 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Isa ibn Salim al-Shashi narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim ibn Malik al-Jazari, from the freedman of Duba'ah, from Duba'ah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded her to enter ihram, and she said: I am sick. He said to her: Stipulate that my place of release is wherever You detain me. When Ibn Abbas heard this hadith, he said: Praise be to Allah that I used to do it, though I had heard nothing about it."
"22510","842 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr, she said: I visited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was complaining (of illness), and I mentioned Hajj to him, so he said: Perform Hajj and stipulate: O Allah, my place of release is wherever You detain me."
"22511","843 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fudayl and Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to me while I was ill, and said: Do you not intend Hajj this year? She said: I am ailing, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Perform Hajj, and say: My place of release is wherever You detain me."
"22512","844 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us: Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Fadl ibn al-Mufaddal, from Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib: She had a sheep in her house, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to her: Feed us from your sheep. She said to the messenger: Nothing remains with us but the neck, and I am too shy to send it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The messenger returned to him and informed him, so he said: Go back to her and say to her: Send it, for it is the guide of the sheep, the closest part of the sheep to good and the farthest from harm."
"22513","Chapter of Ayn. Amrah bint Rawahah al-Ansariyyah, sister of Abd Allah ibn Rawahah, mother of al-Nu'man ibn Bashir. 845 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Hushaym narrated to us: Sayyar, Mughirah, Dawud ibn Abi Hind, Ismail ibn Salim, and Mujalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, he said: My father granted me a gift - Ismail said: he granted him a slave boy - so my mother Amrah bint Rawahah said to him: Go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and take him as witness. So he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: I have granted my son al-Nu'man a gift, and Amrah asked me to take you as witness to that. He said: Do you have other children besides him? I said: Yes. He said: Have you given each of them the like of what you gave al-Nu'man? He said: No. One of these narrators said: This is injustice; another of them said: This is a one-sided grant; take someone other than me as witness to this. Mughirah said: Does it not please you that they be equal to you in dutifulness and kindness? He said: Yes. He said: Then take someone other than me as witness to this. And Mujalid mentioned in his hadith: They have a right upon you to be just among them, just as you have a right upon them to be dutiful to you."
"22514","846 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, he said: I heard Talhah al-Yami narrating, from a woman of Abd al-Qays, from the sister of Abd Allah ibn Rawahah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Going out (for jihad) is obligatory upon everyone who wears a waist-wrapper."
"22515","847 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, from Talhah, from a woman of Abd al-Qays, from the sister of Abd Allah ibn Rawahah, Amrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Going out is obligatory upon everyone who wears a waist-wrapper."
"22516","Amrah bint Hizam al-Ansariyyah. 848 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us: Amr ibn al-Rabi' ibn Tariq narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Bunani, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, from Amrah bint Hizam: She prepared for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a spot among date-palms, which she swept and perfumed, and she slaughtered a sheep for him, and he ate from it; then he performed ablution and prayed Zuhr, and she served him some of its meat, and he ate, then prayed Asr without performing ablution."
"22517","Amrah bint Sahl, wife of Sahib al-Sa'ayn. 849 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Janab al-Massisi narrated to us, (ha) and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us: Amr ibn Zurarah al-Hadathi narrated to us, both said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Uthman al-Balawi narrated to us, from his grandmother, that her mother Amrah bint Sahl ibn Rafi', wife of Sahib al-Sa'ayn whom the hypocrites mocked, narrated to him: Her father went out with his zakat, two sa's of dates, along with his daughter Amrah, until he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he poured out the two sa's, then said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a request to you. He said: What is it? He said: That you supplicate for blessing for me and for her, and wipe her head, for I have no child but her. She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand upon me. She said: And I swear by Allah, the coolness of the palm of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is upon my chest even now."
"22518","Amrah bint al-Harith ibn Abi Dirar al-Khuza'iyyah. 850 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Salamah, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Abi Dirar, from his paternal aunt Amrah bint al-Harith, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This world is sweet and green; whoever takes it rightfully, Allah blesses it for him, and many a one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger shall have the Fire on the Day of Resurrection, the day he meets Him."
"22519","851 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, both said: al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, (ha) and Sahl ibn Musa Shiran al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Salamah al-Makhzumi narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Amrah bint al-Harith ibn Abi Dirar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: This world is sweet and green; whoever obtains something from its lawful portion, that is what is blessed for him in it, and how many a one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger shall have the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"22520","Umayrah bint Mas'ud. 852 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Raja' ibn Muhammad al-Saqati narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Idris narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ja'far ibn Mahmud ibn Maslamah al-Ansari narrated to us: my father narrated to me, that his grandmother Umayrah bint Mas'ud informed him: She entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she and her sisters, to pledge allegiance to him, five of them; they found him eating dried meat, so he chewed a piece of dried meat for them, then handed me the piece, and each one of them chewed a bit of it; they met Allah without ever finding foul breath in their mouths."
"22521","Azzah bint Khabil al-Khuza'iyyah. 853 - Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-Attar narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us: Abbas ibn Abi Shamlah narrated to us, (ha) and Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, (ha) and Ibrahim ibn Duhaym narrated to us: my father narrated to us, both said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, both said: Musa ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, from Ata' ibn Mas'ud al-Ka'bi, from his father, that his paternal aunt Azzah bint Khabil informed him: She came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and pledged allegiance to him, and he took upon her: That you commit no adultery, steal not, and commit no infanticide, whether openly or secretly. I said: As for open infanticide, I have understood it; as for secret infanticide, I have not understood it, O Messenger of Allah, but it has occurred to me that it is spoiling the child, so I shall never spoil a child ever. He said: And she never spoiled a child of hers until she died; the wording is that of the hadith of Ibn Abi Fudayk."
"22522","Aqilah bint Ubayd ibn al-Harith. 854 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, (ha) and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh narrated to us: Hafs ibn Umar al-Juddi narrated to us: Bakkar ibn Abd Allah, nephew of Musa ibn Ubaydah al-Rabadhi, narrated to us: Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to me: Zayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me - and Ali ibn al-Madini said: Zayd ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah - from his mother Hajjah bint Qurayz, from her mother Aqilah bint Ubayd ibn al-Harith, she said: I came with my mother Barirah bint al-Harith al-Utwarriyyah, among some Muhajir women, and we pledged allegiance to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he had pitched a tent at al-Abtah; he took upon us that we associate nothing with Allah, the verse; when we affirmed and stretched out our hands to pledge to him, he said: I do not touch the hands of women; and he sought forgiveness for us, and that was our pledge."
"22523","A'ishah bint Qudamah ibn Maz'un al-Jumahiyyah. 855 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Sulayman, meaning al-Wasiti, narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Hatib narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from his mother A'ishah bint Qudamah ibn Maz'un: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissed Uthman ibn Maz'un on the cheek after he died, and it is not known that he kissed anyone else."
"22524","856 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (ha) and Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, (ha) and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, all said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman al-Hatibi narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from his mother A'ishah bint Qudamah ibn Maz'un, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is grievous to Allah to take the two precious things of a Muslim and then admit him to the Fire - meaning his two eyes."
"22525","857 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman al-Hatibi narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from A'ishah bint Qudamah ibn Maz'un, she said: I was with my mother Ra'itah bint Sufyan, a woman of Khuza'ah, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taking their pledge, saying: I take your pledge that you associate nothing with Allah, steal not, commit no adultery, kill not your children, bring no slander that you fabricate between your hands and feet, and disobey me not in what is right. She said: So they bowed their heads, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say: Yes, in what we are able. So they said: Yes, in what we are able; I would say as they said, and my mother would say: Say yes, so I would say yes."
"22526","858 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Ahmad ibn al-Nu'man al-Farra' al-Massisi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman al-Hatibi narrated to us, from his father, from his mother A'ishah bint Qudamah ibn Maz'un, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of the two blind ones. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the two blind ones? He said: The flood and the aggressive camel."
"22527","Atikah bint Abd al-Muttalib, paternal aunt of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 859 - Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-Attar narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his mother Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt, from Atikah bint Abd al-Muttalib, she said: I saw a rider appear upon Abu Qubays crying out: O family of Ghudar, O family of Fujar, march forth for three! Then he took a rock from Abu Qubays and hurled it at the grinding-stone, and the rock split apart, and no house of Quraysh remained but a fragment of it entered it, except the houses of Banu Zahrah. Al-Abbas said: This is a dream; conceal it and mention it not. Al-Abbas went and met al-Walid ibn Utbah ibn Rabi'ah and mentioned it to him, and al-Walid mentioned it to his father, and the story spread. Al-Abbas said: In the morning I went to circumambulate the Ka'bah while Abu Jahl was with a group of Quraysh discussing the dream of Atikah; when Abu Jahl saw me he said: O Abu al-Fadl, when you finish your circumambulation come to us. When I finished I came until I sat with them, and Abu Jahl said: O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, were you not content that your men should prophesy until your women prophesy too? Atikah has claimed in this dream of hers that he said: March forth for three; we shall wait these three, and if what she says is true it will happen, and if the three pass with nothing of that, we shall write a document against you that you are the most lying household among the Arabs. Al-Abbas said: By Allah, I answered him with nothing but that I denied it and denied that she had seen anything. Al-Abbas said: In the evening a woman of the daughters of Abd al-Muttalib came to me and said: Were you content that this transgressor should attack your men and then attack your women while you listen, with no rebuke from you? By Allah, had Hamzah been present he would not have said what he said. I said: By Allah he did so, and I offered him no rebuke; by Allah, I shall waylay him, and if he repeats it I shall suffice you against him. Al-Abbas said: In the morning of the third day after the dream of Atikah I set out angry, hoping to catch something of the matter, and by Allah as I was walking toward him - he was a light, sharp-faced, sharp-tongued, sharp-sighted man - he rushed out toward the door of the mosque hurrying, and I said to myself: What is with him, may Allah curse him; is all this fear of me that he would revile me? Then he had heard what I had not heard: he heard the voice of Damdam ibn Zur'ah ibn Amr al-Ghifari crying out in the valley-bottom, having hamstrung his camel, turned his saddle over, and torn his shirt, saying: O assembly of Quraysh, Muhammad has set out with his companions; I do not think you will overtake them - help, help! Al-Abbas said: What came of the matter distracted me from him and distracted him from me."
"22528","860 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abi al-Aswad, from Urwah, he said: Atikah bint Abd al-Muttalib, paternal aunt of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), was living with her brother al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, and she saw a dream shortly before Badr and was frightened; she sent for her brother Abbas in that night when she was frightened and awoke from her sleep, and said: I have seen a dream, and I have feared destruction for your people because of it. He said: What did you see? She said: I shall not tell you until you pledge to me that you shall not mention it, for if they hear it they will harm us and make us hear what we dislike. Abbas pledged to her, and she said: I saw a rider approach on his mount from the heights of Makkah, shouting at the top of his voice: O family of Ghudar, O family of Fujar, go forth in two or three nights! Then he entered the mosque on his mount and shrieked three shrieks in the mosque, and men, women, and children gathered to him, and the people were seized with the utmost fright. Then I saw him upon the back of the Ka'bah on his mount, shouting three shouts: O family of Ghudar, O family of Fujar, go forth in two or three nights, until all the people of Makkah between the two mountains heard. Then he set upon a huge rock, tore it from its base, and hurled it upon the people of Makkah; the rock came on with a rumble, and when it reached the foot of the mountain it shattered, and I know of no house or dwelling in Makkah but a splinter of that rock entered it; I have feared that evil would befall your people. Abbas was frightened by it and left her, and late that night he met al-Walid ibn Utbah ibn Rabi'ah, who was a close friend of al-Abbas, and told him the dream of Atikah, bidding him mention it to no one; al-Walid mentioned it to his father, Utbah mentioned it to his brother Shaybah, and her story rose until it reached Abu Jahl ibn Hisham and became widespread. In the morning Abbas went to circumambulate the House, and found Abu Jahl, Utbah ibn Rabi'ah, Shaybah ibn Rabi'ah, Umayyah ibn Khalaf, Zam'ah ibn al-Aswad, and Abu al-Bakhtari among a group talking; when they saw Abbas circumambulating the House, Abu Jahl called to him: O Abu al-Fadl, when you finish your circumambulation come to us. When he finished his circumambulation he came and sat, and Abu Jahl said: O Abu al-Fadl, what dream did Atikah see? He said: She saw nothing. He said: Nay; were you not content, O Banu Hashim, with the lying of men until you have brought us the lying of women? We and you were like two racing horses vying for glory for a long time; when the riders drew level you said: From us is a prophet, and nothing remains but that you say: From us is a prophetess. I know of no household in Quraysh more lying, man or woman, than you. They harmed him that day with severe harm, and Abu Jahl said: Atikah claimed that the rider said: Go forth in two or three nights; when these three pass, the lying of you to Quraysh will become clear, and we shall write a document and hang it upon the Ka'bah that you are the most lying household among the Arabs, man and woman. Were you not content, O Banu Qusayy, that you took the veiling, the council, the watering, the supply of water and the feeding, until you have come to us claiming a prophet among you? They harmed him that day with severe harm, and Abbas said to him: Gently, O yellow-rumped one; will you not desist? Lying is in you and your household. Those present said to him: O Abu al-Fadl, you were never ignorant nor senile. Abbas met with severe hurt from Atikah for divulging her story. On the evening of the third night of the nights in which Atikah saw the dream, there came to them the rider whom Abu Sufyan had sent, Damdam ibn Amr al-Ghifari, saying: O family of Ghalib, march forth, for Muhammad and his companions have set out to intercept Abu Sufyan, so protect your caravan. Quraysh were seized with the utmost fright, feared the dream of Atikah, and marched forth upon every hardy and tractable mount."
"22529","861 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar narrated to us: Mus'ab ibn Abd Allah and others of Quraysh narrated to me: Atikah bint Abd al-Muttalib spoke of the truth of her dream and the denial of Quraysh to her when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smote them at Badr: [fragmentary verse]."
"22530","Atikah bint Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl. 862 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Ubayd Allah ibn al-Walid al-Rusafi narrated to me, from his father, from one who narrated to him, he said: A'ishah said: Atikah bint Zayd was married to Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq."
"22531","Umm Ma'bad al-Khuza'iyyah, whose name is Atikah bint Khulayf - also said Atikah bint Khalid ibn Munqidh ibn Khunays al-Ka'biyyah al-Khuza'iyyah. 863 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Hizam ibn Hisham, from his father, from Umm Ma'bad: She sent a household sheep to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he returned it, saying: Send a sheep that gives no milk."
"22532","864 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Hizam ibn Hisham, from his father, from Umm Ma'bad: A clothing allowance used to run for her, along with something of the produce of Yemen and tar for her camels; Uthman passed by her and she said: Where is my clothing and where is the produce of Yemen that used to come to me? He said: It is yours, O Umm Ma'bad, kept by her; and he followed her until he gave it to her."
"22533","Azzah al-Ashja'iyyah, she has companionship. 865 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Mansur and Husayn, or one of them, from Abi Hazim, from a freedwoman of his called Azzah, she said: Abu Bakr addressed us and forbade us - or forbade - praying upon saddlecloths."
"22534","866 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us: Qabisah narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abi Hazim, from a freedwoman of his called Azzah, who was among the first women, she said: Abu Bakr addressed us and said: Do not pray upon saddlecloths."
"22535","Al-Ajma' al-Ansariyyah. 867 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-Utbi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Marwan ibn Uthman, from Abi Uthman, from Abi Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his maternal aunt al-Ajma', she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The old man and the old woman, when they commit adultery, stone them outright, for what they have enjoyed of pleasure."
"22536","Chapter of Ghayn. Al-Ghumayda'. 869 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Hisham: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Ghumayda': Not until he tastes of your little honey and you taste of his little honey."
"22537","Ghaziyyah bint Jabir ibn Hakim al-Dawsiyyah, Umm Sharik. 870 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ali ibn Husayn, concerning His saying: And a believing woman if she offers herself to the Prophet: That Umm Sharik al-Azdiyyah is the one who offered herself to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"22538","Chapter of Fa'. Fatimah bint Asad ibn Hashim, mother of Ali ibn Abi Talib. 871 - Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah narrated to us: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When Fatimah bint Asad ibn Hashim, mother of Ali ibn Abi Talib, died, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to her and sat at her head and said: May Allah have mercy on you, O my mother; you were my mother after my mother; you fed me to satiety while you went hungry, clothed me while you went bare, denied yourself good food and fed me, seeking thereby the Face of Allah and the Hereafter. Then he ordered that she be washed three times; when the water containing camphor was reached, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured it with his hand. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took off his shirt and dressed her in it, and shrouded her with a cloak over it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Usamah ibn Zayd, Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, Umar ibn al-Khattab, and a black boy to dig; they dug her grave, and when they reached the niche, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dug it with his hand and removed its soil with his hand. When he finished, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and lay down in it, then said: O Allah who gives life and causes death, and He is the Living who dies not: forgive my mother Fatimah bint Asad, prompt her with her proof, widen her entrance for her, by the right of Your Prophet and the prophets before me, for You are the Most Merciful of the merciful. He pronounced four takbirs over her, and they lowered her into the niche: he, al-Abbas, and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with them."
"22539","872 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin and Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh, both Egyptians, narrated to us, both said: Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us: Hisham ibn Ali narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abi al-Bakhtari, from Ali, he said: Fatimah bint Muhammad would suffice him the indoor work, and Fatimah bint Asad would suffice him the outdoor work - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"22540","873 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: my father narrated to us, (ha) and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abi al-Bakhtari, from Ali, he said: I said to my mother Fatimah bint Asad ibn Hashim: Suffice Fatimah bint the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the drawing of water and going out for needs, and she will suffice you the indoor service: grinding and kneading."
"22541","Fatimah bint Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, kunya Umm al-Fadl - also said her name is Umamah, also said Umarah. 874 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, from the daughter of Hamzah, she said: A freedman of mine died leaving his daughter, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided his wealth between me and his daughter, giving me half and her half."
"22542","875 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Hakam, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Umm al-Fadl bint Hamzah - and Umm al-Fadl was the maternal sister of Abd Allah ibn Shaddad - she said: A mukatab of ours died whom she had freed, leaving his daughter; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided his inheritance, giving his daughter half and giving Umm al-Fadl the remaining half."
"22543","876 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Awn informed us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, son of the daughter of Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib: She freed a slave of hers, and he died leaving his daughter and his patroness, the daughter of Hamzah; his daughter inherited half, and the daughter of Hamzah half."
"22544","878 - Sahl ibn Musa Shiran al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la al-San'ani narrated to us: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, (ha) and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i al-Qadi narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'arah narrated to us: Azhar ibn Sa'd narrated to us, both from Ibn Awn, from al-Hakam, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad: The daughter of Hamzah freed a boy, and he died leaving a daughter, so he divided between them."
"22545","879 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad: The daughter of Hamzah - her freedman died leaving his daughter - and the daughter of Hamzah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided the wealth between them in halves."
"22546","880 - Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Harb al-Abbadani narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad: The daughter of Hamzah freed a boy, and he died leaving a daughter of his; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the daughter of Hamzah half, and his daughter half."
"22547","881 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us: Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us: Za'idah narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, he said: The daughter of Hamzah freed a boy, and he died leaving a daughter; the daughter of Hamzah took half, and his daughter half, in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"22548","882 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, (ha) and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: my uncle Abu Bakr narrated to us, both said: Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, that he said: Do you know what the daughter of Hamzah is to me? She is my maternal sister; she freed a man, and he died, so his inheritance was divided between her and her. I said: In the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: In the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"22549","883 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad: A daughter of Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib freed a boy of hers, and he died in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), leaving a daughter of his; so they split the wealth between them in halves."
"22550","884 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Ayyash al-Amiri, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, he said: The daughter of Hamzah freed a boy of hers in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he died leaving a daughter, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the daughter of Hamzah half, and gave his daughter half."
"22551","885 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: my uncle Abu Bakr narrated to us: Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur ibn Habban, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad: A freedman of the daughter of Hamzah died leaving his daughter, and the daughter of Hamzah; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave his daughter half, and the daughter of Hamzah half."
"22552","886 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, he said: I came upon Abd Allah ibn Shaddad while he was narrating to the people, and I heard him say at the end of the hadith: my sister. I asked the people, and his companions narrated to me that he had narrated to them: A daughter of Hamzah - she being a maternal sister of Abd Allah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had - her freedman died leaving his daughter and the daughter of Hamzah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided the wealth in halves."
"22553","887 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us: Imran ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abi Fakhita, from Ja'dah ibn Hubayrah, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gifted me a robe striped with silk, and said to me: Make it into veils among the Fatimahs. So I cut from it three veils: a veil for Fatimah bint Asad, a veil for Fatimah bint Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a veil for Fatimah bint Hamzah."
"22554","Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh ibn al-Muttalib ibn Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza al-Asadiyyah. 888 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri and Ibn Jurayj, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, she said: Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who suffers non-menstrual bleeding and never becomes pure; shall I leave prayer? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is only a vein, not menstruation; when menstruation comes, leave prayer, and when it departs, wash the blood from yourself, then pray."
"22555","889 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us: al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah: Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh would suffer non-menstrual bleeding, so she asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: It is only a vein, not menstruation; when menstruation comes, leave prayer, and when it departs, wash and pray."
"22556","890 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both said: al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, (ha) and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Malik informed us, (ha) and Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: Malik narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah: Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh said: O Messenger of Allah, I never become pure; shall I leave prayer? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: That is only a vein, not menstruation; when menstruation comes, leave prayer, and when it departs, wash the blood from yourself and pray."
"22557","891 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I read to Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, she said: Fatimah bint Hubaysh came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I suffer non-menstrual bleeding; shall I leave prayer? He said: When menstruation comes, leave it for its duration, then wash the blood and pray."
"22558","892 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, (ha) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, (ha) and Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Mazini narrated to us: Kathir ibn Yahya narrated to us, all said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah: Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh sought a ruling from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: I suffer non-menstrual bleeding and never become pure; shall I leave prayer? He said: That is a vein, not menstruation; when menstruation comes, leave prayer, and when it departs, wash the blood from yourself, and perform ablution, for that is only a vein, not menstruation."
"22559","893 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us: Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us: Za'idah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, she said: Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I suffer non-menstrual bleeding and never become pure; shall I leave prayer? He said: That is only a vein, not menstruation; when menstruation comes, leave prayer, and when it departs, wash the blood from yourself and pray."
"22560","894 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah: Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I am a woman who suffers non-menstrual bleeding and never becomes pure; shall I leave prayer? He said: That is only a vein, not menstruation; when menstruation comes, leave prayer, and when it departs, wash the trace of blood from yourself and pray."
"22561","895 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Abu Hanifah narrated to us, (ha) and Ahmad ibn Rustah al-Asbahani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Zufar ibn al-Hudhayl, from Abi Hanifah, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah: Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh said: O Messenger of Allah, I suffer non-menstrual bleeding and the blood never ceases from me. He said: Leave prayer the days of your menstruation; when the days of your menstruation are gone, wash and perform ablution for every prayer."
"22562","896 - Muhammad ibn Mu'adh al-Halabi narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Maslamah al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: my father Maslamah ibn Qa'nab narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah: Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I suffer non-menstrual bleeding and never become pure; shall I leave prayer? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is only a vein, not menstruation; when menstruation comes, leave prayer, and when it departs, wash the blood from yourself and pray."
"22563","897 - al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi narrated to us: Rubayh Abu Ghassan al-Razi narrated to us: Abd Allah narrated to us, from Ibn Maghra', Ubayd Allah said: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah: Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I suffer non-menstrual bleeding and see blood. He commanded her to sit out the days of her regular cycle; when her time of purity came, she would wash, then perform ablution for every prayer, saying: It is only a vein from you."
"22564","898 - al-Fadl ibn Salih al-Hashimi narrated to us: Abu Marwan al-Uthmani narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah, she said: Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh al-Asadiyyah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking a ruling, being a woman who suffered non-menstrual bleeding, and said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I never become pure; shall I leave prayer for this? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is only a vein, not menstruation; when it comes, leave prayer, and when it departs, wash the blood from yourself, then pray."
"22565","899 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to me: Ismail ibn Ullayah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah: Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh said: O Messenger of Allah, I suffer non-menstrual bleeding and never become pure; shall I then leave prayer? He said: That is not menstruation, it is only a vein; when menstruation comes, leave prayer, and when it turns away - or he said: departs - wash the blood from yourself and pray."
"22566","900 - Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Imran ibn Abi Jamil narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abd Allah ibn Sama'ah narrated to us: al-Awza'i narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari narrated to us: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Fatimah bint Qays of Banu Asad of Quraysh: She came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned to him that she suffered non-menstrual bleeding; Fatimah claimed that he said: That is only a vein; when menstruation comes, leave prayer, and when it departs, wash the trace of blood from yourself, then pray."
"22567","Fatimah bint al-Walid. 901 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah, from Ibrahim ibn al-Abbas ibn al-Harith, from Abi Bakr ibn al-Harith, from Fatimah bint al-Walid: She was in Sham wearing garments of khazz, then she would wear a waist-wrapper. It was said to her: Does this not suffice you instead of the waist-wrapper? She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoining the waist-wrapper."
"22568","Fatimah bint al-Mujallil ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Qays ibn Abd Wudd ibn Nasr ibn Amir ibn Lu'ayy ibn Ghalib. 902 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, (ha) and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, (ha) and al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us: Bashshar ibn Musa al-Khaffaf narrated to us, all of them from Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Hatib: my father Uthman ibn Ibrahim informed me, from his grandfather Muhammad ibn Hatib, from his mother Umm Jamil bint al-Mujallil, she said: I came with you from the land of Abyssinia, and when I was a night or two from Madinah, I cooked a meal for you, and the firewood ran out, so I went out seeking it, and you reached for the pot and it tipped over onto your arm. I brought you to Madinah and brought you to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, this is Muhammad ibn Hatib, the first to be named after you. He wiped his hand over your head, supplicated for blessing for you, spat into your mouth, then began spitting upon your hand, saying: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, and heal, You are the Healer; there is no healing but Your healing, a healing that leaves no sickness. I did not rise with you from him until your hand had healed."
"22569","903 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Muhammad ibn Hatib al-Qurashi, he said: I reached for a pot of ours and my hand was burned; my mother took me to a man sitting in the graveyard, and said to him: O Messenger of Allah. He said: At your service, and may you be aided. Then she brought me near to him, and he began to blow and speak words I did not understand. I asked my mother afterwards: What was he saying? She said: He was saying: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind; heal, You are the Healer, there is no healer but You."
"22570","Fatimah bint Utbah ibn Rabi'ah ibn Umayyah ibn Abd Shams. 904 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, from Abi Ayyub, freedman of al-Qasim, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Fatimah bint Utbah ibn Rabi'ah: Abu Hudhayfah ibn Utbah took her and her sister Hind to pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he stipulated upon them, Hind said: Do you know among the women of your people any of these faults and blemishes? Abu Hudhayfah said: Pledge to him, for such is stipulated."
"22571","Fatimah bint Amr ibn Haram, paternal aunt of Jabir ibn Abd Allah. 905 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, he said: My father was brought slain on the day of Uhud, and his sister Fatimah began weeping over him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Weep not over him; the angels continued to shade him with their wings until he was raised."
"22572","Fatimah bint Qays al-Fihriyyah. What Ibn Abbas narrated from Fatimah. 906 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar narrated to us: Abu Shihab narrated to us: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Ata', from Ibn Abbas: Fatimah bint Qays said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted me neither lodging nor maintenance."
"22573","907 - Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr narrated to us: Affan narrated to us, (ha) and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, brother of Hajjaj, narrated to us, both said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ata', from Ibn Abbas, from Fatimah bint Qays: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted her neither lodging nor maintenance."
"22574","Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from Fatimah bint Qays. 908 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Ubayd al-Qasim ibn Sallam and Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, (ha) and Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated to us, all said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: Fatimah bint Qays said: O Messenger of Allah, my husband has divorced me, and I fear he may burst in upon me; so he ordered her to move."
"22575","Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf from Fatimah. 909 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj: Ibn Shihab informed me, from Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman: Fatimah bint Qays narrated to me that she was married to Abu Amr ibn Hafs ibn al-Mughirah, and he divorced her with the last of three divorces; she claimed that she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking a ruling about leaving her house, and he ordered her - she claimed - to move to Ibn Umm Maktum, the blind man. Marwan refused but to cast doubt on the hadith of Fatimah concerning the divorced woman leaving her house."
"22576","910 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Numayr al-Misri narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Ufayr narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to us, from Uqayl, and Rashdin ibn Sa'd, from Uqayl, and Qurrah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Shihab, from Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Fatimah bint Qays: She was married to Abu Amr ibn Hafs ibn al-Mughirah, and he divorced her with three divorces; she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking a ruling about leaving her house, and he ordered her to move to Ibn Umm Maktum."
"22577","911 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us: Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Fatimah bint Qays: She was married to Abu Amr ibn Hafs ibn al-Mughirah, and he divorced her with three divorces; she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking a ruling about leaving her house, and he ordered her to move to the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, the blind man."
"22578","912 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Sa'd al-Zuhri narrated to us: my uncle narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from al-Zuhri, from Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Fatimah bint Qays: She was married to Abu Amr ibn Hafs ibn al-Mughirah, and he divorced her with three divorces; she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking a ruling about leaving her house, and he ordered her to move to the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, the blind man."
"22579","913 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both said: al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, (ha) and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Malik narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, freedman of al-Aswad ibn Sufyan, from Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Fatimah bint Qays: Abu Amr ibn Hafs divorced her irrevocably while he was absent, and sent his agent with some barley, but she scorned it. He said: By Allah, you have nothing due from us. She came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: You have no maintenance. He ordered her to observe her waiting period in the house of Umm Sharik, then said: She is a woman whom my companions frequent; observe your waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is a blind man; you may lay aside your garments, and when you become lawful, come to me. When she became lawful, she mentioned to him that Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan and Abu Jahm ibn Hudhayfah had proposed to her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for Abu Jahm, he never puts his stick down from his shoulder; as for Mu'awiyah, he is a poor man with no wealth; marry Usamah ibn Zayd. She said: I disliked him, then he said: Marry Usamah ibn Zayd; so Allah placed good in him for her, and she came to cherish him."
"22580","914 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Sadusi narrated to us: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman and Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Qusayt, from Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, and from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Fatimah bint Qays, she said: My husband divorced me, and he used to provide me food of poor quality, and I was a woman with no one; I said: By Allah, if I have maintenance due, I shall surely claim it. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: You have no maintenance and no lodging; observe your waiting period with Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is blind, and when you become lawful, inform me. When I became lawful I informed him, and he said: Who proposed to you? I said: Mu'awiyah, and another man. He said: As for Mu'awiyah, he is a youth of the youths of Quraysh with nothing in his hand - or: he has nothing; as for the other, he is a man of evil; marry Usamah ibn Zayd. I disliked him, but he said: Marry him; so I married him."
"22581","915 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to me: Imran ibn Abi Anas narrated to me, from Abi Salamah, he said: I asked Fatimah bint Qays and she informed me that her Makhzumi husband divorced her and refused to maintain her; she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have no maintenance; go and move to Ibn Umm Maktum and stay with him, for he is a blind man; you may lay aside your garments in his presence."
"22582","916 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Ayli narrated to us: Salamah ibn Rawh narrated to us, from Uqayl ibn Khalid, from Imran ibn Abi Anas, from Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Fatimah bint Qays, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"22583","917 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abi Salamah, from Fatimah bint Qays: She was married to a man of Banu Makhzum, and he divorced her irrevocably; she sent to his family seeking maintenance, and they said: No maintenance is due from us. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: You have no maintenance due from them, but the waiting period is upon you; move to Umm Sharik. Then he said: Umm Sharik is visited by her brothers among the Muhajirun; nay, rather move to Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is a blind man; if you lay aside your garments he sees nothing; and do not forestall us with yourself. When she became lawful, she mentioned that Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan and Abu Jahm had proposed to her. He said: As for Mu'awiyah, he has no wealth; as for Abu Jahm, he never puts his stick down from his shoulder; where are you with regard to Usamah? Her family seemed to dislike that, but she said: By Allah, I shall marry none but whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told me; so she married him."
"22584","918 - Abu Yazid Yusuf ibn Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated to us, (ha) and Yusuf narrated to us: Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, both said: Ismail ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abi Salamah, from Fatimah bint Qays: She was married to a man of Banu Makhzum, and he divorced her irrevocably; she sent to his family seeking maintenance, and they said: You have no maintenance due from us. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: You have no maintenance due from them, but the waiting period is upon you; move to Umm Sharik. Then he said: Umm Sharik is visited by her brothers among the first Muhajirun; move to Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is a blind man; if you lay aside your garments he sees nothing; so do not forestall us with yourself. When she became lawful, some men mentioned her, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Where are you with regard to Usamah? Her family seemed to dislike that, but she said: By Allah, I shall marry none but whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said; so she married him."
"22585","919 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abi Salamah, from Fatimah bint Qays, he said: I wrote that down from her mouth. She said: I was married to a man of Banu Makhzum, and he divorced me irrevocably; I sent to his family requesting maintenance, and they said: You have no maintenance due from us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have no maintenance due from them, but the waiting period is upon you; move to Umm Sharik, and do not forestall us with yourself. Then he said: Umm Sharik is visited by her brothers among the first Muhajirun; rather move to Ibn Umm Maktum, for his sight is gone, and if you lay aside anything he sees nothing."
"22586","920 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Shayban, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me that Fatimah bint Qays, sister of al-Dahhak ibn Qays, informed him: Her husband Hafs ibn al-Mughirah al-Makhzumi divorced her three times in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he set out for Yemen. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: She has no maintenance, but the waiting period is upon her. He sent a messenger to her: Do not forestall me with yourself. He ordered her to move to Umm Sharik, then sent to her: Umm Sharik is visited by the first Muhajirun; move to Ibn Umm Maktum. When her waiting period ended, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her to Usamah ibn Zayd ibn Harithah."
"22587","921 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni al-Tustari narrated to us ... Ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us: Fudayl ibn Sulayman al-Numayri narrated to us: Abu Hazim narrated to us: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Fatimah bint Qays: Her husband divorced her in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would send her maintenance; when he saw that, she said: By Allah, I shall surely speak to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); if I have maintenance due, I shall take what suffices me, and if I have no maintenance due, I shall take nothing. So she asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: You have neither lodging nor maintenance."
"22588","922 - Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abi Salamah, from Fatimah bint Qays: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the last night prayer one night, then came out and said: What kept me back was a story Tamim al-Dari was telling me, about a man on an island among the islands of the sea; he came upon a woman dragging her hair, and said: Who are you? She said: I am al-Jassasah; do you marvel at me? He said: Yes; go to that palace. So he went to it, and there was a man dragging his hair, chained in fetters, leaping between heaven and earth. He said to him: Who are you? He said: I am al-Dajjal. Has the prophet of the unlettered come forth? He said: Yes. He said: Did they obey him or disobey him? He said: Nay, rather they obeyed him. He said: That is better for them. And have the waters receded?"
"22589","923 - Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Sa'igh al-Baghdadi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyabi narrated to us: Fadalah ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Mujammi', from Ibn Shihab, from Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Fatimah bint Qays, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat delaying the last night prayer until the people slept, then came out and said: What kept me back was a story Tamim al-Dari told me, about a man on an island; he came upon a woman dragging her hair, and said: Who are you? She said: I am al-Jassasah; do you marvel at me? Go to that palace. So he went, and there was a man dragging his hair, chained in fetters. I said: Who are you? He said: I am al-Dajjal. He said: Has their messenger come forth among the unlettered? I said: Yes. He said: Did they obey him or disobey him? I said: Nay, rather they obeyed him. He said: That is better for them."
"22590","Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah from Fatimah. 924 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah informed me that Abu Amr ibn Hafs ibn al-Mughirah went out with Ali to Yemen, and sent to his wife, the daughter of Qays, the remaining divorce of her divorce; al-Harith ibn Hisham and Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah ordered maintenance for her, but she deemed it scant, so they said: By Allah, you have no maintenance unless you are pregnant. She came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned her affair to him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: You have no maintenance. She sought his permission to move, and he permitted her. She said: Where, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To Ibn Umm Maktum, who was blind; you may lay aside your garments in his presence and he will not see you. When her waiting period with him ended, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her to Usamah ibn Zayd. Marwan sent Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb to ask her about that, and she narrated to him; Qabisah came to Marwan and informed him, and Marwan said: I have not heard this hadith."
"22591","925 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah informed me that Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Uthman divorced - while a young lad, during the governorship of Marwan - the daughter of Sa'id ibn Zayd, whose mother was the daughter of Qays, with an irrevocable divorce. Her maternal aunt Fatimah bint Qays sent to her and ordered her to move from the house of her husband Abd Allah ibn Amr. Marwan heard of that and sent to her ordering her to return to her dwelling, asking her what had prompted her to move before her waiting period ended. She sent informing him that her maternal aunt Fatimah bint Qays had ruled for her that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had ruled for her to leave or move when Abu Amr ibn Hafs al-Makhzumi divorced her. Marwan sent Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb to Fatimah bint Qays to ask her about that, and she informed him that she had been married to Abu Amr ibn Hafs al-Makhzumi. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had placed Ali in command over part of Yemen, so her husband went out with him and sent her the remaining divorce due to her; he ordered Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah and al-Harith ibn Hisham to maintain her, but they said: By Allah, she has no maintenance unless she is pregnant. She sought his permission to move, and he permitted her. She said: Where shall I move, O Messenger of Allah? He said: With Ibn Umm Maktum, who was blind; you may lay aside your garments in his presence and he will not see you. She remained there until her waiting period ended, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her to Usamah ibn Zayd. Qabisah returned to Marwan and informed him of that, and Marwan said: I have heard this hadith only from a woman; we take to the firm practice which we found the people upon. When that reached Fatimah, she said: Between me and you is the Book of Allah. Allah said: Then divorce them for their waiting period, up to His saying: You know not, perhaps Allah will bring about after that a new matter. She said: And what new matter comes after the third? It is only the man taking back his wife; so how do you say: She has no maintenance if she is not pregnant? How is a woman detained without maintenance?"
"22592","926 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Husayn ibn Umar al-Ahmasi narrated to us, from Mukhariq, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Fatimah bint Qays, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): with the hadith of al-Jassasah."
"22593","Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb from Fatimah. 927 - Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri mentioned that Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb narrated to him: The daughter of Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl - she was Mahrama bint Qays, and Fatimah bint Qays was her maternal aunt - was married to Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Uthman, and he divorced her three times; her maternal aunt sent to her and moved her to her house, while Marwan ibn al-Hakam was over Madinah. Qabisah said: Marwan ibn al-Hakam sent me to her to ask her what had prompted her to take a woman out of her house before her waiting period ended. She said: Because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to do that. Then she told her story, saying: And I contend with you by the Book of Allah; Allah says in His Book: When you divorce women, divorce them for their waiting period, count the waiting period, fear Allah your Lord, expel them not from their houses nor let them go forth unless they commit a clear indecency; you know not, perhaps Allah will bring about after that a new matter; and: When they reach their term, the third: Then retain them in kindness or release them in kindness. By Allah, Allah mentioned no detention after the third, after what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me. He said: So I returned to Marwan and informed him, and he said: A woman's hadith, a woman's hadith. Then he ordered the woman returned to her house until her waiting period ended."
"22594","Abd al-Rahman ibn Asim ibn Thabit from Fatimah. 928 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj: Ata' informed me: Abd al-Rahman ibn Asim ibn Thabit informed me that Fatimah bint Qays, sister of al-Dahhak ibn Qays, was married to a man of Banu Makhzum, and she informed him that he divorced her three times and went out on one of the campaigns, leaving an agent to give her some maintenance, but she deemed it scant. She went to one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in while she was with her. She said: O Messenger of Allah, this is Fatimah bint Qays; so-and-so divorced her and sent her some maintenance, but she returned it, claiming it was something he granted as a favor. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He spoke the truth. Then he said to her: Move to Umm Maktum and observe your waiting period with her. Then he said: Nay, Umm Maktum is a woman with many visitors; rather move to Abd Allah ibn Umm Maktum, for he is blind. So she moved to him and observed her waiting period with him until it ended. Then Abu Jahm and Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan proposed to her, and she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking his counsel about them. He said: As for Abu Jahm, I fear for you his harshness with the stick; as for Mu'awiyah, he is a man devoid of wealth. So she married Usamah ibn Zayd after that."
"22595","Abu Bakr ibn Sukhayr ibn Abi al-Jahm from Fatimah. 929 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abi Bakr ibn Abi al-Jahm, he said: I came with Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman to Fatimah bint Qays, sister of al-Dahhak ibn Qays, while she had brought out her niece at noon. I said: What prompted you to this? She said: My husband Abu Hafs ibn al-Mughirah sent me, with Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah, my divorce three times, along with five sa's of barley and five sa's of dates. I said: Is this all the maintenance I have? I gathered my garments and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: How many times did he divorce you? I said: Three. He said: He spoke the truth; you have no maintenance; observe your waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, laying aside your garments."
"22596","930 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Asbahani narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, (ha) and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Abi Bakr ibn Sukhayr, he said: I entered with Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman upon Fatimah bint Qays, whose husband had divorced her three times, and she said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he granted me neither lodging nor maintenance."
"22597","931 - Abd Allah ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Utbah ibn Abd Allah, from Abi Bakr ibn al-Jahm, he said: I entered upon Fatimah bint Qays, whose husband had divorced her three times, and she said: He gave me as provision three sa's of barley and three sa's of dates. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to stay with Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is blind of sight and will not see me when I remove my veil. He said: When you become lawful, do not forestall me. When I became lawful, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did anyone mention you? I said: Yes, Mu'awiyah and Abu Jahm. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for Abu Jahm, he is severe in character toward his wives; as for Mu'awiyah, he has no wealth; but marry Usamah. I said: Usamah - belittling the matter of Usamah - then I said: Hearing and obeying Allah and His Messenger. So he married me to Usamah; Allah honored me through Ibn Zayd, ennobled me through Ibn Zayd, and benefited me through Ibn Zayd."
"22598","Abd Allah al-Bahiyy from Fatimah. 932 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us: Hibban ibn Busr al-Qadi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from al-Bahiyy, from Fatimah bint Qays: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted her neither lodging nor maintenance."
"22599","Al-Aswad ibn Yazid from Fatimah. 933 - Allan ibn Abd al-Samad Maghammah narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Aswad al-Ajlani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from al-Aswad, from Fatimah, she said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he granted me neither lodging nor maintenance."
"22600","Amir al-Sha'bi from Fatimah bint Qays. 934 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, (ha) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, (ha) and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, both said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, she said: My husband divorced me three times, and I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: You have neither maintenance nor lodging."
"22601","935 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Amir al-Sha'bi: Fatimah bint Qays narrated to me - she had been married to Abu Hafs ibn Amr, or Amr ibn Hafs - and she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about maintenance and lodging. He said to her: Listen, O daughter of Qays - gesturing with his hand, stretching it over part of his face as though veiling himself from her, as though saying: Be silent; maintenance is due to a woman from her husband only while return to her remains possible; when return to her is no longer possible, she has neither maintenance nor lodging. Go to so-and-so - or he said: Umm Sharik - and observe your waiting period with her. Then he said: Nay, she is a woman whom people gather to - or he said: converse with; observe your waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum."
"22602","936 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, both said: Musaddad narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, he said: The people of Madinah differed with us about the lodging and maintenance of the divorced woman, saying to me: Between us and you is the hadith of Fatimah bint Qays. So I came to her and entered upon her and asked her. She said: My husband divorced me, and his brother said to me: You have neither lodging nor maintenance. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O daughter of Qays, lodging and maintenance are only while your husband retains return to you."
"22603","937 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays: She asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: My husband divorced me, assigning me neither maintenance nor lodging. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Your husband will not take you back; lodging and maintenance are only for her whom her husband may take back."
"22604","938 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Ubayd al-Qasim ibn Sallam narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Mughirah, Husayn, Sayyar, Dawud ibn Abi Hind, Mujalid, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, and Ash'ath informed us, all from al-Sha'bi, he said: I entered upon Fatimah bint Qays in Madinah and asked her about the ruling of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: My husband divorced me irrevocably, and I disputed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about lodging and maintenance; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted me neither lodging nor maintenance, and ordered me to observe my waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum."
"22605","939 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Tustari al-Bazzaz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Mu'ammal ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us: Sa'id ibn al-Rabi' Abu Zayd al-Harawi narrated to us: Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Sayyar Abi al-Hakam: Amir al-Sha'bi narrated to me, he said: We entered upon Fatimah bint Qays and asked her about the woman divorced three times: where does she observe her waiting period? She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted me, when my husband divorced me, to observe my waiting period among my family."
"22606","940 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us: Umar ibn Hafs narrated to us: my father narrated to me, (ha) and Ahmad ibn al-Qasim al-Ta'i narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us: Abu Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, both from al-A'mash, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, she said: My husband divorced me three times, and I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he granted me neither lodging nor maintenance."
"22607","941 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from al-Sha'bi: Fatimah bint Qays - her husband divorced her with a final divorce, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have neither maintenance nor lodging."
"22608","942 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Aswad narrated to us: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Abi Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Abi Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, she said: My husband divorced me three times, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted me neither lodging nor maintenance."
"22609","943 - Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to me, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Farwah, from Abi al-Zinad, from Amir al-Sha'bi: He asked Fatimah bint Qays, saying: How many divorces did Hafs ibn Abi Amr pronounce upon you? She said: He divorced me three times while going out to Yemen, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upheld that. I sent to my husband's family asking my maintenance, and they wanted to expel me from my home, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Move to Ibn Umm Maktum."
"22610","944 - Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Hammad al-Barbari narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Salim, from Amir al-Sha'bi, he said: I met Fatimah bint Qays at al-Harrah and asked her how her affair was. She said: My husband Abu Amr divorced me before going out to Yemen, appointing Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah as agent and giving me maintenance; I disputed him before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: You have neither maintenance due from them nor lodging."
"22611","945 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abbadah al-Wasiti narrated to us: Qurrah ibn Isa narrated to us: Dawud al-Awdi narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Sha'bi say: Fatimah bint Qays narrated to me that she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my husband divorced me three times, and I sought lodging and maintenance. He said: One divorce, two divorces: you inherit from him and he inherits from you; three: you inherit not from him nor he from you, and you have neither lodging nor maintenance; stay with Ibn Umm Maktum."
"22612","946 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim al-Razi narrated to us: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us: Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, she said: I was married to a man of Banu Makhzum, and he divorced me three times; he said: You have no maintenance due from me. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my husband divorced me, and I requested maintenance from him, but he said: You have neither lodging due from me nor maintenance. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have lodging and maintenance due. He sent for him and he said: I divorced her three times. He said: Then observe your waiting period in the house of Umm Sharik. Then he said: Umm Sharik is a much-visited woman; rather observe your waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is a blind man."
"22613","947 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both said: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mutarrif ibn Tarif, from Amir al-Sha'bi, he said: I asked Fatimah bint Qays about the woman whom her husband divorces three times. She said: My husband divorced me three times in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking about lodging and maintenance; he granted me neither lodging nor maintenance."
"22614","948 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Bazzar al-Tustari narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sawwaf narrated to us: Bakr ibn Bakkar narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Yazid al-Bajali narrated to us: Amir al-Sha'bi narrated to us that he entered upon Fatimah bint Qays, sister of al-Dahhak ibn Qays al-Qurashi, whose husband was Abu Amr ibn Hafs ibn al-Mughirah al-Makhzumi, and she said: Abu Amr ibn Hafs sent me, while setting out with an army to Yemen, my divorce. I asked his guardians for maintenance and lodging for me, and they said: He sent us nothing about that nor enjoined it upon us. I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Amr ibn Hafs sent me my divorce, and I requested lodging and maintenance for me, but his guardians said: He sent us nothing about that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Lodging and maintenance are only for the woman while her husband retains return to her; when she is not lawful to him until she marries another husband, she has neither maintenance nor lodging."
"22615","949 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us: Abu Ma'mar Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Abi al-Hajjaj al-Minqari narrated to us: Abd al-Warith narrated to us: al-Husayn al-Mu'allim narrated to me: Abd Allah ibn Buraydah narrated to me: Amir al-Sha'bi narrated to me that Fatimah bint Qays narrated to him, she said: I married Hafs ibn al-Mughirah, among the best youths of Quraysh; when I became widowed, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf proposed to me among a group of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to me on behalf of his freedman Usamah ibn Zayd. I had been told that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves me, let him love Usamah. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke to me, I said: My affair is in your hand; marry me to whom you wish. He said: Move to Umm Sharik, and Umm Sharik is a wealthy woman of great spending in the path of Allah, with whom guests stay. I said: I shall do so. He said: Do not do so, for Umm Sharik is a woman with many guests, and I dislike that your veil should fall from you or your garment uncover your shins so the people see of you what you dislike; rather move to your cousin Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Umm Maktum, a man of Banu Fihr of Quraysh, of the same clan she is from. So I moved to him."
"22616","950 - Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Jawhari and al-Qasim ibn Abbad al-Khattabi narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Amir al-Sha'bi, he said: I asked Fatimah bint Qays how her affair was. She said: My husband divorced me with three divorces all together, and I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: My in-laws claim I have neither lodging nor maintenance. He said: They spoke the truth; go and observe your waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, who was blind. She said: Abu al-Jahm ibn Hudhayfah proposed to her, and after him Mu'awiyah, after the waiting period ended; she consulted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: As for Abu Jahm, he beats women; as for Mu'awiyah, he is ingratiating - meaning penniless - owning nothing; but where are you with regard to Usamah? I said: Shall I marry Usamah? He said: Yes, marry Usamah."
"22617","951 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq: al-Sha'bi narrated to me: Fatimah bint Qays narrated to me that her husband divorced her three times, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted her neither lodging nor maintenance."
"22618","952 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Hasan ibn Salih, from Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Fatimah bint Qays narrated to us that her husband divorced her three times, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted her neither dwelling nor maintenance. He said: Her husband was Abu Hafs ibn Amr ibn al-Mughirah."
"22619","953 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, he said, she said: My husband divorced me in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) three times, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No lodging and no maintenance."
"22620","954 - Ibrahim ibn Umar al-Waki'i narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Zurayq, from Abi Ishaq, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, she said: My husband divorced me three times, and I sought maintenance, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Move to the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, your cousin, and observe your waiting period with him."
"22621","955 - Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Sufyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan narrated to us, Ghassan ibn Ubayd al-Mawsili narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Hakim al-Habati narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays: her husband divorced her, so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered her to observe her waiting period in the house of Ibn Umm Maktum."
"22622","956 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ayyub Abu Asim al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Amir al-Sha'bi narrated to us, he said: I set out with a man until we entered upon Fatimah bint Qays, sister of al-Dahhak ibn Qays, and we said: O Fatimah, narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: Yes, and she fed us fresh dates and gave us drink, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out one day and sat on the pulpit, and the people gathered around him and clung to him, and he said: O people, only a report has seated me here. Tamim al-Dari came to me today in the midday heat and told me that some of his cousins were cast by their ship in the sea upon an island they did not know, so they walked about in it and met a creature so covered with hair they could not tell whether it was a man or a woman. They said: Who are you? It said: I am al-Jassasah. They said: Tell us. It said: I will neither tell you nor ask you; if you want news, go to this monastery, and it pointed to a monastery on the island not far off. So they walked until they entered it, and there was a man bound with heavy iron chains, leaning his back against the foot of a mountain. He said: Who are you? They said: People from the Arabs. He said: What has the unlettered Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who is awaited done? They said: He has come forth. He said: What have the palms between Amman and Baysan done? They said: As before, they feed and bear fruit. He said: What has the spring of Zughar done? They said: As it was. He said: What has the Lake of Tiberias done? They said: It is full. Then he struck the sole of his foot with his hand and said: If I were to come out of this seat of mine I would leave no spot on earth untrodden except Makkah and Taybah. Then he panted and moved through the mountain, then fell, then moved a second time further than that, then fell, then moved a third time and went into the mountain, then fell. We said: What is wrong with him, may Allah not bless him. And it was as though the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was pleased by his words about Makkah and Taybah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Taybah - twice - the Dajjal shall not enter it; there is no mountain pass of it except that an angel with unsheathed sword stands over it, and what is toward Yemen is as it is. Then he gestured with his hand, his shirt sleeve near thirty times, toward Iraq, and it is near thirty times."
"22623","957 - Abu Ubaydah Abd al-Warith ibn Ibrahim al-Askari narrated to us, Sayf ibn Miskin al-Iswari narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab Ja'far ibn Hayyan al-Utaridi narrated to us, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, she said: I heard the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) calling: Prayer is gathering, so I went out among women of the Ansar until we reached the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the noon prayer, then ascended the pulpit, faced us smiling, then said: By Allah, I have not gathered you for something desired or feared, but for a hadith Tamim al-Dari narrated to me; he came to me, accepted Islam, pledged allegiance, and told me that he sailed with thirty men of Lakhm and Judham, two Arab tribes of the people of Yemen, and they met the sea when it was raging and the waves tossed them for a month, then cast them near sunset upon an island of the islands of the sea, and we met a thick-haired beast whose front could not be known from its back. We said: What are you, O beast? So Allah permitted it and it spoke to us with an eloquent fluent tongue, and said: I am al-Jassasah. We said: What is al-Jassasah? It said: Away from me; go to that monastery at the far end of the island, for in it is a man most eager for your news. So we came to the monastery, and there was the greatest man I ever saw and the finest in body, with his right eye effaced as though his eye were spittle on a plastered wall, his hands chained to his neck, and his legs bound with fetters from his knees to his feet. We said to him: What are you, O man? He said: As for my news you have already come upon it, but tell me your news: what cast you upon this island? And this island no human has reached since I came out to it. So we told him, and he said: Tell me about the Lake of Tiberias, what has it done? We said: About which of its affairs do you ask? He said: Has its water receded, and have wonders appeared in it? We said: No. He said: Yet it shall be. Then he was silent a while, then said: Tell me about the spring of Zughar, what has it done? We said: About which of its affairs do you ask? He said: Do its people plough by it? We said: Yes. He said: Yet its water shall sink away. Then he was silent a while, then said: Tell me about the palms of Baysan, what have they done? We said: About which of their affairs do you ask? He said: Do they bear fruit? We said: Yes. He said: Yet they shall not bear fruit. Then he was silent a while, then said: Tell me about the unlettered Prophet, what has he done? We said: About which of his affairs do you ask? He said: Has he appeared yet? We said: Yes. He said: What have the Arabs done with him? We said: Some of them fought him and some believed him. He said: Yet whoever believes him, it is better for him. So we said: Tell us your news, O man. He said: Do you not know me? We said: Had we known you we would not have asked you. He said: I am the Dajjal; soon I shall be permitted to come out, and when I come out I shall tread all the islands of the Arabs except Makkah and Taybah; whenever I intend them an angel with drawn sword meets me and turns me back from them. Abu al-Ashhab said: Amir said: Fatimah bint Qays said: And I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his hands until we saw the whiteness of his armpits, then he said: Shall I not tell you that this is Taybah, three times, then he said: Shall I not tell you that he is in the Sea of Sham, three times, then he was covered for a while, then he recovered and it was lifted from him, and he said: Rather he is in the Sea of Iraq; when he comes out, he will come out from a town called Asbahan, from one of its villages called Rustaqabad, and those who come out at his vanguard will be seventy thousand wearing al-Sijan, with him two rivers, a river of water and a river of fire; whoever of you reaches that and is told: Enter the water, let him not enter it, for it is fire, and if told: Enter the fire, let him enter it, for it is water."
"22624","958 - Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Ma'mar Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Abi al-Hajjaj al-Minqari narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Husayn ibn Dhakwan al-Mu'allim narrated to me, Ibn Buraydah narrated to me, Amir ibn Sharahil al-Sha'bi of Sha'b Hamdan narrated to me that he asked Fatimah bint Qays, sister of al-Dahhak ibn Qays, who was among the first emigrant women. He said: Narrate to me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) without attributing it to anyone but yourself. She said: If you wish I shall do so. He said to her: Yes, narrate to me. She said: I heard the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) calling: Prayer is gathering, so I went out to the mosque and prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I was in the women's row next to the backs of the men. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer he sat on the pulpit laughing, and said: Let every person stay at his prayer place, then he said: Do you know why I gathered you? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: By Allah, I have not gathered you for something desired or feared, but I gathered you because Tamim al-Dari was a Christian man, then he came, pledged allegiance and accepted Islam, and narrated to me a hadith matching what I used to narrate to you about the Masih al-Dajjal. He narrated to me that he sailed in a sea ship with thirty men of Lakhm and Judham, and the waves tossed them for a month in the sea, then they drifted to an island in the sea at sunset, so they sat in the ship's boat and entered the island, and a thick-haired very hairy beast met them so they could not tell its front from its back for its abundant hair. They said: Woe to you, what are you? It said: I am al-Jassasah. They said: What is al-Jassasah? It said: O people, go to this man in the monastery, for he is most eager for your news. When it named a man to us we feared it might be a she-devil, so we set out swiftly until we entered the monastery, and in it was the greatest human we ever saw in creation and the most tightly bound, his hands gathered to his neck, and between his knees and his ankles bound with iron. We said: Woe to you, what are you? He said: You have already come upon my news, so tell me who you are. They said: People from the Arabs; we sailed in a sea ship and met the sea when it was raging, and the waves tossed us for a month, then cast us upon this island of yours, so we sat in its boat and entered the island, and a thick-haired very hairy beast met us so we could not tell its front from its back, and we said: Woe to you, what are you? It said: I am al-Jassasah. We said: What is al-Jassasah? It said: Betake yourselves to this man, for he is most eager for your news. So we came to you swiftly, and we feared it and were not sure it was not a she-devil. He said: Tell me about the palms of Baysan. We said: About which of their affairs do you ask? He said: I ask you about its palms, do they bear fruit? We said: Yes. He said: Yet they shall soon not bear fruit. He said: Tell me about the Lake of Tiberias. We said: About which of its affairs do you ask? He said: Is there water in it? We said: It is abundant in water. He said: Tell me about the spring of Zughar. They said: About which of its affairs do you ask? He said: Is there water in the spring, and do its people cultivate with the spring's water? We said: Yes, it is abundant in water and its people cultivate with its water. He said: Tell me about the unlettered Prophet, what has he done? They said: He came out of Makkah and settled in Yathrib. He said: Did the Arabs fight him? We said: Yes. He said: How did he fare with them? So we told him that he prevailed over the Arabs near him and they obeyed him. He said to them: That indeed happened? We said: Yes. He said: Yet that they do so and obey him is better for them. I shall tell you about myself: I am the Masih, and soon I shall be permitted to come out, so I shall come out and travel through the land, leaving no town but I shall descend upon it in forty nights, except Makkah and Taybah, and they are both forbidden to me; whenever I wish to enter either of them an angel with drawn sword meets me and bars me from it, and over every mountain pass of them are angels guarding them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, striking the pulpit with his short staff: This is Taybah, this is Taybah, this is Taybah - meaning Madinah - did I not narrate that to you? The people said: Yes. He said: What pleases me in the hadith of Tamim al-Dari is only that it matches what I used to narrate to you about it, and about Madinah and Makkah. He is in the Sea of Sham, or the Sea of Yemen; no, rather from the direction of the east, he is from the direction of the east, he is from the direction of the east, and he gestured with his hand toward the east. She said: I memorized this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"22625","959 - Abu Shu'ayb Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Imran ibn Sulayman al-Qaysi, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Fatimah bint Qays narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called: Prayer is gathering, at an hour in which he would not usually call, so the people came out to the mosque, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, ascended the pulpit, then said: I warn you of the Dajjal - three times - he was not in what has passed, yet he shall be among you, O community, and Tamim al-Dari told me that he sailed the Sea of Sham with a party of Lakhm and Judham, and the wind cast them upon an island of its islands, and they met al-Dahma dragging its hair. They said: What are you? It said: I am al-Jassasah. They said: Tell us. It said: I shall neither tell you nor ask you, but go to a man in this monastery, for he is most eager for your news. So they went to him, and there was a man with effaced eye, bound to a pillar with iron. He said: Who are you? They said: We are Arabs. He said: What have the Arabs done? We said: An unlettered Prophet was sent to them calling them to Allah. He said: What did the people do? They said: Some followed him and some left him. He said: Yet if they follow him and believe him it is better for them, if only they knew. Then he said: What have the Arabs done? What is their clothing? We said: Wool and cotton which their women spin. Then he struck his thigh with his hand, then said: Alas. Then he said: What have the palms of Baysan done? We said: They are strong, and we find them every year. Then he struck his thigh with his hand, then said: Alas. Then he said: What has the spring of Zughar done? We said: Its water is abundant, gushing, giving drink to whoever comes to it. Then he struck his thigh with his hand, then said: Alas. Then he said: If Allah were to release me from my bonds, no watering place would remain but I would enter it except Makkah and Taybah, for I am not allowed to enter them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is Makkah, and this is Taybah, which Allah made sacred as Ibrahim made Makkah sacred. There is no mountain pass nor lane except that an angel with drawn sword stands over it, barring it from the Dajjal until the Day of Resurrection."
"22626","960 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, she said: While the people had no alarm in Madinah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out, prayed the noon prayer, then walked until he ascended the pulpit, so the people were alarmed at that. When he saw that in their faces he said: O people, I did not come out for a matter to alarm you, but a matter came to me which gladdened me, so I wished to tell you of your Prophet's gladness. Tamim al-Dari told me that some of his cousins sailed the sea, and their ship brought them to an island they did not know, so they went out walking and met a human they could not tell, male or female, for its abundant hair. They said: Who are you? It said: I am al-Jassasah. They said: Tell us. It said: Go to the monastery, for in it is a man eager for you to speak to him. So they entered the monastery, and there was a bound man groaning with severe groaning. He said: Who are you? They said: Of the people of Palestine, of the Arabian Peninsula. He said: Has their Prophet come out yet? They said: Yes. He said: What did he do? They said: Some pledged allegiance to him and some parted from him, then he fought with his companions who pledged allegiance to him until the people of stone and clay yielded to him. He said: What has the Lake of Tiberias done? They said: Full, its sides overflowing. He said: What has the spring of Zughar done? They said: Its sides overflow. He said: What have the palms between Amman and Baysan done? They said: They give food. He said: If I were released from these bonds of mine I would tread the earth except Taybah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is Taybah - twice - Madinah; there is no road in it, nor narrow nor wide place, plain nor rugged, except that an angel with drawn sword stands over it; were he to wish to enter it, he would strike his face with the sword. Amir said: And I met Muharrar ibn Abi Hurayrah and narrated to him, and he said: Did she add anything to it? I said: No. He said: She spoke the truth; I bear witness upon Abu Hurayrah that he narrated to me, and added to it in it. He said: Then he said: The Sea of Sham, what is it? The Sea of Iraq, what is it? Then he gestured with his hand toward the east twenty times. And I met Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr and narrated to him, and he said: Did she add anything to it for you? I said: No. He said: She spoke the truth; I bear witness upon Aishah that she narrated to me, but she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And in Madinah there is in it."
"22627","961 - Abu Muslim al-Kashi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us; and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Mujalid; and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Asim ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Mujalid; and Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Farwah Yazid ibn Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Rahawi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah narrated to me, from Mujalid ibn Sa'id, Amir al-Sha'bi narrated to me, Fatimah bint Qays narrated to me, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out one day, prayed the midday prayer, then sat, and the people were alarmed, so he said: O people, I did not stand in this standing place of mine to alarm you, but Tamim al-Dari came to me and told me a report that kept midday slumber from me along with joy and coolness of eye, so I wished to give you glad tidings of your Prophet's joy. He told me that a party of his cousins sailed the sea, and a storm struck them and drove them to an island, so they sat in the ship's small boat until they came out to the island, and they met a thick-haired very hairy thing, not knowing whether it was a man or a woman, so they greeted it and it greeted them back. They said: Will you not tell us? It said: I shall neither tell you nor ask you, but this monastery which you have seen, in it is one most eager for your news, to tell you and to ask you. We said: What are you? It said: I am al-Jassasah. So they set out until they came to the monastery, and there was a man bound in iron, tightly chained, showing grief, complaining much. They greeted him and he greeted them back, and said: Who are you? They said: From the Arabs. He said: What have the Arabs done, has their Prophet come out yet? They said: Yes. He said: What did they do? We said: Good; they believed in him, followed him and deemed him truthful. He said: That is better for them. They said: And he had enemies, so Allah gave him victory over them. He said: Are the Arabs' God one, their word one, their religion one? They said: Yes. He said: What has the spring of Zughar done? They said: It is overflowing; its people drink its water and water their crops from it. He said: What have the palms between Amman and Baysan done? They said: They yield their harvest every year. He said: What has the Lake of Tiberias done? They said: It is full. Then he panted, then panted, then swore: If I were to come out of this place of mine I would leave no land of Allah's earth untrodden except Taybah; I have no authority over it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is among what gladdened me - he said it three times - Taybah is Madinah, then Allah has forbidden my sanctuary to the Dajjal. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) swore: By Allah, besides whom there is no god, it has no narrow nor wide road, plain nor mountain, except that an angel with drawn sword stands over it until the Day of Resurrection; the Dajjal cannot enter it against its people. Al-Sha'bi said: And I met al-Muharrar ibn Abi Hurayrah and narrated to him the hadith of Fatimah, and he said: I bear witness upon my father that he narrated to me as Fatimah narrated to you, except that he said: He is in the east. Then I met al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, and he said: I bear witness upon Aishah that she narrated to me as Fatimah narrated to you, except that she said: Both sanctuaries are forbidden to him, Makkah and Madinah. And the wording is that of the hadith of Yahya ibn Sa'id, and the others are similar."
"22628","962 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj, Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir, and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Qattan the Egyptians narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Hizami narrated to us, from Abi al-Zinad, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit and said: O people, Tamim al-Dari narrated to me that some people of his people were in the sea in a ship of theirs, and it broke, so some of them rode upon a plank of the ship and came out to an island in the sea, and they met a disheveled black woman with abhorrent hair. They said: What are you? She said: I am al-Jassasah. Do you marvel at me? They said: Yes. She said: Enter the palace. So they entered, and there was an old man bound with chains, and he asked them who they were, so they told him. He said: What has the spring of Zughar done? And what have the lake and the palms of Baysan done? So they told him. Then he said: By Him by whom oaths are sworn, no land shall remain but I shall tread it with my feet except Taybah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And this is Taybah."
"22629","963 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Waddah ibn Yahya al-Nahshali narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us; and Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub told us, both said: Isa ibn Abi Isa al-Hannat narrated to us, he said: I heard Amir al-Sha'bi saying: I entered upon Fatimah bint Qays, and she brought near to me fresh dates of the dates of Ibn Talib, so I ate, and she said: While I was sitting in the mosque, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out, sat on the pulpit, and the people gathered to him. She said: And I called out to hear, and I heard him saying: O people, I did not gather you upon news that came to me from an enemy of yours, but Tamim al-Dari narrated to me that some of his cousins sailed the sea, and a wind struck them so they knew not whether they went east or west, then they anchored at an island and walked about in it, and they met a beast dragging its hair. They said: What is this? It said: I am al-Jassasah. They said: What is the news? It said: The news is with the master of the monastery. So they went to the monastery, and there was the Dajjal, whom they recognized, bound in iron. He said: Who are you? They said: From the community of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And has he been sent? They said: Yes. He said: What has the Tiberian lake done? So they told him about it. He said: What have the palms of Baysan done? So they told him about them. He said: What has the spring of Zughar done? So they told him about it. Then he pointed to his legs and said: You see these two legs of mine; no land of Allah's earth shall remain but I shall tread it with them, except what is of Makkah and Taybah. And he is in the sea between the east and the west, and he is nearer to the east. And the wording of both is one."
"22630","964 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashi narrated to us, both said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abu Umar al-Darir and Abu Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind told us, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays al-Fihriyyah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came one day hastening until he ascended the pulpit, and it was called out among the people: Prayer is gathering. So he addressed them and said: I did not call you for something desired or feared that befell, but Tamim al-Dari told me that some people of the people of Palestine sailed the sea, and the wind cast them upon an island of the islands of the sea, and they met a hairy beast, not knowing whether it was male or female for its abundant hair. They said: What are you? It said: I am al-Jassasah. They said: Tell us. It said: I shall neither tell you nor ask you, but in this monastery is a man most eager for you to tell him and for you to ask him. So they entered the monastery, and there was the man fettered with iron. They said: Who are you? He said: Who are you? They said: We are from the Arabs. He said: Has the Prophet appeared among you? They said: Yes. He said: Have the Arabs followed him? They said: Yes. He said: Yet that is better for them. He said: Has he prevailed over Persia? They said: No. He said: Yet he shall prevail over them. Then he said: What has the spring of Zughar done? They said: It gushes forth full. He said: What has the Lake of Tiberias done? They said: It gushes forth full. He said: What have the palms of Baysan done? They said: Their earliest have yielded. Then he leapt so they thought he would slip out of his shackles, and said to them: I am the Dajjal; I shall tread the whole earth except Makkah and Taybah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rejoice - and he gave the Muslims glad tidings - this is Taybah; he shall not enter it."
"22631","965 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdullah told us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"22632","966 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Umayr ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays al-Fihriyyah, she said: It was called out in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Prayer is gathering, so we went out and sat behind the shoulders of the men. She said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Your brother Tamim al-Dari has narrated to me about some of his cousins who sailed the sea, and the wind carried them until it drove them to an island of the islands of the sea, so they went out asking about the way, and they met a creature of Allah's creation than which they had never seen anything greater; upon it was nothing of what the children of Adam weave, and hair covered it. We asked it about the way, and it said: If you wish to ask about the way of one who will tell you and desires your speech, then go to this monastery. So we said: Tell us, what are you? It said: I am al-Dassasah, so we knew it was a woman. Then we went to the monastery and entered it, and there was a creature than which we had never seen anything greater, filled from his collarbones to his ankles with iron, with effaced eye. So we asked him about the way, and he said: I shall not tell you until you tell me about what I ask you. We said: Ask about whatever you wish. He said: Tell me about the Prophet of the Arabs, has he come out yet? We said: Yes. He said: To what does he call? So we told him. He said: How swift are the people to what he called them to? We said: Swift. He said: That is better for them. He said: Tell me about the Lake of Tiberias, what has it done? We said: It overflows. He said: Tell me about the spring of Zughar? We said: It overflows. He said: Ask about whatever you wish. We said to him: What are you? He said: I am the Dajjal; by Him in whose hand is my soul, no land of Allah's earth shall remain but I shall tread it with these two feet of mine except Taybah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is Taybah, meaning Madinah."
"22633","967 - al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Warraq al-Raqqi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Sha'bi, and Ibrahim ibn Amir, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I entered Madinah and sat by the pulpit, and a man came and sat by me and said: Will you point me to a man who will narrate to me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So he took me to Fatimah bint Qays, and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood upon the pulpit, and the people heard that he had stood upon the pulpit, so the people came hastening, and I was among those who came to him, and I heard him saying: Tamim al-Dari narrated to me that some of his cousins sailed in a ship of theirs in the sea as merchants, and the wind drove them to an island, so they - or those of them who - went out to see whether they saw anyone, until they were met by one covered by hair so it could not be discerned whether male or female. They said: The news. He said: The news is with the master of this monastery; I am al-Jassas. So they came to the monastery, and there was a man laden with iron, so he asked them whence they were, and they told him. He said: What has the Prophet of the Arabs done, has he come out yet? They said: Yes. He said: Who follows him, the lowly or the nobles of the people? They said: The foolish follow him. He said: Do they increase or decrease? They said: They increase. He said: Does anyone who came to him turn back? They said: No. He said: That is better for them. What has the Lake of Tiberias done, is there water in it? They said: Yes. He said: What have the palms of Baysan done, do they bear? They said: Yes. He said: What has the spring of Zughar done, is there water in it? They said: Yes. He said: Yet if I were permitted I would have trodden with this foot of mine the whole earth except Taybah. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And this is Taybah; over every mountain pass are angels guarding it from the Dajjal."
"22634","968 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Habib ibn Bishr, maternal brother of Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, narrated to us, Hammad ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Sayyar Abi al-Hakam, from al-Sha'bi, he said: We entered upon Fatimah bint Qays, and she presented us fresh dates and fed us to satiety sawiq of sult, and said: It was called out among the people: Prayer is gathering, so I set out among those women who set out, and I was in the first row of the women, next to the last row of the men, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Some cousins of Tamim al-Dari sailed in the sea, and their ship cast them upon an island of the islands of the sea, so they saw there a beast hidden by its hair. When the people looked at it, it said: I am al-Jassasah, and in that monastery is one most eager to see you. So the people set out and found a man shackled with iron, contending with them, and it was as though their entering pleased him, so he asked them: Has your companion come out yet? They said: Yes. He said: The Lake of Tiberias, what has it done? We said: Abundant in water. He said: What have the palms of Baysan done? We said: They have yielded. He said: And the spring of Zughar? We said: Abundant in water. He said: Yet if I were to come out I would tread all the lands except Makkah and Taybah. She said: And it is as though I look at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his hand: This is Taybah, gesturing toward Madinah."
"22635","969 - Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Kamil ibn Talhah al-Jahdari narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah narrated to me, from Amir al-Sha'bi, he said: I entered upon Fatimah bint Qays, and she brought near to me dates, so I said: This is indeed good. She said: Who are you? I said: Amir. She said: Al-Sha'bi? I said: Yes. I said: Narrate to me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: He stood one day upon the pulpit, and the people gathered, and he said: O people, no news has come to me from an enemy of yours, but Tamim al-Dari narrated to me that a party of his people sailed the sea, and the wind blew fiercely and drove them to an island, so they landed, and there was a beast dragging its hair. We said: Who are you? It said: I am al-Jassasah and al-Dassasah. It said: Go to that monastery, for there is the news. And there was a nearby monastery. They said: So we set out, and there was the Dajjal. He said: Who are you? They said: From the community of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he rejoiced, and said: Has Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) been sent? Then he asked them about the spring of Zughar and Tiberias, and about the palms of Baysan, then he lifted one of his legs, and they were both fettered, and said: If this were released I would tread the earth with it except Makkah and Madinah."
"22636","970 - Ubayd al-Ijl, Allan ibn Abd al-Samad Maghammah, and al-Haytham ibn Khalaf al-Duri narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn al-Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl narrated to us, Talq ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from Abi Ma'shar Ziyad ibn Kulayb, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us at a time in which he would not usually address us, and said: I have addressed you at this hour only for news that came to me. Tamim al-Dari told me that some of his cousins sailed the sea, and their ship broke upon an island in the sea, and they met a beast. They said: What are you? It said: I am al-Jassasah. And he mentioned the hadith in full."
"22637","971 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: I heard Ghaylan ibn Jarir narrating from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, she said: Tamim al-Dari came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith in full."
"22638","972 - Salamah ibn Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, the hadith in full."
"22639","973 - Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Bakkar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hudhali narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, she said: The caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called: Prayer is gathering, so I went out, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon the pulpit, and he said: O people, I had told you about the Dajjal, and this is Tamim al-Dari telling you. Tamim al-Dari told me that he sailed the sea, and he mentioned the hadith in full."
"22640","974 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Aban ibn Salih al-Tubba'i narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam al-Urani narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi al-Safar narrated to me, Amir al-Sha'bi narrated to us, Fatimah bint Qays, sister of al-Dahhak ibn Qays, narrated to me, and he mentioned the hadith similarly."
"22641","975 - Ahmad ibn Ubaydullah al-Hubayri narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Taymi the judge narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dawud al-Khuraybi narrated to us, from Sa'd al-Iskaf, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a sermon and mentioned the like of it."
"22642","976 - Ahmad ibn Hamdan al-Tustari narrated to us, at Abadan from the original of his book, Ali ibn Harb al-Junday Saburi narrated to us, Ash'ath ibn Attaf narrated to us, Abu Hani Umar ibn Bashir and Abdullah ibn Habib ibn Jurayj al-Absi narrated to us, all of them narrated to me from Amir al-Sha'bi, he said: I entered upon Fatimah bint Qays and asked her about her divorce, and she mentioned that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have no lodging nor maintenance. She said: And the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called: Prayer is gathering, so he ascended the pulpit and said: Tamim al-Dari narrated to me, and he mentioned the hadith of al-Jassasah in full."
"22643","977 - Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Khasib al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jahdami al-Basri narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dawud al-Khuraybi narrated to us, Muti' al-Ghazzal narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us, praised Allah and extolled Him, and mentioned the hadith of al-Jassasah in full."
"22644","978 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Sari ibn Ismail, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, and he mentioned the hadith similarly."
"22645","979 - Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl al-Nakha'i narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abi Hamzah, from al-Sha'bi, from Fatimah bint Qays, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: In your wealth there is a right besides zakat."
"22646","980 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abi Jamrah, similar to it."
"22647","981 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Hurayth ibn Abi Matar, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abi al-Sanabil, from Fatimah bint Qays, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing gold and stringing it, so a woman threw down a bracelet of gold, and it stayed in the mosque for days and no one took it."
"22648","982 - Ahmad ibn Hamdan al-Khallal al-Tustari narrated to us, at Abadan from the original of his book, Ali ibn Harb al-Junday Saburi narrated to us, Ash'ath ibn Attaf narrated to us; and Abu Hani Umar ibn Bashir, Abdullah ibn Habib ibn Abi Thabit, Abu Ajrafah, Hatim Abu Amr al-Tammar, and Habib ibn Jurayy al-Qaysi narrated to us, all of them narrated to me from al-Sha'bi, he said: I entered upon Fatimah bint Qays and asked her about her divorce, and she mentioned that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have no lodging nor maintenance. She said: And the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called: Prayer is gathering, so he ascended the pulpit and said: Tamim al-Dari narrated to me, and he mentioned the hadith of al-Jassasah in full."
"22649","983 - Ahmad ibn Ubaydullah ibn Yusuf al-Hubayri narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Taymi the judge narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Dawud al-Khuraybi narrated to us, from Sa'd al-Iskaf, from Fatimah bint Qays, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he gave a sermon and mentioned the like of the hadith of al-Jassasah in full."
"22650","984 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, Fatimah al-Khuza'iyyah narrated to me, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited an Ansari woman who was ill, and said to her: How do you find yourself? She said: Well, except that Umm Mildam - meaning fever - has afflicted me severely. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be patient, for it removes the filth of the son of Adam as the bellows removes the filth of iron."
"22651","985 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Abi Salih, from Umm Hani, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to me, so I excused myself to him, and he excused me."
"22652","986 - al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Mujashi'i narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Ya'qub al-Kirmani narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, whose name is Salma, narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I used to pass by this verse and not know what it was, His saying: By the afternoon and the sunrise, until Umm Hani bint Abi Talib narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her, called for ablution water in a bowl, and it was as though I look at the trace of dough in it, so he performed ablution, then stood and prayed al-Duha, and said: O Umm Hani, this is the Ishraq prayer."
"22653","987 - Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Iyad ibn Abdullah al-Fihri narrated to me, from Makhramah ibn Sulayman, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one day the Duha supererogatory prayer as eight rak'ahs, giving salams after every two rak'ahs."
"22654","988 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Ufayr narrated to us, Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Iyad ibn Abdullah, from Makhramah ibn Sulayman, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Umm Hani, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of the Conquest bathed, wrapped himself in a garment, and prayed eight rak'ahs."
"22655","989 - Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Iyad ibn Abdullah told me, from Makhramah ibn Sulayman, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Umm Hani bint Abi Talib narrated to me that she gave protection to a man of the polytheists on the day of the Conquest, so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: We have given protection to whom you gave protection, and we have granted safety to whom you granted safety."
"22656","990 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Harun son of the daughter of Umm Hani, from Umm Hani, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her, and a vessel was brought and he drank, so she said: O Messenger of Allah, I was fasting, but I disliked refusing your leftover. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If it was making up a Ramadan fast, then make it up another day, and if it was voluntary, then make it up, and if you wish then do not make it up."
"22657","991 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; and Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh and Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, both said: Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, both said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ibn Umm Hani, from Umm Hani, she said: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and drink was brought and he drank from it, then handed it to me and I drank from it, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed a sin, so seek forgiveness for me. He said: And what is it? I said: I was fasting and broke my fast. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Was it a make-up fast you were observing? She said: No. He said: Then it does not harm you."
"22658","992 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ibn Umm Hani, from Umm Hani, she said: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and drink was brought and he drank from it, then handed it to me and I drank from it, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I fear I have done something wrong. He said: And what is it? She said: I was fasting, but I disliked refusing your hand, so I drank. He said: Was it a fast you were making up? She said: No. He said: Then it does not harm you."
"22659","993 - al-Haytham ibn Khalid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ibn Umm Hani, from his grandmother Umm Hani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought drink on the day of the conquest of Makkah, so he drank from it, then handed it to me and I drank, though I was fasting, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I drank though I was fasting. He said: Were you making up anything for yourself? I said: No. He said: Then it does not harm you."
"22660","994 - Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Nawfali, Musa ibn Harun, and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, they said: Abu Mus'ab al-Zubayri narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Thabit, one of the Banu Abd al-Dar ibn Qusayy, narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Atiq, from Sa'id ibn Amr ibn Ja'dah, from his father, from his grandmother Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah favored Quraysh with seven traits which He gave to none before them nor shall give to any after them: Allah favored Quraysh that I am of them, for prophethood is among them, and the custodianship of the Ka'bah is among them, and the providing of water to pilgrims is among them, and He aided them against the Elephant, and they worshipped Allah for ten years when none but they worshipped Him, and Allah sent down concerning them a surah of the Quran which was not sent down concerning any but them."
"22661","995 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Mus'ab al-Zubayri narrated to us; and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Makhlad ibn Malik al-Harrani narrated to us, both said: Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Amr ibn Ja'dah ibn Hubayrah narrated to us, from Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, who is his grandmother, she said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I used to pray a prayer which has become heavy for me, so direct me to a deed I can do for which Allah will reward me while I am sitting. He said: O Umm Hani, when you wake in the morning, glorify Allah a hundred times, declare His oneness a hundred times, praise Him a hundred times, and magnify Him a hundred times; for a hundred glorifications are like a hundred sacrificial camels, and a hundred magnification are like a hundred sacrificial camels you gift, and a hundred declarations of oneness leave no sin before them nor after them."
"22662","996 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Thabit ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Yahya ibn Ja'dah, from Umm Hani, that she entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Makkah, and he brought her drink, drank from it and gave her to drink. She said: I was fasting, but I disliked refusing your drink. He said: Were you making up a fast? I said: No. He said: It does not harm you."
"22663","997 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Mis'ar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Abi al-Ala, from Yahya ibn Ja'dah, he said: Umm Hani said: I used to hear the voice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was upon my trellis - meaning his recitation in the night prayer. And Abu al-Ala from whom Mis'ar narrated this hadith is Hilal ibn Khabbab."
"22664","998 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from a man, from Yahya ibn Ja'dah, from Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, she said: I used to hear the recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was upon my trellis praying."
"22665","999 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Khabbab, from Yahya ibn Ja'dah, from Umm Hani, she said: I used to hear the recitation of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) repeating it in the depth of the night while I was reclining upon my trellis."
"22666","1000 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim and Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, both said: Sa'id ibn Zayd narrated to us, Abu Yunus al-Qushayri narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Badham Abi Salih, freedman of Umm Hani, that Umm Hani said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this verse: And you commit evil in your assemblies. He said: They used to sit on the road, pelt the wayfarer, and mock them."
"22667","1001 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us; and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, both said: Hatim ibn Abi Saghir narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to me, Abu Salih, freedman of Umm Hani, narrated to us, Umm Hani narrated to me that she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about this verse, and he mentioned the like of it."
"22668","1002 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abi Salih, from Umm Hani, she said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about His saying: And you commit evil in your assemblies. He said: They used to pelt whoever passed by them on the road and mock him."
"22669","1003 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, both said: Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us; and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' and Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Abi Salih, from Umm Hani, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me on the day of the conquest of Makkah, bathed, then prayed eight rak'ahs which he had not prayed before that day nor after it."
"22670","1004 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Abi Salih, from Umm Hani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he conquered Makkah, was brought water, so they screened him and he bathed, then prayed eight rak'ahs which no one saw him pray thereafter."
"22671","1005 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Anbasah ibn al-Azhar, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Abi Salih, from Umm Hani, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to me, but I was not lawful to him because I had not emigrated, so there was sent down: And the daughters of your paternal uncles and the daughters of your paternal aunts and the daughters of your maternal uncles and the daughters of your maternal aunts who emigrated with you."
"22672","1006 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abi Salih, from Umm Hani, she said: I never saw the belly of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except that I remembered folded sheets, some upon others."
"22673","1007 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; and Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, both said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Israil, from al-Suddi, from Abi Salih, from Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to me, so I excused myself to him and he excused me, then Allah sent down: Indeed We have made lawful to you your wives, up to His saying: And the daughters of your maternal aunts who emigrated with you. So I was not lawful to him; I had not emigrated with him; I was of the freed ones."
"22674","1008 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us, Musa ibn Khalaf al-Ammi narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us, from Abi Salih, freedman of Umm Hani, from Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me one day, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have grown old, so command me with a deed I can do while sitting. He said: Glorify Allah a hundred glorifications, for they equal a hundred necks of the children of Ismail; and praise Allah a hundred praises, for they equal a hundred bridled saddled horses you carry upon in the path of Allah; and magnify Allah a hundred magnifications, for they equal a hundred accepted sacrificial camels; and declare Allah's oneness a hundred declarations, for they fill what is between heaven and earth, and no one's deed shall be raised better than them except one who brings the like of what you brought."
"22675","1009 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr told us, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn, from Abi Murrah, freedman of Umm Hani, from Umm Hani, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me on the day of the Conquest, bathed and prayed, covered in a single garment, eight rak'ahs. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I gave protection to my in-laws, and the son of my mother claims he will kill them - meaning Ali - so he said: O Umm Hani, we have given protection to whom you gave protection."
"22676","1010 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Husayn narrated to me, from Abi Murrah, freedman of Umm Hani, from Umm Hani, that she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Conquest and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have given protection to my in-laws, and the son of my mother - meaning Ali - claims he will kill them. He said: O Umm Hani, we have given protection to whom you gave protection. Then water was poured for him, then he was screened, bathed, then wrapped a garment with its two ends upon his shoulders, then prayed the noon prayer as four rak'ahs."
"22677","1011 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr told us, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn, from Abi Murrah, freedman of Aqil ibn Abi Talib, from Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, she said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Conquest and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have given protection to my in-laws, and the son of my mother claims he will kill them - meaning Ali - so he said: We have given protection to whom you gave protection, O Umm Hani. Muhammad said: And I saw Abu Murrah."
"22678","1012 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn, from Abi Murrah, from Umm Hani, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed at her house in the year of the Conquest. She said: So I entered upon him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have given protection to two men; Ali ibn Abi Talib claims he will kill my in-laws and violate my protection. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have given protection to whom you gave protection. Then he prayed al-Duha as eight rak'ahs in a single garment, crossing its two ends."
"22679","1013 - Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abi Murrah, freedman of Aqil, from Umm Hani, she said: I gave protection to two in-law men of mine of the polytheists, then Ali ibn Abi Talib came to me and rushed at them to kill them, and said: Do you give protection to polytheists? So I said: By Allah, you shall not kill them until you begin with me before them. Then he left, so I said: Close the door against him. Then I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the lower mountain pass, but did not find him, and found Fatimah, who was harsher to me than her husband, and said: Why do you give protection to polytheists? Until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appeared, wearing a single garment, and said: Welcome to Fakhitah Umm Hani. So I said: What I met from the son of my mother: I gave protection to two in-law men of mine of the polytheists, and he rushed at them to kill them. He said: He had no right to that; we have given protection to whom you gave protection, and granted safety to whom you granted safety."
"22680","1014 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us; and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, both said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abi Murrah, freedman of Aqil, he said: I heard Umm Hani saying: When it was the day of the Conquest, my two in-laws came to me and I granted them safety, then Ali ibn Abi Talib came wanting to kill them, so I went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have given protection to whom you gave protection, and granted safety to whom you granted safety. Then he ordered Fatimah, so she poured his bath water for him, then he was screened and bathed, stood and prayed al-Duha as eight rak'ahs in a single garment, crossing its two ends. I never saw him pray before nor after."
"22681","1015 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abi Murrah, freedman of Aqil ibn Abi Talib, from Umm Hani, she said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Conquest but did not find him, so I waited for him until he entered. I said: The son of my mother entered upon me - meaning Ali ibn Abi Talib - and wanted to kill my two in-laws the sons of Hubayrah. I said: I have given them protection. He said: That is not yours, that you give protection to polytheists? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have given protection to whom you gave protection. Then he said: O Fatimah, pour water for me, so he bathed. Then he prayed eight rak'ahs in a single garment, having crossed its two ends."
"22682","1016 - Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abi Murrah, freedman of Aqil, from Umm Hani, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her on the day of the Conquest, bathed, and prayed al-Duha as eight rak'ahs in a single garment, having crossed its two ends. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have given protection to my two in-laws the sons of Hubayrah, and the son of my mother claims he will kill them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have given protection to whom Umm Hani gave protection."
"22683","1017 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik; and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Malik told us; and Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Malik narrated to me, from Abi al-Nadr, freedman of Umar ibn Ubaydullah, that Abu Murrah, freedman of Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, told him that he heard Umm Hani bint Abi Talib saying: I went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of the Conquest and found him bathing, with Fatimah screening him with a garment, so I greeted him. He said: Who is this? I said: I am Umm Hani bint Abi Talib. He said: Welcome to Umm Hani. When he finished his bath he stood and prayed eight rak'ahs wrapped in a single garment. When he finished I said: O Messenger of Allah, the son of my mother claims he will kill a man I gave protection to, so-and-so son of Hubayrah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have given protection to whom you gave protection, O Umm Hani. Umm Hani said: And that was in the forenoon."
"22684","1018 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Malik, from Maymun ibn Maysarah, from Abi Murrah, freedman of Umm Hani, he said: I heard her saying: I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"22685","1019 in abridged chain - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik; and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Malik told us; and Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Musa ibn Maysarah, from Abi Murrah, freedman of Aqil, from Umm Hani, she said: I went to the Messenger of Allah on the day of the Conquest and found him bathing, with Fatimah his daughter screening him with a garment, so I greeted, and that was in the forenoon. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is this? I said: Umm Hani bint Abi Talib. He said: Welcome to Umm Hani. When he finished his bath he prayed eight rak'ahs wrapped in a single garment, then finished. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the son of my mother claims he will kill so-and-so son of Hubayrah, a man I gave protection to. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have given protection to whom Umm Hani gave protection. Thus al-Dabari said, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Malik, from Maymun ibn Maysarah, and he erred in it; and the correct is what al-Qa'nabi and others narrated, from Malik, from Musa ibn Maysarah."
"22686","1020 - al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, that Abu Murrah, freedman of Aqil, narrated to him that Umm Hani bint Abi Talib narrated to him that when it was the day of the Conquest, two men of Banu Makhzum fled to her and she gave them protection. Ali entered upon me and said: I shall surely kill them. When I heard him say that I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at the upper part of Makkah. When he saw me he welcomed me and said: What has brought you, O Umm Hani? I said: O Prophet of Allah, I had granted safety to two men of my in-laws, and Ali wants to kill them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have given protection to whom you gave protection. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to his bath, Fatimah screened for him, then he took his garment, wrapped himself in it, and prayed eight rak'ahs, the Duha supererogatory prayer."
"22687","1021 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, from Abi Murrah, freedman of Aqil, from Umm Hani, she said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Makkah, two men of my in-laws of Banu Makhzum fled to me, so I hid them in my house. My brother entered upon me and said: I shall surely kill them. So I locked the door upon them, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him. He said: We have given protection to whom you gave protection, and granted safety to whom you granted safety."
"22688","1022 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Sa'id narrated to me, from Abi Murrah, freedman of Aqil, that Umm Hani bint Abi Talib said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) camped at the upper part of Makkah, two men of my in-laws of Banu Makhzum came to me - and she was under Hubayrah ibn Abi Wahb. She said: Ali ibn Abi Talib entered upon me and said: I shall surely kill them. So I locked my door upon them, then came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the upper part of Makkah, and found him bathing in a bowl in which was the trace of dough, with Fatimah his daughter screening him with a garment. When he bathed he took his garment and wrapped himself in it, then prayed eight rak'ahs in the forenoon, then turned to me and said: Welcome and greetings, O Umm Hani, what has brought you? So I told him the news of the two men and the news of Ali. He said: We have given protection to whom you gave protection."
"22689","1023 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki and Mas'adah ibn Sa'd al-Attar narrated to us, both said: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, that Abu Murrah, freedman of Aqil ibn Abi Talib, told him that Umm Hani told him: She came with two men of Banu Makhzum on the day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Makkah, then Ali entered upon her and said: What is this, O Umm Hani? I shall surely kill them. She said: So I locked them in, then went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and found him bathing with his daughter Fatimah screening him with a garment. He bathed, then took the garment and wrapped himself in it, then prayed al-Duha as eight rak'ahs, then said: What is wrong with you, O Umm Hani? I said: I gave protection to two men of my in-laws, then Ali came wanting to kill them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have granted safety to whom you granted safety, and given protection to whom you gave protection."
"22690","1024 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salim al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Junadah ibn Salm narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Abi Murrah, freedman of Umm Hani, he said: I heard Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, who is Ali's full sister by his father and mother, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me on the day of the Conquest, bathed, then prayed eight rak'ahs."
"22691","1025 - Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Abi Murrah, freedman of Aqil, from Umm Hani, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her on the day of the Conquest and prayed al-Duha as eight rak'ahs in a single garment."
"22692","1026 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Umm Hani - and he was staying with her - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Conquest was screened, bathed in the forenoon, and prayed eight rak'ahs; one knows not whether his standing was longer or his bowing or his prostration."
"22693","1027 - Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Yahya narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us; and al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to me; and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, he said: I sought to find anyone to tell me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) glorified Allah in voluntary prayer while traveling, but found no one to tell me until Umm Hani bint Abi Talib told me: He stood on the day of the Conquest, ordered a screen, was screened, bathed, then glorified Allah with eight rak'ahs."
"22694","1028 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Qurrah ibn Abd al-Rahman, and Uqayl ibn Khalid, from Ibn Shihab, Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated to me that his father Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal said: I asked and was keen to find anyone of the people to tell me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the Duha prayer, until I heard Umm Hani saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came after the day had risen on the day of the Conquest, ordered a garment, was screened with it, bathed, then stood and bowed eight rak'ahs; I know not whether his standing therein was longer or his bowing or his prostration; all of that was close together, and I never saw him glorify it before nor after."
"22695","1029 - Harun ibn Kamil al-Misri narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Yunus; and Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Anbasah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal narrated to me, from his father, he said: I asked and was keen to find anyone to tell me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) glorified the Duha glorification, but found no one to narrate to me but Umm Hani bint Abi Talib. She told me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came after the day had risen on the day of the Conquest, ordered a garment, was screened with it, bathed, then stood and bowed eight rak'ahs; I know not whether his standing was longer or his bowing or his prostration; all of that was close together, and I never saw him glorify it before nor after."
"22696","1030 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, he said: I asked in the time of Uthman ibn Affan about the Duha prayer, whether the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed it. I saw no one claiming he saw him do that except Umm Hani, for she claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Fatimah while she was with her on Friday, the day of the conquest of Makkah, poured water over himself, then prayed eight rak'ahs which we never saw him pray before nor after."
"22697","1031 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, he said: I met the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked them about the Duha prayer, but found no one to narrate to me about it until I came to Umm Hani bint Abi Talib and asked her. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the house of Fatimah in Makkah on Friday, called for a handful of water, poured it, then bathed, with Fatimah screening him, and prayed eight rak'ahs which he had not prayed before them nor after them."
"22698","1032 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, he said: Umm Hani told me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed al-Duha at the upper part of Makkah as eight rak'ahs."
"22699","1033 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, he said: Umm Hani told me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he conquered Makkah, I entered upon him, I and Fatimah, and Fatimah screened him, so he bathed, then prayed al-Duha as eight rak'ahs."
"22700","1034 - Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Abi Ayyub, from Abi Safwan, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Umm Hani, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me on the day of the Conquest in my house, ordered water, so it was poured into a bowl, then ordered a garment and was screened, then bathed, then sprinkled a side of the house, then prayed eight rak'ahs whose standing, bowing, prostration and sitting were equal, close to one another."
"22701","1035 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Mujammi', from Abd al-Karim ibn Abi al-Mukhariq, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, he said: I entered upon Umm Hani and she narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the Duha prayer. So I went out, met Ibn Abbas, and said: Come to Umm Hani. So we entered upon her, and I said: Narrate to your cousin about the Duha prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So she narrated to him, and he said: We interpret this verse as the Ishraq prayer, and it is the Duha prayer."
"22702","1036 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Umm Hani, she said: When it was the day of the conquest of Makkah, Fatimah came and sat to the left of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with Umm Hani to his right, and a vessel with drink was brought and he drank from it, then handed it to Umm Hani and she drank from it, then she said: O Messenger of Allah, I have broken my fast though I was fasting. He said: Were you making up anything? I said: No. He said: Then it does not harm you if it was voluntary."
"22703","1037 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Sha'ir narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Makhul mentioned, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, that she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was judging between the people, and he kept judging between them until the day had risen, then stood and prayed al-Duha as eight rak'ahs."
"22704","1038 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Uthman narrated to us, Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Abbad narrated to us, Ibn Thawban narrated to us, from his father, from Makhul, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Umm Hani, similar to it."
"22705","1039 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Umm Hani, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) camped at the upper part of Makkah on the day of the Conquest, so I came to him, and Abu Dharr came with a bowl with water in it. She said: I could see in it the trace of dough. So Abu Dharr screened him and he bathed, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) screened Abu Dharr and he bathed, then he prayed eight rak'ahs, and that was in the forenoon."
"22706","1040 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, both said: Waki' narrated to us; and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah and Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Umm Hani, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take sheep, for in them is blessing."
"22707","1041 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Umm Hani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take sheep, for in them is blessing."
"22708","1042 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Umm Hani, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Take something of sheep. I said: No. He said: Take them, for in them is blessing."
"22709","1043 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Ata told me, from Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, she said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Conquest while he was in a tent of his, and found him bathing with water that was in a tray; I could see in it the trace of dough, and found him praying in the forenoon."
"22710","1044 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, she said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Makkah, screened with a garment while bathing in a bowl in which was the trace of dough. When he finished his bath he prayed al-Duha."
"22711","1045 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, he said: Umm Hani told me, she said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was bathing, screened with a garment. When he finished his bath he prayed al-Duha."
"22712","1046 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata, from Umm Hani, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me on the day of the Conquest, and I said: Will you not excuse me concerning Ali? He said: What is wrong with him? I said: A man came to me and sought refuge with me, and Ali said: Step aside from me or I shall pierce you with the spear, and he struck me on the front of my head. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ali would not strike you."
"22713","1047 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Mahak narrated to me that he entered upon Umm Hani bint Abi Talib and asked her about the entry of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Conquest. She said: He entered in the forenoon, so we poured water for him in a tray of ours; I could see in it the grease of dough - Yusuf said: I know not which of the two she told me: whether he performed ablution or bathed - then he bowed in this mosque, of a mosque in her house, four rak'ahs."
"22714","1048 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Shafi'i narrated to us, my uncle Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafi'i narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Umm Hani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"22715","1049 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Umm Hani, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with four braids."
"22716","1050 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, both said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Umm Hani, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us in Makkah with four plaits."
"22717","1051 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Umm Hani, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with four plaits."
"22718","1052 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us; and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah and Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, both said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, both said: Ibrahim ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Umm Hani, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bathed, he and Maymunah, in one vessel, in a bowl in which was the trace of dough."
"22719","1053 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated to us, Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Umm Hani, she said: When it was the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for water, and Umm Hani, Umm Sulaym, and Umm Anas ibn Malik were screened with a sheet, then he entered the house of Umm Hani and prayed al-Duha as four rak'ahs."
"22720","1054 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Harrani narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Umm Hani, she said: When it was the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for water, and Umm Hani and Umm Salamah screened him, so he bathed and prayed al-Duha as eight rak'ahs."
"22721","1055 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Mujahid, from Umm Hani, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in Makkah two rak'ahs and four, and did not repeat them."
"22722","1056 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Abi Ma'shar, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, that Umm Hani came with two men, and Ali wanted to kill them, so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: We have given protection to whom Umm Hani gave protection."
"22723","1057 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Kathir, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, that Umm Hani bint Abi Talib narrated to him that Ali ibn Abi Talib entered upon her in the campaign of the Conquest in Makkah and found with me two men of my husband's family who had fled to me, and wanted to kill them. When I saw that I locked my door upon them, then went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at the upper part of Makkah. When he saw me he welcomed me and said: What has brought you, O Umm Hani? I said: O Messenger of Allah, two men of my husband's family sought refuge with me, and Ali found them with me and claims he will kill them, so I came to you concerning that. He said: We have given protection to whom you gave protection, and granted safety to whom you granted safety. Then I poured water for him and he bathed, Fatimah his daughter screened him with a garment. When he bathed he took it and cast it aside, then stood and prayed eight prostrations, and that was in the forenoon."
"22724","1058 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Umm Hani, she narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her on the day of the Conquest and prayed al-Duha as four rak'ahs."
"22725","1059 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Umm Hani, that he - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - ate a shoulder, then prayed, and did not perform ablution."
"22726","1060 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muzakki narrated to us; and al-Qasim ibn Abbad al-Khattabi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Buhlul al-Anbari narrated to us, my father narrated to us; and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Rizqullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Shabbabah ibn Sawwar narrated to us, they said: Abd al-A'la ibn Abi al-Musawir narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spent the night in which he was taken by night in my house, and I missed him in the night, so sleep was kept from me fearing that some of Quraysh had confronted him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril came to me, took my hand and brought me out, and upon the house was a beast smaller than a mule and larger than a donkey, so he carried me upon it, then set out until he brought me to Bayt al-Maqdis. He showed me Ibrahim, whose build resembles my build and my build resembles his; he showed me Musa, tall, lank-haired, I likened him to the men of Azd Shanuah; he showed me Isa son of Maryam, of medium stature, fair inclining to redness, I likened him to Urwah ibn Mas'ud al-Thaqafi; and he showed me the Dajjal, with effaced right eye, I likened him to Qatan ibn Abd al-Uzza. And I wish to go out to Quraysh and tell them what I saw. So I took his garment and said: I remind you by Allah that you will come to a people who will drive you away and deny your saying, and I fear they will assault you. She said: So he pulled his garment from my hand, then went out to them, came to them while they were sitting, and told them what he told me. Then Jubayr ibn Mut'im stood and said: O Muhammad, had you been young as you were you would not have spoken this while among us. A man of the people said: O Muhammad, did you pass by camels of ours in such-and-such place? He said: Yes, by Allah, I found them having lost a camel of theirs and seeking it. He said: Did you pass by camels of so-and-so's sons? He said: Yes, in such-and-such place; a red she-camel of theirs had broken, so I found them, and with them was a bowl of water, so I drank what was in it. They said: Tell us their number and what herdsmen are in them. He said: I was distracted from their number. Then he stood, the camels were brought, so he counted them and knew what herdsmen were in them, then came to Quraysh and said: You asked me about the camels of so-and-so's sons, and they are such-and-such, with such-and-such herdsmen among them, and you asked me about the camels of so-and-so's sons, and they are such-and-such, with Ibn Abi Quhafah and so-and-so among the herdsmen, and they will meet you in the morning at the mountain pass. He said: So they went in the morning to the pass to see whether what he said was true, met the camels, and asked: Did a camel of yours stray? They said: Yes. Then they asked the other: Did a red she-camel of yours break? They said: Yes. They said: Was there a bowl with you? Abu Bakr said: By Allah, I placed it, and none drank it nor spilled it on the ground. And Abu Bakr deemed him truthful and believed in him, so he was named al-Siddiq that day."
"22727","1061 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Rafi', that Umm Hani bint Abi Talib went out adorned with her earrings showing, so Umar ibn al-Khattab said to her: Know that Muhammad will avail you nothing. So she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is wrong with people who claim that my intercession will not reach my household, when my intercession will reach Ha and Hukm."
"22728","1062 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Abi Maryam, from Salih, freedman of Wajzah, from Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, she said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who has grown heavy, so teach me something to say while I am sitting. He said: Say: Allah is Greatest a hundred times, for it is better for you than a hundred garlanded accepted sacrificial camels; and say: Glory be to Allah a hundred times, for it is better for you than a hundred saddled bridled horses you carry upon in the path of Allah; and say: Praise be to Allah a hundred times, for it is better for you than a hundred necks you free of the children of Ismail; and say: There is no god but Allah a hundred times; they leave no sin, and no deed precedes them."
"22729","1063 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i the judge narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Faid al-Attar narrated to us, from Dhakwan Abi Salih, from Umm Hani, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The forerunners are four: I am the forerunner of the Arabs, Salman is the forerunner of Persia, Suhayb is the forerunner of Rome, and Bilal is the forerunner of Abyssinia."
"22730","1064 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Humayd al-Tawil narrating, from Muhammad ibn Qays, from Umm Hani, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her on the day of the Conquest and prayed al-Duha as six rak'ahs."
"22731","1065 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Qays, storyteller of Ibn Abd al-Aziz, told us, from Umm Hani, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed al-Duha in my house on the day of the Conquest as eight rak'ahs."
"22732","1066 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Humayd, from Abi Ishaq al-Hamdani, from al-Asbagh ibn Nubatah, from Umm Hani, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, and said: Why do I see no blessings with you? I said: And which blessings do you mean? He said: Allah sent down three blessings: the sheep, the palm tree, and fire."
"22733","1067 - Abu Muslim al-Kashi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi and Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, both said: Shu'bah narrated to us; and Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla saying: No one told us that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying al-Duha except Umm Hani, for she mentioned that on the day of the conquest of Makkah he bathed in her house and prayed eight rak'ahs; I never saw him pray a prayer lighter than it, except that he completed its bowing and prostration."
"22734","1068 - al-Abbas ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Aqil al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Ismail al-Mu'addib narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to me, and I said: I have no aversion to you, O Messenger of Allah, but I do not wish to marry while my children are small. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why? The best women who rode camels are the women of Quraysh, most tender to a child in his childhood, and most caring for a husband in his means."
"22735","1069 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Thabit al-Thumali, from al-Sha'bi, from Umm Hani, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me and said: Have you anything? I said: No, except dry crumbs and vinegar. He said: No household is poor that has vinegar as condiment."
"22736","1070 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abi Fakhitah, Umm Hani narrated to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was gifted a striped silk robe, so he sent it to Ali, and Ali went out wearing it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: I am not pleased for you with what I am not pleased with for myself; I did not clothe you with it to wear it, I only clothed you with it to make it headscarves among the Fatimahs."
"22737","1071 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ammi narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from Sa'id, from Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me on the day of the conquest of Makkah covered with dust, ordered a bowl, and it was as though I look at the trace of dough, so I poured into it, he ordered a garment between me and him and was screened, stood and poured water over himself, then stood and prayed al-Duha as eight rak'ahs. Mujahid said: So I narrated this hadith to Ibn Abbas, and he said: It is the Ishraq prayer."
"22738","1072 - Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub and Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Duwayd ibn Abi Duwayd, from Umm Hani, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, I have grown old and weak, so teach me a supplication I may attain thereby. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Umm Hani, if you glorify Allah a hundred times it shall be better than a hundred necks you free; and if you praise Allah a hundred times it shall be better than a hundred horses you carry upon in the path of Allah; and if you declare Allah's oneness a hundred times no deed shall precede it, and no sin shall remain with it."
"22739","1073 - Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abi al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he heard Durrah bint Mu'adh narrating, from Umm Hani, that she asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Shall we visit one another when we die, and shall some of us see others? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Souls shall be birds clinging to trees, until when it is the Day of Resurrection every soul shall enter its body."
"22740","1074 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ma'mar ibn Bakkar al-Sa'di narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I gifted to my maternal aunt Fakhitah bint Amr a slave boy, and ordered her not to make him a butcher, nor a goldsmith, nor a cupper."
"22741","1075 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from a son of Ka'b ibn Ujrah, my paternal aunt narrated to me - and she was the sister of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri - that Furay'ah bint Malik narrated to her that her husband went out seeking runaway non-Arab slaves until, when he was at the edge of al-Qadum - a mountain - they overtook them and they killed him. So she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), mentioned to him that her husband was killed and that he left her in a dwelling not his, and sought permission to move. So he permitted her. Then she set out until, when she was at the door of the chamber, he ordered her brought back, ordered her to repeat her story to him, so she did, and he ordered her not to leave her husband's house until the decree reaches its term."
"22742","1076 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Salimi narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways al-A'sha narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Atiq, and Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, that Sa'd ibn Ishaq ibn Ka'b ibn Ujrah told him, from his paternal aunt Zaynab bint Ka'b ibn Malik, from Furay'ah bint Malik, sister of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, she told her that she was under a man of Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, and he went out seeking runaway non-Arab slaves of his, overtook them at the edge of al-Qadum, and they assaulted him and killed him. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Until the decree reaches its term."
"22743","1077 - Idris ibn Ja'far al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id told us, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq, with its chain, similar to it."
"22744","1078 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq ibn Ka'b ibn Ujrah, from his paternal aunt Zaynab bint Ka'b ibn Ujrah, from Furay'ah bint Malik - Hammad said: And I heard it from Sa'd ibn Ishaq - that her husband went out seeking a slave boy of his and was killed at the edge of al-Qadum. So she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sought his permission to move to her family. So he permitted her. When she turned away he called her and said: Remain in your house until the decree reaches its term."
"22745","1079 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; and Abu Muslim al-Kashi narrated to us, Ibn Aishah narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id told us, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq ibn Ka'b ibn Ujrah, from his paternal aunt Zaynab bint Ka'b, that Furay'ah bint Malik, sister of Abu Sa'id, her husband was afflicted at the edge of al-Qadum. So she sought the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permission to go to her family in Madinah. So he permitted her, then said: No, until the decree reaches its term."
"22746","1080 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq told me, Ibn Jurayj told us, Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr told me that Sa'd ibn Ishaq ibn Ka'b ibn Ujrah, from his paternal aunt Zaynab bint Ka'b ibn Ujrah, that Furay'ah bint Malik, sister of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, told her: A husband of hers went out until, when he was six miles from Madinah at the edge of a mountain called al-Qadum, robbers assaulted him and killed him. And Furay'ah was among Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj in a dwelling not her husband's; it was only a lodging. So her brothers came, among them Abu Sa'id, and said: We have no means to give you and keep you, and we are only right if we are together, and we fear loneliness for you. So ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sought his permission to be with them. He said: Do so if you wish. Then she turned away until, when she was in the chamber, he said: Come, repeat what you said. So she returned, and he said: Remain in your dwelling until the decree reaches its term."
"22747","1081 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Sa'd ibn Ishaq ibn Ka'b ibn Ujrah narrated to us, from Furay'ah bint Malik, sister of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that her husband went out seeking non-Arab slaves of his and was killed at the outskirts of al-Qadum. So she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), mentioned to him her circumstance, and mentioned to him moving to her brothers. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted her. When she turned away he called her and said: Remain in your house until the decree reaches its term: four months and ten days."
"22748","1082 - Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Sa'd ibn Ishaq ibn Ka'b ibn Ujrah - or Ishaq ibn Sa'd, Shu'bah doubted - narrated to me that he heard his paternal aunt Zaynab narrating, from Furay'ah, that she was with her husband in a village of the villages of Madinah, and he followed non-Arab slaves and they killed him. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), mentioned to him the loneliness, and mentioned that she was in a house not hers, and that she sought permission to go to her brothers in Madinah. So he permitted her, then called her back and said: Remain in your house in which his death news came to you until the decree reaches its term."
"22749","1083 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim ibn Ka'b ibn Ujrah, from his paternal aunt Zaynab bint Ka'b ibn Ujrah, from Furay'ah bint Malik, that her husband was killed at al-Qadum. She said: So she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Her husband was killed at al-Qadum, and she has family. So he ordered her to move. When she turned away he called her and said: Remain in your house until the decree reaches its term: four months and ten days."
"22750","1084 - Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq ibn Ka'b ibn Ujrah, from his paternal aunt Zaynab, from Furay'ah, this hadith."
"22751","1085 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq ibn Ka'b ibn Ujrah, from his paternal aunt Zaynab bint Ka'b, from Furay'ah, sister of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, she said: My husband set out seeking non-Arab slaves until, when he was at the edge of al-Qadum, they caught up with him and killed him. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My husband was killed at the edge of al-Qadum, and my husband left me neither dwelling nor wealth, and I wish to move to my brothers so our affair is more united. She said: So he permitted me. Then I went out until, when I was at part of the chamber, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me and said: Remain in the house in which your husband's death news came to you until the decree reaches its term."
"22752","1086 - al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Muhammad, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq ibn Ka'b ibn Ujrah, from his paternal aunt Zaynab bint Ka'b, from al-Furay'ah bint Malik, sister of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that her husband Bakkar hired non-Arabs to work for him, and they killed him. So she mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: I am not in a dwelling of his, nor does any provision flow to me from him, so shall I move to my family and my orphans and take charge of them? He said: Do so. Then it occurred to him, and he said: Observe your waiting period where the news reached you."
"22753","1087 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim narrated to us, both said: al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik; and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Malik told us, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq ibn Ka'b ibn Ujrah, from his paternal aunt Zaynab bint Ka'b, from Furay'ah bint Malik, that her husband was afflicted at the edge of al-Qadum. So she sought the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permission to go to her family, then he said: No, until the decree reaches its term."
"22754","1088 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq ibn Ka'b ibn Ujrah, Zaynab bint Ka'b narrated to me, from Furay'ah bint Malik, she said: My husband went out seeking non-Arab slaves of ours, overtook them at the edge of al-Qadum, and they killed him. His death news came to me while I was in a house far from my family's houses. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sought his permission to go to my family. So he permitted me, then said: No, until the decree reaches its term."
"22755","1089 - Yusuf the judge narrated to us, Abu al-Khattab Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman narrated to us, Sa'd ibn Ishaq ibn Ka'b ibn Ujrah narrated to us, Zaynab bint Ka'b ibn Ujrah narrated to me, from Furay'ah bint Malik, that she told him: Her husband went out seeking non-Arab slaves of his until, when he was at the edge of al-Qadum, they killed him. The news reached her while she was in a house far from her family. So he permitted her. When she reached the chamber he brought her back and said: Remain where the news came to you until the decree reaches its term."
"22756","1090 - al-Hadrami narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq ibn Ka'b ibn Ujrah, from Zaynab bint Ka'b, from Furay'ah bint Malik, that her husband went out seeking non-Arab slaves of his, and he mentioned the hadith."
"22757","1091 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq ibn Ka'b, from Furay'ah bint Malik, that her husband went out seeking non-Arab slaves of his, and he mentioned the like of it."
"22758","1092 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad, Anas ibn Iyad, and Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq ibn Ka'b ibn Ujrah, my paternal aunt Zaynab bint Ka'b told me, from Furay'ah bint Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"22759","1093 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Mas'ud Ahmad ibn al-Furat narrated to us, Hammad ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq, from his paternal aunt Zaynab, from Furay'ah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"22760","1094 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, Hind bint Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri narrated to me, from her paternal aunt, that she saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat bread and meat, pray, and not perform ablution."
"22761","1095 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to me, Amr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Mu'adh al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: I heard Hind bint Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri narrating, from her paternal aunt, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came visiting Abu Sa'id al-Khudri when ill, so we presented to him a foreleg of sheep, so he ate, and prayer came, so he rinsed his mouth, then stood and prayed, and did not perform ablution."
"22762","1096 - Mus'ab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad, from Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd, from Hind bint Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from her paternal aunt, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited them, ate a sheep shoulder, then prayed, and did not perform ablution."
"22763","Chapter of Qaf: Qaylah bint Makhramah al-Anbariyyah. 1 - Abu Muslim al-Kashi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar Abu Umar al-Darir al-Hawdi narrated to us; and Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab Abu Khalifah narrated to us, both said: Abdullah ibn Sawwar ibn Qudamah ibn Anazah al-Anbari narrated to us; and Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us; and Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja al-Ghudani narrated to us; and Muhammad ibn Hisham ibn Abi al-Dumayk al-Mustamli narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aishah al-Taymi narrated to us, they said: Abdullah ibn Hassan al-Anbari Abu al-Junayd, brother of Banu Ka'b al-Anbari, narrated to us, my two grandmothers Safiyyah and Duhaybah, daughters of Ulaybah, who were the stepdaughters of Qaylah, narrated to me that Qaylah bint Makhramah narrated to them that she was under Habib ibn Azhar, brother of Banu Janab, and bore him daughters, then he died, and Athwab ibn Azhar their paternal uncle seized her daughters from her. So she went out seeking company to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the beginning of Islam. A little girl of them, Hudayba, wept; scabies had seized her, she being the youngest, wearing a woolen wrap of hers. So she pitied her and carried her along. While they were trotting the camel, the hare inflated, and the little Hudayba the child said: No, by Allah, your ankle shall never cease higher than Athwab's ankle in this story ever. Then when the fox turned aside, she named it a name other than fox, which Abdullah ibn Hassan forgot. Then she said concerning it what she said concerning the hare. While they were trotting, the camel knelt and was seized with trembling. So the little Hudayba the child said: By Allah, Athwab's seizure has overtaken you. So I said, compelled to her: Woe to you, what shall I do? She said: Turn your clothes inside out and roll your back to your belly, and turn your camel's saddle cloths. Then she took off her wrap, turned it, and rolled her back to her belly. When I did what she ordered me the camel shook, then stood, spread its legs and urinated. So the little Hudayba said: Put your gear back on. So I did what she ordered me and put them back. Then they went out trotting, and Athwab was on our trail with drawn sword. So we took refuge at a large tent, he circled it until the camel cast itself at the courtyard of the middle house; a docile camel, so I rushed inside it with the girl. He caught me with the sword, its edge struck part of the locks of my head, and said: Throw to me my brother's daughter, O Dafar. So I threw her to him, he placed her upon his shoulder and went with her. And I knew him better than the people of the house. I went to a sister of mine married among Banu Shayban, seeking company to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the beginning of Islam. While I was with her one night, my eye thinking it asleep, her husband came from the evening gathering and said: By your father, I have found a companion for Qaylah, a truthful companion. My sister said: Who is he? He said: Hurayth ibn Hassan al-Shaybani, returning as delegate of Bakr ibn Wail to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) this morning. My sister said: Woe to me, let not my sister hear of this, lest she go out with the brother of Bakr ibn Wail between the hearing of the earth and its sight with no man of her people with her. He said: Do not mention it to her, for I shall not mention it to her. So I heard what they said. In the morning I saddled my camel, found him not far, and asked him for company. He said: Yes, with honor, and his mounts were kneeling by me. So I went out with him, a truthful companion, until we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying the dawn prayer with the people, it having been called when dawn split, the stars interlaced in the sky, and men hardly recognized from the darkness of night. So I lined up with the men, a woman fresh from ignorance. The man next to me in the row said to me: Are you a woman or a man? I said: No, rather a woman. He said: You almost tempted me, so pray among the women. And there was a row of women that had formed by the chambers which I had not seen when I entered. So I was among them until, when the sun rose, I drew near, and whenever I saw a man with a cloak and comely appearance my sight aspired to him to see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) above the people, until a man came after the sun had risen and said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And upon you peace and Allah's mercy. And upon him were worn-out two wrappers dyed with saffron, threadbare, with a stripped trimmed palm stalk in his hand, bare except two leaflets at its top, squatting. When I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) humble in sitting I trembled with fear. His companion said to him: O Messenger of Allah, the poor woman trembled. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - and he did not look at me while I was behind his back: O poor woman, calmness be upon you. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said it, Allah removed what had entered my heart of dread. My companion, the first man Hurayth ibn Hassan, advanced and pledged allegiance to him upon Islam and upon his people. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, write between us and Banu Tamim by al-Dahna: none of them shall cross it to us except a traveler or passer-by. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Write by al-Dahna, O boy. When it was ordered for him, I was lifted by it, for it is my homeland and dwelling. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, he did not ask you for fairness in the matter when he asked you; this al-Dahna with you is the tying place of the camel and pasture of sheep, and the women of Banu Tamim and their children are beyond that. He said: Hold back, O boy. The poor woman spoke the truth. The Muslim is brother of the Muslim; water and trees suffice them both, and they help one another against raiders. When Hurayth saw that his writ was barred he struck one hand upon the other, then said: I and you are as one said: A ewe carries its death in its hooves. She said: By Allah, I know not whether you were a guide in darkness, generous to a man, chaste toward a female companion, until we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); but blame me not for asking my share when you asked your share. He said: And what is your share in al-Dahna, may you have no father? I said: The tying place of my camel, you ask it for your wife's camel. He said: No blame; I call the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to witness that I am your brother and companion as long as I live, since you praised me thus before him. So I said: Since I began it I shall not waste it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is the son of this woman blamed for settling the dispute and aiding one behind the chamber? Then I wept and said: By Allah, I bore him, O Messenger of Allah, unlawful, then he fought with you on the day of al-Rabadhah, then he went to bring me provisions from Khaybar, fever seized him and he died, leaving women upon me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in whose hand is my soul, had you not been a poor woman you would have been dragged upon your face - Abdullah ibn Hassan doubted which of the two wordings the two women narrated to him - can one of you not keep good company in the world, then when what is between him and who is worthier of him intervenes, he says: My Lord, give me steadfastness for what has passed, and help me upon what remains. By Him in whose hand is Muhammad's soul, one of you weeps, then seeks a companioness for her. O servants of Allah, do not torment your dead. Then he wrote for her on a red leather strip, for Qaylah and the women of Qaylah's daughters: their right shall not be wronged, nor shall they be compelled to marriage, and every believer and Muslim is their helper; do good and do not do evil. Muhammad ibn Hisham said: Ibn Aishah explained it to us, saying: al-Firsah is humpback; al-Firsah is a piece of musk; al-Firsah is opportunity; it is said: Seize your opportunity, meaning your turn. al-Sabij is a woolen wrap. al-Ratakan is a kind of pace. al-Intifaj is swift travel. Shannaha means he turned his right sides to you, some Arabs make it his left sides, and they take omens by one and good omens by the other. Tafajja: opened. Fa'walna: we took refuge at a tent. Dafar: O foul one, from that is the Arabs' saying about the world: Umm Dafr, for its foulness. Then she asked about him: inquired about him. al-Maqshuww: peeled. al-Fattan: devils, singular fatin. A ewe carries its death in its hooves: a proverb of the Arabs about a sheep that dug with its hooves in the earth and exposed a knife, so it was slaughtered with it, and it became a proverb. al-Qadiyyah: settlement of matters. Shakhasa: my sight rose. Kabiran: from the greatness of what I heard. Asini: make for me a comfort in what You give. Asfa': black."
"22764","2 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ali ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from a man of Banu al-Anbar, from Qaylah, she said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and prayed with him part of the prayer. When he finished the prayer I stood, and he looked at me, and she was a tall woman, and said: The son of this woman would indeed fight from behind the barrier. She said: By Allah, he was indeed so, O Messenger of Allah, but he died. She said: Write for me a writ. She said: And with me were three daughters. So he wrote: From Muhammad the Messenger of Allah to Qaylah and the three women: their right shall not be wronged, nor shall they be compelled to marriage, and every believer or Muslim is their guardian and helper; do good and they shall not do evil."
"22765","3 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Sawwar al-Anbari narrated to us; and Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Imran al-Isbahani narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Sawwar al-Anbari narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Hassan al-Anbari narrated to us that his two grandmothers Safiyyah and Duhaybah, daughters of Ulaybah, told him that Qaylah bint Makhramah, when she took her share of sleep after the night prayer, would say: In the name of Allah, and I rely upon Allah; I lay my side down for my Lord, and seek His forgiveness for my sin, repeating it several times, then say: I seek refuge in Allah and His perfect words which no righteous nor wicked transcends, from the evil of what descends from heaven and what ascends therein, the evil of what descends in the earth and the evil of what comes out of it, the evil of the trials of day and the evil of the visitants of night, except a visitant that knocks with good. I believed in Allah and held fast to Him. Praise be to Allah to whose power all things submit, praise be to Allah to whose might all things humble, praise be to Allah to whose greatness all things bow, praise be to Allah to whose dominion all things submit. O Allah, I ask You by the bonds of might of Your Throne, the utmost of mercy of Your Book, Your lofty grandeur, Your greatest name, and Your perfect words which no righteous nor wicked transcends, to look upon us with a merciful glance, leaving us no sin but You forgive it, no poverty but You mend it, no enemy but You destroy him, no naked but You clothe him, no debt but You settle it, and no affair of ours wherein is good in this world and the Hereafter but You grant it to us, O Most Merciful of the merciful. I believed in Allah and held fast to Him. Then she would say: Glory be to Allah thirty-three times, Allah is Greatest thirty-three times, and praise be to Allah thirty-four times. Then she would say: O my daughter, this is the seal's head: the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him seeking a servant, so he said: Shall I not point you to better than a servant? She said: Yes. So he ordered her with this hundred at bedtime after the night prayer."
"22766","Qaylah Umm Bani Anmar 4 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Khalaf narrated to us, Ya'la ibn Shabib narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn A'yan ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Qaylah Umm Bani Anmar who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Marwah while he was leaving ihram after an Umrah, so I sat with him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who buys and sells; when I want to sell goods I sometimes ask more than I intend to sell for, then I lower the price until I sell at what I intended, and when I want to buy goods I offer less than I intend to pay, then I raise until I take it at what I intended. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not do that, O Qaylah; when you want to sell goods, ask for what you intend to sell it for, whether you are given it or denied, and when you want to buy goods, offer what you intend to take it for, whether you are given it or denied."
"22767","Qutaylah bint Sayfi al-Juhaniyyah 5 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi and Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, both saying: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Ma'bad ibn Khalid, from Abd Allah ibn Yasar, from Qutaylah bint Sayfi who said: A Jewish scholar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, you are a fine people, were it not that you associate partners with Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And what is that? He said: When you swear, you say: By the Ka'bah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) waited a while, then said: Whoever swears, let him swear by the Lord of the Ka'bah. Then he said: O Muhammad, you are a fine people, were it not that you set up a rival to Allah. He said: Glory be to Allah, and what is that? He said: You say to a man: What Allah wills and you will. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) waited, then said: He has spoken; so whoever says: What Allah wills, let him put between them: then you will."
"22768","6 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Mas'udi, from Ma'bad ibn Khalid, from Abd Allah ibn Yasar, from Qutaylah bint Yasar, from Qutaylah bint Sayfi al-Juhaniyyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same as it."
"22769","7 - al-Miqdam ibn Dawud al-Misri narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Mis'ar ibn Kidam narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ja'far al-Qattat al-Kufi narrated to us, saying: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir informed us, from Mis'ar, from Ma'bad ibn Khalid, from Abd Allah ibn Yasar al-Juhani, from Qutaylah, a woman of them, who said: A Jew and a scholar came to the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: You associate partners with Allah and you set up rivals; you say: No, by the Ka'bah, and you say: What Allah wills and you will. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them to say: No, by the Lord of the Ka'bah, and to say: What Allah wills, then you will."
"22770","The chapter of Kaf: Kubayshah, also called Kabshah 8 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us. And Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, both saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah al-Ansari, from a grandmother of his called Kubayshah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me while a waterskin was hanging with me, and he drank from the mouth of the waterskin while standing, so I cut off the mouth of the waterskin seeking blessing by that."
"22771","Kabirah bint Sufyan 9 - Muhammad ibn al-Sari ibn Mihran al-Naqid al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Masmul al-Makki narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Waraqah ibn Sa'id: My mistress Kabirah bint Sufyan informed me - she had lived in the pre-Islamic era and was among those who gave allegiance - she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I buried alive four sons of mine in the pre-Islamic era? He said: Free four slaves. She said: So I freed your father Sa'id, and his two sons Maysarah and Jubayr, and the mother of Maysarah. She said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: The blood of Afra is purer before Allah than the blood of a black woman."
"22772","Karimah bint Kulthum al-Himyariyyah 10 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i the judge narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Makhul, from Ghusayf ibn al-Harith, from Atiyyah ibn Busr who said: Akkaf ibn Wada'ah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O Akkaf, do you have a wife? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I will not cease until you marry me to whomever you wish. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have married you, in the name of Allah and with blessing, to Karimah bint Kulthum al-Himyariyyah."
"22773","Kulaybah bint Burthun al-Anbariyyah 11 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Sa'd ibn Ammar ibn Shu'ayb ibn Abd Allah ibn Zaynab bint Tha'labah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, saying: I heard my grandmother Zaynab say: Kulaybah - or Kulthum - bint Burthun al-Anbariyyah called me and said: O my son, this man took my cloak which I used to wear, so I met the man and brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, this man took my mother's cloak? He said: Return to him his mother's cloak."
"22774","The chapter of Lam: Lubabah bint al-Harith, Umm al-Fadl, wife of al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib 12 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: Lubabah bint al-Harith ibn Hazn ibn Bujayr ibn Ribah ibn Abd Allah ibn Hilal ibn Amir ibn Sa'sa'ah ibn Mu'awiyah."
"22775","What Umm al-Fadl narrated: Abd Allah ibn Abbas from his mother Umm al-Fadl 13 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah: that Ibn Abbas, on the day of Arafah, was brought pomegranate and ate it, and Ibn Abbas said: Umm al-Fadl narrated to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke his fast at Arafah; she brought him milk and he drank."
"22776","14 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke his fast at Arafah, and Umm al-Fadl gave him milk as a gift and he drank at Arafah."
"22777","15 - al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Salih, the freedman of al-Taw'amah, from Ibn Abbas who said: Umm al-Fadl narrated to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought milk at Arafah and he drank while he was delivering the sermon."
"22778","16 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd Allah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from Umm al-Fadl who said: I brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Umm Habib bint al-Abbas while she was a little girl, and I placed her in the lap of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she urinated, so I struck her on her back, then I lifted her. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gently, then he called for a cup of water and poured it over the place of her urine, then said: Pour water over the place where urine is."
"22779","17 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, from his mother Umm al-Fadl who said: The last thing I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in Maghrib was Surah al-Mursalat."
"22780","18 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik. And Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Malik informed us. And Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Malik narrated to me. And Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us, Juwayriyah ibn Asma narrated to us, Malik narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas: that Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith heard him reciting: By those sent forth in succession, and she said: O my son, your recitation of this surah has reminded me that it is the last thing I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in Maghrib."
"22781","19 - al-Muttalib ibn Shu'ayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, from Umm al-Fadl who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray Maghrib and recite therein: By those sent forth in succession, and it was the last thing he prayed, then he did not pray after it."
"22782","20 - Ahmad ibn Rashdin al-Misri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, Rashdin ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Qurrah ibn Uqayl and Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas who said: Umm al-Fadl informed me, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in the Maghrib prayer: By those sent forth in succession."
"22783","21 - Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah informed me that Ibn Abbas said: Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith ibn Hazn narrated to me that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in Maghrib: By those sent forth in succession."
"22784","22 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us. And Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us. And Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, all saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, from Umm al-Fadl who said: The last thing I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in Maghrib was: By those sent forth."
"22785","23 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my uncle narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas: that his mother Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith informed him that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in Maghrib: By those sent forth in succession, then he did not pray again until Allah took his soul, mighty and majestic is He."
"22786","Tammam ibn al-Abbas from Umm al-Fadl 24 - Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us. And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Tammam ibn Abbas who said: Umm al-Fadl heard me reciting: By those sent forth in succession, and she said: O my son, this is the last surah I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in the Maghrib prayer."
"22787","What Anas ibn Malik narrated from Umm al-Fadl 25 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr and Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Dawud al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, from Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Maghrib in his house wrapped in a garment; he did not pray any prayer after it until he passed away, may Allah bless him and grant him peace."
"22788","What Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal narrated from Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith 26 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us. And Yusuf ibn Ya'qub the judge narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us. And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, all saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Umm al-Fadl: that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I had a wife, then I married another besides her, and the first claimed that she had suckled the later one. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One suckling and two sucklings do not make unlawful."
"22789","27 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Umm al-Fadl: that a woman divorced by her husband, then he married another woman, and his wife claimed that she had suckled her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One suckling and two sucklings do not make unlawful."
"22790","28 - Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us. And Khalifah narrated to us, Dawud ibn Shabib narrated to us, both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Umm al-Fadl: that a man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I married a woman while I have another wife, and she claimed that she suckled the later one. He said: One suckling and two sucklings do not make unlawful."
"22791","29 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Umm al-Fadl: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Does one suckling make unlawful? He said: No."
"22792","30 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Umm al-Fadl: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One suckling and two sucklings do not make unlawful, nor one nursing and two nursings."
"22793","31 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr and Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, both saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith: that Umm al-Fadl narrated to him that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One nursing and two nursings, or one suckling and two sucklings, do not make unlawful."
"22794","32 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abd Allah informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Umm al-Fadl who said: While I was sitting at the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was ill, I wept. He said: What makes you weep? I said: I fear for you, and we do not know what we will face from people after you. He said: You are the oppressed ones after me."
"22795","Kurayb, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Umm al-Fadl 33 - Ahmad ibn Zayd ibn Harun al-Qazzaz al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us. And Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, both saying: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Rashdin, from Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith: that whenever she heard someone recite: By those sent forth, she said: May Allah bless His Messenger; he recited in the Maghrib prayer: By those sent forth in succession; he did not pray Isha for us again until Allah took his soul, mighty and majestic is He."
"22796","Umayr, the freedman of Umm al-Fadl, from Umm al-Fadl 34 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik. And Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Abu al-Nadr, the freedman of Umar ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Ma'mar, from Umayr, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith: that people differed in her presence on the day of Arafah about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); some said: He is fasting, and some said: He is not fasting. So she sent him a cup of milk while he was standing on his camel, and he drank at Arafah."
"22797","35 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Abd Allah ibn Umar and al-Thawri, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Umayr, the freedman of Umm al-Fadl, who said: They doubted about the fasting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Arafah, so Umm al-Fadl said: I will find out for you. She sent him a cup of milk and he drank from it."
"22798","36 - al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me that Abu al-Nadr narrated to him that Umayr, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, narrated to him that he heard Umm al-Fadl say: People doubted about fasting on the day of Arafah, while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I sent him a cup of milk while he was at Arafah, and he drank it."
"22799","37 - Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abu al-Nadr, the freedman of Umar ibn Ubayd Allah, from Umayr, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Umm al-Fadl who said: People doubted about the fast of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Arafah, so I said: I will find out for you. I sent him a vessel with milk in it and he drank."
"22800","Qabus ibn al-Mukhariq from Umm al-Fadl 38 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Mizzi narrated to us, Ali ibn Salih narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Qabus al-Shaybani, from his father who said: Umm al-Fadl came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I saw part of your body in my house. He said: What you saw is good; Fatimah will give birth to a boy and you will nurse him with the milk of Qutham. She said: She brought him carrying him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she took him and placed him in his lap, and he urinated, so she struck him with her hand. He said: You have hurt my son, may Allah have mercy on you. She said: Give me your garment so we may wash it. He said: The urine of a girl is washed, and the urine of a boy is sprinkled over."
